hadiths[1159]{hadithnumber,text}:
"650","Hameed said: I asked Umar bin Abdul Aziz, may God bless him and grant him peace: I wish you would have gathered all the people on one thing. He replied: If they had not disagreed, I would not have been happy."
"651","Aun bin Abdullah said: I do not like that the Companions of the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, do not disagree, because if they agree on something and a man abandons that thing, it is as if he abandoned the Sunnah, and if they disagree and a man follows the saying of any of these Companions, then (as if) he followed the Sunnah."
"652","On the authority of Layth (Ibn Abi Salim) Imam Taaws (may Allah have mercy on him) said: Sometimes Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) formed an opinion and then abandoned it."
"653","Marwan bin Huqam said: Sayyidna Uthman bin Affan (RA) said to me: Sayyidna Umar bin Al-Khattab (RA) said to me: I have an opinion about grandfather’s legacy. were"
"654","Asim al-Ahwal narrated that I presented the hadith rulings to Imam Shaabi, may God have mercy on him, and he allowed me to narrate them."
"655","Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated that I asked Amr bin Dinar: Have you heard this hadith from Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a man who was passing by the mosque with an arrow: \Take hold of its tip (by its side).\"" Amr bin Dinar said: Yes"
"656","Narrated Sufyan bin Uyaina, I said to Abd al-Rahman bin Al-Qasim: Did you hear your father narrating on the authority of Sayyida Aisha, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to kiss him while he was fasting? He said: Yes, I heard them say that."
"657","Shuba narrated that Mansoor wrote a hadith and sent it to me. When I met him, I said: Can I narrate this hadith on your behalf? He said: When I write something to you, it is synonymous with narration and narration. (That is, as if I told you two Badoos)."
"658","Shu'ba (bin al-Hajjaj) said: I asked Ayyub al-Sakhtiani, and he gave the same answer."
"659","It is narrated on the authority of Mu'mar that he (Imam) presented the book to Zahri (may Allah have mercy on him) and said: May I narrate it to you? He said: Did someone other than me narrate it for you?"
"660","It is narrated from Hisham bin Urwa that his father (Urwa) said: Presenting the Book and Hadith to the teacher is the same."
"661","On the authority of Ja'far bin Muhammad, his father said: Reciting the Book or the Hadith is the same thing."
"662","Dawud bin Atta (Mulay al-Muznayin) said: Zayd bin Aslam considered it equal to presenting a book or a hadith, and Ibn Abi Zayb also held the same view."
"663","Mutarf (bin Abdullah bin Mutarf) said: Imam Malik, may God have mercy on him, considered presenting the book or reciting the hadith as equal."
"664","On the authority of Amish, Ibrahim said: (The second person) will stand on the left of the Imam."
"665","Aqar bin Mughira bin Shuba narrated from his father, Sayyidna Mughira bin Shuba, may Allah be pleased with him, that Sayyidna Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, asked the people: Did any of you hear from the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, about the fetus? So Sayyidna Mughira bin Shuba (RA) stood up and said: He (PBUH) decided to give a slave or a slave (in marriage) regarding this matter. Sayyiduna Umar (RA) then asked the people, then the one for whom this decision was made stood up and said: The Prophet (PBUH) had decided for me a slave or a slave girl in exchange for the fetus. The day of the fetus is judged by the one who neither ate, nor drank, nor cried, nor cried, that is, did not utter a sound or speak at the time of birth. Hearing this, Sayyiduna Umar said: If I had not known the decision of the Prophet, I would have declared the two deities to be one."
"666","Ayyub said: If you want to know the mistake of your teacher, consult someone other than him."
"667","Ayyub narrated that we mentioned (the Iddah) that a man dies in Makkah, I said: The Iddah will be counted from the day on which news of this is received, as is the opinion of Hasan Qatadah and our other Companions. Ayyub said: I was met by Talaq bin Habib and said: You are very honorable to me, and you are in a city where the sight is high, and I do not consider you safe, and Talaq said: You have issued a fatwa against the inhabitants of this city. Therefore, I do not consider you safe, I said: Is there a difference in this issue? Talaq said: Yes, the Idda of this woman will be counted from the day her husband died. Ayub said: I met Saeed bin Jubeer and asked him about this issue, and he also said: The Idda will be counted from the day she died. Then I asked Mujahid, and he also said: \Idtah\"" on the day he died. Then I asked Ata bin Abi Rabah"
"668","It was narrated on the authority of Hakam bin Masoud that we asked Sayyiduna Umar (may God be pleased with him) about the brothers who share in the brotherhood (i.e. real, real, and Akhiyafi brothers) and he did not include them as partners. The next year we went to him again and said: All share (in the inheritance). We said: Last year you said the opposite."
"669","On the authority of Hajjaj al-Aswad, Wahib bin Munba said: In the past, the scholars used to protect their knowledge from the worldly, so the worldly were interested in their knowledge, and they would throw their world on them, but today's scholars have cast their knowledge on the worldly, so the worldly have surrendered their knowledge, and have saved their world from them."
"670","(Maqtu' Hadith) Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim informed us, Muhammad ibn 'Umar ibn al-Kumayt narrated to us, 'Ali ibn Wahb al-Hamdani narrated to us, al-Dahhak ibn Musa narrated to us, who said: Sulayman ibn 'Abd al-Malik passed by Medina intending Makkah, so he stayed there for some days. He said: ""Is there anyone in Medina who met anyone from the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ)?"" They said to him: ""Abu Hazim, O Commander of the Faithful."" So he sent for him."
"671","Zaid Al-Umi informed some jurists that they said: O scholar! Act according to your knowledge, and donate your excess wealth, and refrain from excessive talk except that which will benefit you in the sight of Allah. O master of knowledge! If you did not act on the knowledge you acquired, then when you meet your Lord, this (non-action) will be an end to your excuse and excuse. O master of knowledge! What you have been commanded to obey Allah is so that you stay away from what you have been prevented from disobeying Allah. O scholar! Not to be strong in other work and weak in your work. O master of knowledge! What is for someone other than you, should not distract you from what is for you. O master of knowledge! Respect the scholars, flock to them and listen to them, and do not fight with them. O master of knowledge! Honor the scholars because of their knowledge and look down on the ignorant because of their ignorance, but do not drive them away, but bring them closer and teach them knowledge. O knowledge giver! Do not narrate a hadith in an assembly that you do not understand, and do not answer a man until you understand what he has asked you. \n O knowledge! Do not deceive Allah, and do not deceive people, to deceive Allah is to turn away from His command, and to deceive people is to follow their desires, and fear Allah, in that Allah has commanded to fear Him, and fear people so as not to lead them into temptation. \n O knowledge! Indeed, just as daylight is perfected only by the sun, so wisdom is perfected by obedience to Allah. \n O master of knowledge! Just as cultivation is maintained by water and soil, faith is maintained by knowledge and action. \n O master of knowledge! Just as every traveler collects the zaad of the road and gets the zaad of the road when needed. In the same way, every doer in the hereafter will be in need of his actions that he did in this world. \n O master of knowledge! When Allah Ta'ala inspires you to worship Him, know that Allah Ta'ala intends to explain your value and status to Him, so do not turn to anyone else except Him, that you turn away from His value and status to humiliation and humiliation. \n O master of knowledge! If you move stones and iron, it is easier than if you narrate a hadith to a person who does not understand what you are saying, and the example of a person who narrates his hadith without understanding is like someone who calls for the dead and sets a table for the dead."
"672","(Maqtu' Hadith) 'Abd al-Malik ibn Sulayman Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Antaki informed us, from 'Abbad ibn 'Abbad al-Khawwas al-Shami Abu 'Utbah, who said: ""As for what follows: Understand, and intellect is a blessing. How many a person of intellect has had his heart occupied by excessive profundity in what harms him, away from benefiting from what he needs, until he became heedless of that? And from the excellence of a person's intellect is leaving the investigation of that in which there is no investigation, lest the excellence of his intellect become a burden upon him in abandoning competition with one who is beneath him in righteous deeds. Or a man whose heart is occupied by an innovation in which he has adopted his religion from men other than the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), or he suffices with his own opinion in that in which he sees no guidance except in it, and no misguidance except in abandoning it. He claims he took it from the Qur'an, yet he calls to separation from the Qur'an. Were there not carriers of the Qur'an before him and before his companions who acted upon its clear verses and believed in its ambiguous ones? And they were therefrom upon a beacon for the clear path. And the Qur'an was the Imam of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was the Imam of his Companions, and his Companions were Imams for those after them—known men, attributed in the lands, agreed upon in refuting the people of desires, despite the differences among them. And the people of desires scattered with their opinions into divergent, deviant paths, straying from the Straight Path. Their guides led them astray in misleading deserts, so they plunged deeper into them, wandering obstinately in their confusion. Whenever Satan invented for them an innovation in their misguidance, they moved from it to another, because they did not seek the trace of the predecessors, nor did they follow the Emigrants. It is mentioned from 'Umar that he said to Ziyad: 'Do you know what destroys Islam? The slip of a scholar, the disputation of a hypocrite with the Qur'an, and misguiding leaders. Fear Allah regarding what has occurred among your reciters and people of your mosques of backbiting, tale-bearing, and walking among people with two faces and two tongues. It is mentioned that whoever has two faces in the world will have two faces in the Fire. The backbiter meets you and backbites to you one whom he sees you love to hear backbitten, then he goes to your companion and brings him the like of it from you. Thus he achieves his need with each of you, while it remains hidden from each of you what he brought to his companion. His presence with those present is the presence of brothers, and his absence from those absent is the absence of enemies. Whoever is present from them gets preference, and whoever is absent has no sanctity. He tempts those present with praise, and backbites those absent with slander. So, O servants of Allah, is there not among the people a righteous one or a reformer who would restrain him from his scheming and turn him away from the honor of his Muslim brother? Rather, he knew their desire in what he walked to them with, so he gained power over them and they enabled him of his need, so he ate with his religion along with their religions. Allah, Allah! Protect the sanctities of your absent ones, and restrain your tongues from them except with good. Be sincere to Allah regarding your Ummah, since you are the carriers of the Book and the Sunnah. For the Book does not speak until it is spoken by, and the Sunnah does not act until it is acted upon. So when will the ignorant learn if the scholar is silent, not denouncing what has appeared, and not commanding what has been abandoned? And Allah took the covenant of those given the Book: 'You shall make it clear to the people and not conceal it.' Fear Allah, for you are in a time in which piety has become thin, humility has become little, and the corrupters carry knowledge, loving to be known for carrying it, and hating to be known for wasting it. So they spoke in it with desire when they introduced error into it, and they distorted words from the truth they left to the falsehood they worked. Their sins are sins that are not forgiven, and their shortcomings are shortcomings that are not acknowledged. How can the seeker of guidance be guided if the guide is perplexed? They loved the world..."""
"673","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) said: When we were forbidden to take the initiative in speaking to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), we used to prefer that a wise and sensible Bedouin villager come and question the Prophet (peace be upon him) and we sit beside him. By chance, once we were sitting when a villager came and knelt down in front of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Muhammad! Your messenger came to us and said to us, \You say that Allah has sent you as a Messenger?\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""He spoke the absolute truth.\"" He said: By the One who raised the heavens"
"674","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) that a villager came to the Holy Prophet (PBUH) and said: O son of Bani Abd al-Muttalib! \Peace be upon you\"""
"675","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) said: Banu Sa’d bin Bakr sent Sayyidna Zammam bin Tha’albah (RA) to the Messenger of Allah (SAW), so he came and sat his camel at the door of the mosque, then tied it and then entered the mosque. He stood near the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Which of you is the son of Abdul Muttalib? The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I am the son of Abdul Muttalib.” He said: Muhammad? He said: \Yes\"""
"676","On the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Malik Ash'ari, may God bless him and grant him peace, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Purity is half of faith"
"677","A man from Banusalim said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited these glorifications on my hand. \Glory be to Allah\"" fills half the scale and \""Alhamdulillah\"" fills the whole scale and \""Allah Akbar\"" fills the space between heaven and earth"
"678","The freed slave of the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, Sayyidna Thawban, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said: \Stay upright and strong"
"679","Abu Kash al-Sali narrated that he heard a freed slave of the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, say that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Adopt a moderate way and keep nearer to what is right. And the best of your actions is prayer"
"680","It is narrated from Ikrimah that Sayyiduna Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas (RA) used to pray all five prayers in one ablution, but Sayyidna Ali (RA) used to perform ablution for each prayer, and he recited this verse:"
"681","Ubaidullah, the son of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) said: I thought what was the opinion of Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (RA) about performing ablution for every prayer whether he was pure or not, why did he do that? He said: Asma bint Zayd bin Al-Khattab narrated to him that Abdullah bin Hanzalah bin Abi Amir narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered him to perform ablution for every prayer, whether the ablution was pure or impure, then when it became difficult for him to do so, he ordered a miswak for every prayer, and Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with him, believed that he had the power of ablution for every prayer, so he They did not abandon ablution for any prayer."
"682","Ibn Buraidah narrated from his father Sayyiduna Buraidah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to perform ablution for every prayer, even when Makkah was conquered, he, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed all the prayers with one ablution, and wiped his khafeen. He said: I have done this on purpose. \n Abu Muhammad Imam Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: So the action of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, is indicative of the fact that this verse \When you come to prayer\"" [Maidah: 6/5] means that every person who has a hadith has ablution for every prayer"
"683","Sayyiduna Mughira bin Shuba (RA) said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) on some journeys, and when the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) used to go out for ablution, he used to go far away."
"684","Sayyidna Mughira bin Shuba (RA) said that when the Prophet (PBUH) used to go to defecate, he would go far away. \n Imam Abu Muhammad al-Darmi said: This is one of the manners of having a need. That is, if a person goes into the forest, he should be hidden from the eyes, then he should relieve himself so that no one can see him."
"685","On the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Huraira, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever wears a headscarf should wear it oddly, and if he does it, it is better not to wear it, then there is no harm in it, and whoever does it loosely, then he should wear it oddly, and if he does it, then it is better not to do it, then there is no problem. No, and the person who goes to the toilet should be under cover, if there is nothing to cover except a pile of sand, then he should sit under its cover, because the devils play with the private part of a person."
"686","On the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Ja'far, may Allah be pleased with him: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, liked the shelter of mounds or palm trees when he defecated."
"687","On the authority of Sayyiduna Sahl bin Hanif, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: \You are my messenger and preacher to the people of Makkah"
"688","On the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When you go to the bathroom"
"689","It was narrated from Anas (RA) that when the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) intended to defecate, he would not lift his cloth until he was close to the ground. Imam al-Darmi Abu Muhammad (may God have mercy on him) said: This is also one of the manners of the empty space and it is similar to the hadith of Mugheera."
"690","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) said: \I went up to the roof of my house and saw the Prophet (PBUH) sitting on two bricks facing the Holy City.\"""""
"691","Sayyiduna Hudhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him) said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to a nation's garbage (dirt heap) and urinated standing up. Imam al-Darmi Abu Muhammad (may God have mercy on him) said: I do not know of any aversion to urinating while standing."
"692","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the bathroom (to relieve himself), he would recite this supplication: \O Allah"
"693","On the authority of Umm al-Mu'minin Sayyidah Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said: \Whenever one of you goes to the abode"
"694","Amara bin Khuzimah bin Thabit al-Ansari narrated from his father Sayyiduna Khuzimah (may God be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \It should be done with three stones that do not contain dung.\"""""
"695","On the authority of Sayyidna Sahl bin Hanif, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: \You are my messenger and preacher to the people of Makkah"
"696","Abdullah bin Abi Qatadah narrated from his father Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \None of you should touch his private parts with his right hand"
"697","On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I am for you as a father is for his children, I teach you, so do not turn your face or back towards the Qiblah when you defecate, and when you defecate, do not defecate with your right hand.” Zakariya said: \Al-Rama\"" means old bones."""
"698","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to defecate, I and a boy would bring a spear and a pot of water with which he would perform ablution."
"699","It was narrated from Anas (RA) that when the Prophet (PBUH) would come out of the toilet, a boy would bring a bucket of water from which he (PBUH) would relieve himself. Imam al-Darmi Abu Muhammad, may God have mercy on him, said: The name of Abu Muadh is Ata bin Muni Abi Maimunah."
"700","Musayyib bin Najaba said that my maternal grandmother who was married to Sayyidna Huzaifa (RA) narrated that Sayyidna Huzaifa (RA) used to drink water."
"701","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \Bring water for ablution.\"" Then he (PBUH) went to a grove of trees."""
"702","Ibrahim bin Jarir bin Abdullah narrated from his father the same from the Prophet."
"703","Yusuf bin Abi Burda narrated from his father, on the authority of Sayyida Aisha, that when the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, would come out of the toilet, he would say: \Ghufranak\"" meaning \""O Allah"
"704","On the authority of Sayyiduna Anas, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Indeed"
"705","On the authority of Sayyiduna Anas, the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said: \I have told you a lot about Miswak.\"" (That is"
"706","On the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \If there was no difficulty for my ummah"
"707","On the authority of Sayyida Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \The toothpick purifies (cleanses) the mouth and pleases the Lord.\"""""
"708","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Hudhayfah that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to clean his mouth with a toothpick when he got up for Tahajjud."
"709","Abul Malih narrated on the authority of his father Usama bin Umayr (RA): The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Allah does not accept any prayer without ablution"
"710","On the authority of Sayyiduna Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \The key to prayer is purity"
"711","Sayyiduna Safina (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform ablution with one mud and perform ghusl with one saa."
"712","Abdullah bin Abdullah said: I heard Sayyiduna Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he used to say: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to perform ablution with one mukuk and perform ghusl with five mukuk."
"713","Sayyidah Rabi bint Mu'awz (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) used to visit our house, so I used to take a bowl of water from my house, which was one mudd and one-third mudd or one-quarter mudd of water and put water in it."
"714","On the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \He who does not say Bismillah does not have ablution.\"""""
"715","On the authority of Sayyiduna Aws bin Abi Aws, may Allah be pleased with him, that he saw the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, performing ablution, and he poured water three times on both his arms. I asked: What is meant by \Astuqaf 3sa\""? So he said: Washed his hands three times."""
"716","On the authority of Hamran Mulli Uthman bin Affan, Sayyiduna Uthman bin Affan performed ablution, then he rinsed, wiped his nose, and washed his face three times, and both hands (up to the elbows) three times, then he wiped his head and washed his feet (up to the ankles) three times, then he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, perform ablution exactly as I performed ablution. He said: \Whoever performs ablution like my ablution"
"717","Amr bin Yahya Mazni narrates from his father that Sayyidna Abdullah bin Zayd Radiyallahu Anhu (who is the grandfather of Amr) called for water, first he poured water on his hands and washed his hands three times (twice in Bukhari), then he washed his face three times, then he washed his hands up to the elbows twice, then he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, perform ablution like this."
"718","The above state of ablution has been narrated by Sayyidna Abdullah Bin Zayd RA from the Prophet SAW."
"719","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) said: Shall I not tell you the method of ablution of the Messenger of Allah (PBUH)? After that he washed the organs of ablution one by one. The narrator said or said: That ablution is one time."
"720","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, washed the organs of ablution one at a time, and rinsed and inhaled with one straw."
"721","On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Saeed al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say: \Should I not tell you something by which Allah"
"722","The above-mentioned hadith was narrated from Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, in another way."
"723","On the authority of Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \We have been ordered to perform ablution well.\"" It is in the tradition of Ibn Majah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered us to perform ablution."""
"724","Abd Khair narrated that Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) after offering Fajr prayer came to Rahbah (which is a place in Kufa) and sat down, then he said to his slave: Bring water for ablution. The narrator said: The slave brought a pot of water and a saucer. Abd Khair said: We were sitting and looking at him, he put his right hand (in water) and filled his mouth with water, rinsed it, and put water in his nose and wiped it with his left hand. (i.e. rinsing, inhalation and exhalation)."
"725","The above-mentioned hadith is also narrated from this chain of transmission."
"726","It was narrated from Aa'iz bin Abdullah that I heard Sayyiduna Abu Huraira, may God be pleased with him, say: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: \He who pours water into his nose should clean it"
"727","Shaqiq bin Salama said: I saw Sayyiduna Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, performing ablution, so he stroked his beard and said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, perform ablution in the same way."
"728","Asim bin Laqit bin Sabra narrated from his father, Sayyiduna Laqit bin Sabra, who was in the delegation of Bani Muntafaq, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When you perform ablution"
"729","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \(Dry) heels are the punishment of fire"
"730","Muhammad bin Ziyad said: I heard Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) who was passing by us and people were performing ablution with their loot, he was saying: Perform ablution well. Abul Qasim (peace be upon him) said: \The punishment of fire is for dry heels.\"" Abu Muhammad said: This hadith is more beloved to me than the hadith of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him)."""
"731","Shaqiq bin Salamah said: I saw Sayyiduna Uthman performing ablution, he wiped his head and the inside and outside of both ears, then he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"732","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Zayd bin Asim Mazni (RA) said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) performing ablution, so he rinsed, put water in his nose, then washed his face three times, then washed both hands (up to the elbows) three times, then wiped his head, and washed his two feet until they were clean, and wiped his head with new water instead of the water left in his hand. Abu Muhammad said: From the last sentence, the interpretation of the first wipe is intended."
"733","On the authority of Sayyidna Amr bin Umayyah Zamri, may Allah be pleased with him, he saw the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, wipe his socks and turban. Abu Muhammad (Darmi) was asked: Do you accept this as a proof? He said: Yes, by Allah."
"734","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) performed ablution once and sprinkled water on his private parts."
"735","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) said: I asked my aunt Sayyida Maimunah (RA) about the Ghusl Janabat of the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) and she said: A vessel of water would be brought, he (PBUH) would pour water from his right hand to his left hand, then he would wash his private parts and where the dirt was, then he would perform ablution in the same way as he performs ablution for prayer, then he would wash his head and the rest of his body, then leave that place. He would wash both his feet, then if a towel was brought, he would place it in front of him, and wipe off the water with his fingers and would not touch it (towel)."
"736","It was narrated from Sayyidna Mughira bin Shuba, may Allah be pleased with him, that I was traveling one night with the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, when he said: \Do you have any water?\"" I said: Yes"
"737","Sayyiduna Ali bin Abi Talib (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) prescribed three days and three nights for the traveler, and one day and one night for the resident, i.e. for wiping over the socks."
"738","Abd Khair said: I saw Sayyiduna Ali performing ablution and wiping both shoes, then he said: If I had not seen the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, do the same as you saw me (wiping), I think that wiping the soles would have preceded the upper step. Imam al-Darmi Abu Muhammad, may God have mercy on him, said: This hadeeth \And wipe your heads and your feet to the Ka'ba\"" [Al-Ma'idah: 6/5] is abrogated"
"739","Sayyiduna Uqba bin Aamir (RA) narrated that he went out with the Prophet (PBUH) in the Battle of Tabuk, and one day the Prophet (PBUH) was sitting with his Companions narrating a Hadith. Sayyiduna Uqbah (RA) said: I thank Allah who gave me the opportunity to hear this hadith from the Messenger of Allah (PBUH). Sayyidna Umar bin Al-Khattab (RA) who was sitting in front of me said: Are you surprised at this hadith? The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said something even better than this before you came. I said: My parents are sacrificed to you, what is that? So Sayyiduna Umar, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Whoever performs ablution well"
"740","It was narrated from Asim bin Sufyan that those people returned to Sayyiduna Mu'awiya (may Allah be pleased with them) after the raids, and Sayyidna Abu Ayyub and Sayyidna Uqbah bin Aamir (may Allah be pleased with them) were present with them. Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub (RA) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) say: \Whoever performs ablution as ordered"
"741","On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Huraira, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When a Muslim or a believer performs ablution and washes his face"
"742","It was narrated from Abu Uthman that I was under a tree with Sayyiduna Salman Farsi, may Allah be pleased with him, when he broke a dry branch and shook it, and all its leaves fell off. He said: Will you not ask me why I did this? Asked: Why did you do that? He said: This is what the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, did when I was with him. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \When a Muslim performs ablution well and performs all the five prayers"
"743","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to perform ablution for every prayer, and ablution was sufficient for each of us until something came up that broke the ablution. (i.e. urine, stool, sleep, etc.)."
"744","On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When one of you feels a movement in his bowels during prayer"
"745","On the authority of Sayyiduna Mu'awiya bin Abi Sufyan, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Indeed"
"746","Sayyiduna Sahl bin Haneef (RA) said: I had a severe complaint of the disease, due to which I used to take ghusl often, so I mentioned it to the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) and asked him about it. Sayyiduna Sahl (RA) said: I asked: And what should I do with what is on my clothes? He said: \Fill a bucket of water and sprinkle it on the affected area.\"""""
"747","On the authority of Sayyidah Basra bint Safwan, may Allah be pleased with her, she heard the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: \If a person touches a private part"
"748","On the authority of Sayyidah Basrah bint Safwan, may Allah be pleased with her, she heard the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: \Whoever touches his private parts should perform ablution.\"" Imam al-Darmi (may Allah have mercy on him) said: This is the most reliable hadith regarding the Sharm Gah."""
"749","Al-Khahir bin Zayd Ansari reported that his father Sayyidna Zayd bin Thabit (RA) heard the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) say: \Whatever is cooked on fire is ablution.\"" Imam Darmi (may Allah have mercy on him) was asked: What is your action on this? He said: No."""
"750","On the authority of Jafar bin Amr bin Umayyah that his father Sayyiduna Amr bin Umayyah (RA) informed him that he saw the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) cutting off a goat's glove and eating it with a knife."
"751","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira Radiyallahu Anhu said: Some people of Banumdilj came to the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of Allah! We live in the sea, we sit on the boards and hunt, then we remain absent for two nights, three nights, four or four nights. We carry sweet water with us for our lips, so if we perform ablution with it, then our lives will be in danger, and if we prioritize our own self and perform ablution with the water of the sea, then our hearts are troubled that this water is not impure? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Do ablution with the water of the sea"
"752","On the authority of Mughira bin Abi Burda that he heard Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah Radiyallahu Anhu saying: A man from Banu Abd al-Dar asked the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, that we ride in the sea, and we have a little sweet water with us. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Its water is pure and its dead is lawful.\"""""
"753","On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Hurairah, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \None of you should urinate in stagnant water"
"754","On the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, I heard that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about the water of the forest, from which cattle and beasts drink (it can be used)."
"755","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about the water from which beasts and fools drink. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \When the amount of water is equal to two large matkas"
"756","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) came to visit me because I was ill and fainted."
"757","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that one of the wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up and performed ablution from a tub of water. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up to perform ghusl with the remaining water. He said, \I have bathed in this tub before you.\"""""
"758","It is narrated in the same manner from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) in another chain of transmission."
"759","It was narrated from Kabsha bint Ka'b bin Malik, who was the daughter-in-law of Sayyiduna Abu Qutada, that when Sayyiduna Abu Qatada came to her, she (his son's wife) brought him water for ablution. At that time, a cat came and began to drink water, so Sayyiduna Abu Qutada tilted the pot so that it (the cat was satisfied) could drink the water easily. Kabsha said: Sayyidna Abu Qutada Radiyallahu Anhu found me looking like this and said: O niece! So wondering? I said: Yes, so he said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \This (cat) is not impure"
"760","On the authority of Sayyidina Abdullah bin Mughfil (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) said: \When a dog puts its mouth in a pot"
"761","On the authority of Umm al-Mu'minin, Sayyidah Maimunah (may Allah be pleased with her) that a mouse fell into the ghee and died, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Throw out the mouse and the ghee around it and eat (the remaining ghee).\"""""
"762","On the authority of Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, passed by two graves and said: \Both of them are being punished in their graves"
"763","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Anas that a villager came to the Holy Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam) and when he stood up, he began to urinate in a corner of the mosque."
"764","It was narrated from Sayyidah Umm Qays bint Muhsan (RA) that she brought her son to the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) who had not yet learned to eat (i.e. he was an infant)."
"765","On the authority of Umm Wold Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, she came to Umm al-Mominin, Sayyida Umm Salama, may Allah be pleased with her, and said, “I keep my skirt long, and it passes through dirty ground (i.e., the skirt becomes impure). Sayyida Umm Salama, may Allah be pleased with her, said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The land that comes after this impure land purifies it.” The narrator said: I asked Imam Darmi: Is this your fatwa? He said: I do not know."
"766","Sayyidna Imran bin Hussain (RA) said: We were on a journey with the Messenger of Allah (PBUH). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) camped, asked for water for ablution and performed ablution, then the call to prayer was given and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led the prayer, and after turning to greet him, he saw a man standing alone, he had not even prayed. The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: \Why did you not pray with the congregation?\"" He said: O Messenger of Allah! I have become Janabat and there is no water. The Messenger of Allah"
"767","On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Saeed al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, two persons were on a journey, the time for prayer had come, and they had no water with them, so they both performed tayammum with pure clay and prayed, then they got water and there was still time for prayer, one person performed ablution and repeated the prayer, the other did not repeat it. Repeated: \You followed the Sunnah and your prayer was completed.\"" (It was enough)"
"768","It was narrated from Sayyidna Ammar bin Yasir (RA) that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) used to say about Tayammum, \It is sufficient for the face and hands to strike the ground once.\"" Imam al-Darmi (may God have mercy on him) said: Its chain of transmission is valid. That is"
"769","It is narrated from Umm al-Mu'minin Sayyida Aisha (RA) that she asked Sayyida Asmaa (RA) for a necklace and it was lost, so the Messenger of Allah (SAW) sent some of his companions to look for it. When the time for prayer came and there was no water, they prayed without ablution. Sayyidna Asayd bin Hudair (RA) said: May Allah reward you well, by Allah, whenever a calamity befell you, Allah averted it, and made it a blessing for the Muslims."
"770","Umm al-Mu'minin Sayyidah Maimunah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: I kept water for the Prophet (peace be upon him) and he poured it on his hands, then he washed his private parts, then he rubbed his hand on the ground or on the wall (this is Sulaiman's doubt), then he rinsed his nose, washed his face and hands up to the elbows, and poured water over his head and body. I offered you a sheet but you refused and started drinking water with your hand. It is narrated from Sulaiman that Salim said: This was your Ghusl Janabat."
"771","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said that when the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to wash his hands, he would first wash his hands, then he would perform ablution in the same way as he would perform ablution for prayer, then he would take water in his hand and run it through the roots of his hair, and when he was satisfied that the water had reached the roots, he would pour water on his head three times, and then he would perform ghusl. Imam al-Darmi Abu Muhammad, may God have mercy on him, said: This method is more beloved to me than the tradition of Salim bin Abi al-Jaad."
"772","Umm al-Mu'minin, Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said, \I and the Messenger of Allah"
"773","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: I and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to bathe with the same vessel, which was different."
"774","It was narrated from Ameerul Momineen Sayyiduna Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Whoever leaves a place in the Ghusl of Janabat"
"775","Ata bin Abi Rabah said that he heard Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may God bless him and grant him peace, that a man was injured during the time of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and then he contracted a fever, and he was ordered to take a bath, and he died. Ata bin Abi Rabah said: It has reached me that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked after that, and he, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \He (the wounded man) should have washed his body and left his head where it was wounded.\"""""
"776","It was narrated from Anas (RA) that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) visited all his wives in one day."
"777","It is narrated from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) visited all his wives in one night."
"778","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Ja'far (RA) said, \One day the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) made me ride behind him and whispered something that I would never tell anyone"
"779","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) said: Sayyidna Umar (RA) asked the Messenger of Allah (SAW) that I have janabat at night? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Wash that organ"
"780","On the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Aswad, his father asked Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) what did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do when he wanted to sleep in the state of janabat. He said: He used to perform ablution after praying and then went to sleep."
"781","On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Ayyub Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said: \Water is from water.\"""""
"782","Sayyidna Sahl bin Sa'd Sa'idi (RA) who saw and heard the Prophet (PBUH), and at the time of his death, Sahl was 15 years old, narrated that Sayyidna Abi Bin Ka'b (RA) narrated to me that people used to give the fatwa that water is water, so this was the ease that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) had given in the beginning of Islam, but later he (PBUH) ordered to take bath. Imam al-Darmi (may Allah have mercy on him) said: The second narrator said: Imam Zuhri (may Allah have mercy on him) said: The one whom I like, narrated this hadith to me from Sayyiduna Sahl bin Saad (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"783","On the authority of Sayyiduna Sahl bin Saad, may Allah be pleased with him, that Sayyidna Abi bin Ka'b, may God be pleased with him, narrated to me that the fatwa that people give about \al-ma'am min al-ma'a\"" was a leave that the Messenger of Allah"
"784","On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Hurairah, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When a man sits between the four branches of a woman"
"785","Saeed bin Al-Musayyib said, \My aunt (Khulah bint Hakim al-Salmiyyah) asked the Messenger of Allah"
"786","On the authority of Urwa bin Zubayr, Sayyida Aisha, the wife of the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, told him: Sayyida Umm Salim, may Allah be pleased with her, the mother of Banu Abu Talha, entered the presence of the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of Allah! Allah Ta'ala is not ashamed of speaking the truth. If a woman sees her while sleeping like a man, will she bathe? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Yes"
"787","Sayyiduna Anas (RA) said that Umm al-Mominin (RA) was sitting near the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) when Sayda (RA) Umm Salim (RA) entered and asked: What should a woman do if she sees a man in a dream? Sayyida Umm Salama (may Allah be pleased with her) said: Your hands are dirty, you have disgraced the women, but the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, supported Sayyida Umm Salim (may Allah be pleased with him) and said: \Rather (O wife)"
"788","It was narrated from Sayyida Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said about a person who, upon waking up, sees a dream, but does not remember the dream, he said: \He should perform ghusl"
"789","On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When one of you wakes up from sleep"
"790","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) said: We were with the Holy Prophet (PBUH), he entered the bath, and when he came out after ablution, food was served, and it was said: \Will you not perform ablution?\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""Should I pray when I perform ablution?\"""""
"791","It was narrated from Urwa bin Zubair and Umrah bint Abdur Rahman that Sayyida Aisha, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said that Sayyida Umm Habiba bint Jahsh, may God bless him and grant him peace, who was married to Sayyidna Abd al-Rahman bin Awf, may God be pleased with him, was suffering from istihaza for seven years. It is the blood of a vein, so when you menstruate, leave the prayer, and when the period of menstruation ends, take a bath and pray.\ Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: So she used to bathe and pray for every prayer"
"792","It was narrated from Sayyida Aisha that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to fast and have intercourse with his wives."
"793","It was narrated from Sayyida Aisha that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to fast and have intercourse with his wives."
"794","It was narrated from Sayyida Aisha that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to her: \Lift the mat for me.\"" He said: I am menstruating. He said: \""Menstruation is not in your hands.\"""""
"795","Fatimah bint al-Munzir narrated from her grandmother (or grandmother) Sayyidah Asma bint Abi Bakr (RA) that she heard a woman asking the Messenger of Allah (PBUH), she was saying, \What should she do with her clothes when she is free from menstruation?\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""If you see blood on it"
"796","Umm al-Mu'minin Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: An Ansari woman asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about taking a bath during menstruation. How to install? You remained silent, he asked again: How should I apply? Then he remained silent, then Sayyida Aisha (RA) whispered that take a piece of cotton with musk and put it on the spot of blood. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard it and did not deny it."
"797","It was narrated from Sayyida Aisha (RA) that Sayyida Fatima bint Abi Habish (RA) came to the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah! I am a pregnant woman, the bleeding does not stop, so should I skip the prayer? The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \It is the blood of a vein (not menstruation)"
"798","It was narrated from Sayyida Aisha that Jahish's daughter contracted istihaza during the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, so he ordered her to take a bath during every prayer. When she sat in a tub full of water (Merkan), she took a dip and when she got out of the water, the blood would cover the water, then she would pray."
"799","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: There is such and such a woman whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered to bathe before every prayer, and when it became difficult for her to take a bath during each prayer, he (peace be upon her) ordered that she should recite Zuhr and Asr together in one bath, and Maghrib and Isha in one bath, and take a separate bath for Fajr. Imam Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: People say that woman was Sahila bint Suhail, and Yazid bin Haroon said that she was Sahila bint Sahil."
"800","It is narrated on the authority of Sayyida Aisha (RA) that a woman was suffering from Istihaha during the time of the Messenger of Allah (PBUH). Shuba said: I asked Abd al-Rahman bin Qasim: Did the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, give him an order? Abd al-Rahman said: I am not narrating from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"801","The translation and takhrej of this hadith has also been passed in Hadith No. (797)."
"802","On the authority of Sayyida Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, Fatima bint Abi Habish said: O Messenger of Allah! I am such a woman who suffers from the blood of istihazah, so should I give up prayer in such a condition? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \No"
"803","It was narrated from Sayyida Umm Salama, the wife of the Prophet, peace be upon him: A woman used to bleed during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Sayyida Umm Salama, may God bless him and grant him peace, asked the Messenger of God for a fatwa about her, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Count the number of days and nights that she menstruated each month before this disease, and give up prayer for that number of days, then when those days have passed and the time for prayer has come. So take a ghusl, keep a cotton pad on the fridge, then pray.\""
804"""
"804","(Marfu' Hadith) 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abd al-Majid narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from 'Urwah, from 'A'ishah, from Umm Habibah (ra), who said: ""O Messenger of Allah, blood (istihadah) has overcome me."" He said: ""Perform ghusl and pray."""
"805","Umrah bint Abd al-Rahman said: I heard from Umm al-Momineen Sayyida Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, that Sayyida Umm Habiba bint Jahsh, may Allah be pleased with her, came to the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace. She had been complaining of istihadah for seven years. Read it.” Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: So Sayyida Umm Habiba (may Allah be pleased with her) used to bathe before every prayer and would pray, and when she sat in the tub, red blood would come to the surface of the water, then (after bathing) she would pray."
"806","It was narrated from Sayyida Aisha (RA) that Sayyida Umm Habiba bint Jahsh (RA) fell ill with istihaza during the time of the Messenger of Allah (PBUH), so the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) ordered her to bathe before every prayer."
"807","Qasim said: The woman who contracted istihazah was Badiya bint Ghilan al-Thaqfiyyah."
"808","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: Indeed, it was the lady Sahlah bint Sahl bin Amr who complained of istihazah, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered her to take a bath before every prayer, and when it became difficult for her, he (peace be upon her) ordered her to recite Zuhr and Asr in one bath, and Maghrib and Isha in one bath, and to bathe in the morning prayer."
"809","Sa'd bin Ibrahim said: The dispute over the name of this woman occurred because the three women (to whom this complaint was made) were married to Sayyidna Abd al-Rahman bin Awf, so some said she was Umm Habiba, some said she was Badiya, and some said she was Sahlah bint Suhail."
"810","Qaqaa bin Hakim asked Saeed (Ibn Al-Masib) about the issue of Mustahadah, so he said: Nephew! Is there no one left who knows more about this problem than me? When there are days of menstruation, she should leave the Mustahadha prayer and when her period ends, she should take a bath and pray."
"811","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, about the Mustahadhah that she will give up prayer during the days of menstruation, then take a bath and put on a piece of cotton, then pray. Someone asked: What if the blood continues to flow? He said: Even if it does not flow like a stream. That is, he should fill a specific place with cotton and pray as much blood as he wants."
"812","Ammar bin Abi Ammar said that Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) used to have the strictest position regarding Mustahadhah, but then he relaxed. A woman came to him and inquired that I am Mustahadhah, can I enter the Kaaba? He said: Yes, no matter how much blood flows, you can enter the Kaaba, tie a cotton well and go inside."
"813","Qameer (daughter of Imran, wife of Masrooq) said: I asked Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) about Mustahazah, and she replied that she should wait (i.e. skip the prayer) during the days (of menstruation) on which she used to skip the prayer, and when the day of purification (purification) comes on which she was purified, then she should perform ablution and perform ablution at the time of each prayer and pray."
"814","Abu Jaafar narrated the above saying from Sayyida Aisha."
"815","Qameer narrated from Sayyida Aisha. The translation of this hadith has passed in (813)."
"816","On the authority of Udi bin Thabit, he heard from his father, and he from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \The Mustahadha should leave the prayer during the days of the menstrual period"
"817","Imam Hasan al-Basri (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated about the Mustahadha woman who knows her menstrual periods, when she gets divorced and the bleeding continues, she will have three menstrual periods according to the days. And it was narrated from them about her prayer that she will not pray on the days of her menstruation in every month."
"818","It is narrated from Mu'tamar (bin Sulaiman) that his father asked Qatadah: What should a woman do if she knows the days of her menstruation, and the bleeding continues for five, four or three more days? He said: I will pray. Sulaiman said: If the bleeding continues for two days? He said: This is the blood of menstruation. He said: And I asked Imam Ibn Sirin, may God have mercy on him, and he said: Women know this better."
"819","Imam Hasan al-Basri (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated: A woman who bleeds during the days of purification, in my opinion, she should perform ghusl and pray."
"820","On the authority of Shahr bin Hushab: Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with her, was asked about a musthaza woman, and he said: She will wait for the number of days of her menstrual period and stop praying, then she will perform ghusl and pray until the days of her menstruation come, then she will stop praying and then perform ghusl."
"821","Abu Ja'far Muhammad bin Ali said about Mustahadhah: During the days of menstruation, she should stop praying, then she will take a bath and put on a piece of cotton and perform ablution during each prayer."
"822","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: A musthazah will sit during her period (i.e. she will not pray), then she will take a ghusl and perform ablution for each prayer (i.e. it is not necessary to take a bath)."
"823","Anas bin Sireen said: A woman from All Anas was afflicted with istihaza, so he ordered me to inquire about the problem from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas. He replied that when she sees a lot of red blood, she should not pray, and when she sees tahr at any time of the day, she will perform ghusl and pray. (In other words, if menstruation stops after a while, she will take a bath and pray)."
"824","Anas bin Sireen said: Anas bin Malik's slave girl (Umm Wuld) became mustahaha, so people asked me to ask Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him, for a fatwa."
"825","A woman asked him: I have istihaza disease, so he said: When you see fresh blood, you should stop praying during the days of menstruation."
"826","Ibrahim said: A musthazah will sit in the period of menstruation (i.e. she will not pray and become pure), she will perform ghusl once for Zuhr Asr, she will delay Maghrib and pray at the beginning of Isha, and she will perform ghusl once for Fajr, and she will not fast, nor associate with her husband, nor touch the Holy Qur'an."
"827","Ata said: Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) used to say about Mustahadhah that she would perform ghusl once for Zuhr and Asr and once for Maghrib and Isha, and he also used to say that she would delay Zuhr and pray Asr early, and delay Maghrib and pray Isha early."
"828","It was narrated from Mujahid about Mustahadhah that when her menstrual blood becomes cloudy, at Asr time, if the bleeding is large, she should perform ablution and take a cloth and tie it with cotton, then recite Zuhr and Asr together, and continue doing the same, then recite Maghrib Isha together, and continue doing the same, then pray the morning prayer."
"829","Ata, Saeed, Ikrima, may God have mercy on him, used to say about Musthaza that she would perform ghusl once a day for the first prayer (Zhuhr) and Asr, and perform ghusl once for Maghrib Isha, perform both prayers, and perform ghusl once for Fajr prayer."
"830","Abdullah bin Shaddad said: A woman with excessive menstruation will perform ghusl, then recite Zuhr Asr together, if she sees something, then she will perform ghusl and recite Maghrib Isha together."
"831","Sumayi said: I asked Saeed bin Al-Masayyib about Mustahadah, and he said: She will sit during the days of menstruation, and she will take a ghusl once from Zuhr to Zuhr (a day), and whose clothes she will tie, her husband can have intercourse with her, and she will also fast. Simi said: Has anyone said this? So they picked up the pebbles."
"832","Yahya bin Saeed narrated to Saeed bin Al-Musayyib that (Mustahazah) will perform Ghusl once from Zuhr to Zuhr and perform ablution (only) for each prayer."
"833","Qaqaa bin Hakim and Zayd bin Aslam sent Sami to Saeed bin Al-Masib to ask him about Mustahadhah and how he should perform Ghusl. Saeed said: She will perform Ghusl once from Zuhr to Zuhr on the second day."
"834","It was narrated from Imam Hasan (may Allah have mercy on him) about Mustadha that she would perform (one) Ghusl from Zuhr to Zuhr the next day."
"835","Imam Hasan al-Basri, may God have mercy on him, said: A musthazah will give up prayer during the days of her menstruation, then she will perform one ghusl from noon to noon, and she will perform ablution for each prayer, she will fast, she will pray, and her husband can have intercourse with her."
"836","Ibad bin Mansoor narrated the same from Hasan and Ata."
"837","On the authority of Masrooq, may God have mercy on him, on the authority of Qumayr, that Sayyida Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, said about Mustahadhah that she would perform ghusl once every day."
"838","It is narrated on the authority of Nafi that Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (RA) used to say: A musthahaza woman will perform ghusl from Zuhr to Zuhr. Marwan said: This is also the opinion of Imam Uzai, may God have mercy on him."
"839","On the authority of Abd al-Karim (bin Malik al-Jazri), Saeed bin Al-Musayb, may God have mercy on him, said: A musthazah will perform ghusl for the first prayer of every day."
"840","It is narrated from Ikrimah that Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) did not see any problem in having intercourse with a musthazah's husband."
"841","Salim al-Aftas said: Saeed bin Jubayr, may God have mercy on him, was asked: Can sexual intercourse be performed with Mustahadhah? So he said: Prayer is greater than sexual intercourse."
"842","On the authority of Sami, Saeed bin Al-Musayb, may God have mercy on him, said: Her husband can have sexual intercourse."
"843","On the authority of Yunus, Imam Hasan (may God have mercy on him) said about Mustahadhah: Her husband can have sexual intercourse."
"844","On the authority of Abdullah bin Muslimah, Saeed bin Jubayr, may God have mercy on him, said about Mustahadhah: Her husband can have intercourse with her, even if the blood does not fall on the mat."
"845","On the authority of Hameed, it was said to Bakr bin Abdullah that Hajjaj bin Yusuf says that her husband cannot have sexual intercourse with a musthaza woman."
"846","On the authority of Hameed, Imam Hasan (may God have mercy on him) said: The husband can have sexual intercourse."
"847","Ata said about Mustahadhah: Her husband can have sexual intercourse, she will give up prayer during the days of menstruation, when prayer is permissible for her, sexual intercourse will also be permissible."
"848","On the authority of Imam Shaabi, may God have mercy on him, Sayyiduna Ali (may God be pleased with him) said: Her husband can have sexual intercourse with a mustahadhah."
"849","Narrated by Qatadah: Saeed bin Al-Masib, Hasan and Ata said about Mustahadhah: She will perform ghusl and pray, fast in Ramadan, and her husband can have sexual intercourse with her."
"850","Narrated by Hafs: Imam Hasan Basri (may Allah have mercy on him) used to say that her husband will not have sexual intercourse with a musthazah. Abul Nu'man said: Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan said to me: I do not know that anyone has narrated this saying from Hasan."
"851","It is narrated from Khalid (bin Mehran) that Imam Muhammad bin Sirin, may God have mercy on him, considered sexual intercourse with a mustahadah woman to be an abomination."
"852","Imam Ibrahim Nakhai, may God have mercy on him, said: Her husband will not have sexual intercourse with a musthazah, nor will she fast, nor will she touch the Mushaf."
"853","It is narrated on the authority of Qamir that Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: Her husband will not sleep with a Mustahadhah."
"854","Imam Ibrahim Nakhai (may God have mercy on him) said: It was said that a musthazah will not have sexual intercourse, she will not fast, she will not touch the Mushaf, only she is allowed to pray. Yazid bin Haroon (his narrator) said: Her husband will have sexual intercourse with her and everything is lawful for her (Mustahazah) that is lawful for a chaste woman."
"855","On the authority of Yunus (bin Ubayd), Imam Hasan Basri, may God have mercy on him, said: A woman will refrain from prayer for seven days during her menstruation, then if she becomes pure, then it is fine, otherwise she will refrain from prayer for ten days after the beginning of menstruation, and if she becomes pure on ten days, then it is fine, otherwise she will perform ghusl and pray, and she will be regarded as mustahaha."
"856","Narrated by Rabi', Hasan, may God have mercy on him, said: The period of menstruation is ten days, more than that there will be mustahadah."
"857","Ata said: The maximum period of menstruation is fifteen days."
"858","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik Radiyallahu Anhu said: The period of menstruation is ten days, if it is more than that, it is mustahaha."
"859","Saeed bin Jubayr, may God have mercy on him, said: The period of menstruation is up to thirteen days, more than that (if the bleeding continues, it is mustahadah)."
"860","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik Radiyallahu Anhu said: Menstruation will be counted for ten days, then that woman will be considered Mustahadhah."
"861","Saeed bin Jubayr, may God have mercy on him, said: Menstruation lasts for thirteen days, more than that is mustahadah."
"862","Imam Hasan Basri, may God have mercy on him, said: When he sees blood, he should stop praying, and wait for one or two days after the menstrual period, after that it will be considered mustahadhah."
"863","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: A woman with excessive menstruation will wait for three, four, five, six, seven, eight, nine, and ten days (that is, only the menstrual period will be counted)."
"864","Ata said: It has come to us that the Mustahadha will wait one day for her period."
"865","Sayyidna Anas bin Malik Radiyallahu Anhu says: Mosthaha will be done on more than ten days."
"866","Ata said: The maximum duration of menstruation is fifteen days."
"867","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The minimum period of menstruation is three days. Imam Darmi (may Allah have mercy on him) was asked: Is this your view? He said: Yes, when the habit is like this, the menstrual period is only three days. Sufyan said: I asked Imam Darmi, may God have mercy on him, about this, and he said: The minimum period of menstruation is one day and one night, and the maximum period is fifteen days."
"868","Imam Hasan (may Allah have mercy on him) said: The minimum period of menstruation is three (days)."
"869","Al-Hakam ibn al-Mubarak informed us, Makhlad ibn Yazid informed us, from Ma'qil ibn 'Ubayd Allah, from 'Ata', who said: \The minimum duration of menstruation is one day.\"""""
"870","Imam Hasan (may Allah have mercy on him) said: If the bleeding occurs one or two days before the start of menstruation, it is menstruation."
"871","Qatadah and Qays bin Saad narrated from Ata about a virgin girl that if she menstruates and the bleeding continues, in such a case she will abandon the prayer according to her female counterparts."
"872","Sufyan said: When a woman menstruates for the first time, she will be considered to be menstruating like other women."
"873","Ata said about an old woman who bleeds: We do not consider it as menstruation."
"874","It is narrated from Ata about a woman who did not menstruate for thirty years, then she saw the blood, so they ordered (this old woman) like Mustadha. (That is, she is under the order of Mustahadhah, she will pray after performing ghusl and ablution.)"
"875","Ata said: If an elderly woman bleeds, she is under the command of Mustahadha, and she will do the same as Mustahadha."
"876","It is narrated from Ata and Haqm bin Utaiba about an old woman whose menstruation has stopped and she bleeds, then she will perform ablution and pray, but she will not take bath. Imam al-Darmi (may Allah have mercy on him) was asked about such a woman and he said: She will perform ablution and pray, and if she is divorced, she will observe the Idda according to the month."
"877","Sufyan Thauri said: The period of tahr is fifteen days."
"878","Imam Ibrahim Nakhai, may God have mercy on him, said: When a woman menstruates three times in a month or forty days? He said: Let the true righteous women bear witness that it happened that the prayer became forbidden for her due to menstruation, so her period was completed. Abu Muhammad Imam Darmi said: I heard Yazid bin Haroon saying: I consider the period of tahr to be fifteen days as correct."
"879","Amir (Shaabi) said: A woman brought a dispute to Sayyidna Ali (RA) that her husband had divorced her, and that I had menstruated three times in one month. How can I decide in your presence? He said: Decide. He said: And you are here? Then he said: You decide, then (the judge) Shareeh said: If the pious and trustworthy women of his family say that this has happened, and every time she has prayed after being free from menstruation, then it is permissible for her, otherwise not. Hearing this, Sayyiduna Ali (RA) praised him and said: Qalun Qalun, in the Roman language Qalun Shabash, is called a very good person."
"880","Ikrimah (the teacher of Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him) said in the commentary of the verse: “And it is not lawful for them to conceal what Allah has created in the mercy of them.” (That is, it is not permissible for women to hide what Allah has created in their wombs, i.e. to hide the cessation of menstruation). \n Imam al-Darmi (may Allah have mercy on him) was asked: Do you also say that this means menstruation? So he said: No, and Imam Darami was asked about the decision of the above-mentioned Shariah that he also says the same? So he said: No, how can menstruation occur three times in one month?"
"881","It is narrated from Umrah that Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) used to prevent women from seeing menstrual blood at night, and said: It may be yellow or cloudy water."
"882","Rabat, the maidservant of Umrah, said that Umrah prohibited women from bathing until the cotton turned white."
"883","Sufyan Al-Thawri said: Khaki (muddy water) and yolk during the days of menstruation will count as menstruation, and after the days of menstruation, everything between the blood and yolk will be considered istihadah. Imam Darmi (may Allah have mercy on him) was asked: Do you believe in Sufyan's statement? He said: Yes."
"884","Fatimah bint Muhammad (who was the guardian of Umrah) said that a Quraysh woman sent a piece of cotton to Umrah, which had something like yolk on it, and asked if a woman saw only such yolk during menstruation, did she become pure? Umrah replied that no, unless the cotton came out completely white (that is, the woman was not purified)."
"885","Fatimah (bint al-Munzar) said: We were in the lap of Sayyida Asmaa bint Abi Bakr (may God be pleased with her) and one of us would menstruate, then she would perform ghusl and pray when she was pure."
"886","Ata said: In the days of menstruation, Safra and Qudra will be counted as menstruation. That is, if the yellow and clay-like fluid comes during the days of menstruation, it is menstruation, so that woman will leave the prayer."
"887","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: When bleeding, do not pray until you see a white cloth, then take a bath and pray."
"888","Asim Al-Ahwal said: Imam Hasan, may God have mercy on him, did not consider anything like bile and turbidity and the smoke of meat. That is, they did not return from menstruation."
"889","Sayyida Umm Atiya, may Allah be pleased with her, said: We did not count yellow and brown (colour). That is, they did not give any importance to it."
"890","Imam Hasan, may God have mercy on him, said about the woman who saw blood during the days of Tahar, he said: In my opinion, she will perform ghusl and pray."
"891","Imam Ibn Sireen, may God have mercy on him, said: People did not consider any evil in Safra and Qadra."
"892","Muhammad bin Al-Hanafiyyah said about a woman who sees jaundice after tahr (purity) that it is triya (i.e. triya, secretion), she should wash it and perform ablution and pray."
"893","Imam Hasan (may Allah have mercy on him) said: After Ghusl, there is nothing except Tahur in the Triya. Imam al-Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: Tariya means: Safrah and Kadrah."
"894","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: If a woman feels dry after one or two days of bathing, she will clean herself and pray."
"895","Ata said: There is nothing else except cleanliness in the toilet after the bath."
"896","Sayyida Umm Atiya (RA) who also pledged allegiance to the Prophet (PBUH), said: After taking a bath, we did not care about Safra and Kudra."
"897","Imam Hasan (may God have mercy on him) said: If a menstruating woman sees clotted fresh blood one or two days after taking a bath, then she should not pray for another day, after that she will be considered Mustahadha."
"898","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: When a woman is purified from menstruation, then after purification she sees something that makes her suspicious, then this is the movement of the devil in the womb, so when she sees something like hemorrhage or a spot of blood or the smell of meat, she should perform ablution and perform the prayer, and if she sees fresh blood in which there is no doubt, then she should abandon the prayer (that is, count it as menstrual blood). Imam Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: I heard Yazid bin Haroon say: If a woman's menstrual period is seven days and she sees the whiteness of tahr and then marries, and then sees blood within ten days of this seven-day period, then her marriage is valid and valid. And if she becomes pure for less than seven days and gets married, then the blood comes, then her marriage is not valid and permissible, it is menstrual blood. Imam Darmi (may Allah have mercy on him) was asked: Do you also say the same? He said: Yes."
"899","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) about a woman whose period of menstruation is six or seven days, then if she sees bile or blood or one drop or two drops of blood, it is useless and there is no harm in it."
"900","Abdul Kareem said: I asked Ata about a woman who takes a ghusl after her period is over, and then gets jaundice."
"901","Ata said about Mustahadhah: She will not pray for one or two more days after menstruation, then she will perform ghusl, then if she sees tar, she will perform ablution and pray. When the sun sets and she sees Tri, she performs ablution and prays, and if it is blood, she postpones Maghrib and prays early Isha, and performs both prayers with one bath. Imam al-Darmi (may Allah have mercy on him) said: According to me, Iqra means menstruation."
"902","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyida Aisha that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed I'tikaf, and some of his wives also performed I'tikaf with him, even though she was mustahaha and was bleeding, and because of the blood, she used to put down a pan. Ikramah said: Sayyida Aisha (RA) saw the yellow colored water and said: This kind of water used to come to so-and-so Sahiba."
"903","Hajjaj bin Artat said: I asked Atta about the woman who was purified from menstruation and then saw jaundice, so he said: Perform ablution."
"904","Imam al-Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: I read the hadith of Malik bin Anas on Zayd bin Yahya and asked him about the woman whose period of menstruation is seven days and the bleeding continues, so he said: She will wait three more days. (That is, menstruation will be counted for ten days, then it will enter the order of Mustahadhah.)"
"905","Imam Hasan (may God have mercy on him) said: If a woman is pure at the time of prayer and does not perform ghusl despite being able to do so, then she should perform this prayer."
"906","It is narrated from Imam Hasan Basri, may God have mercy on him, that when a woman menstruates after praying two rak'ahs, she will not perform the qadha of this prayer after she is purified."
"907","This effect has the same meaning as mentioned in (905)."
"908","Ata said about the woman who becomes pure at Zuhr and does not take bath until Asr, both of them said that she will recite Zuhr Qadha."
"909","(Maqtu' hadith) Muhammad ibn Isa informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Yunus informed us from al-Hasan..."
"910","(Maqtu' hadith) And Mughirah, from Amir..."
"911","It was narrated from Imam Hasan, Imam Amir Shaabi and Imam Ibrahim, may God have mercy on him, about a woman who neglects prayer and gets her period, they said: She will perform this prayer (Qadha) (i.e., she will have to perform those prayers after ablution)."
"912","Imam Hasan (may Allah have mercy on him) said about a woman who neglects to pray when it is time to pray and does not pray even if her menstruation begins, then she will perform Qadha after taking a bath."
"913","Hasan and Qatadah said: If a woman misses a prayer and menstruates, there is a qadha (of this prayer) after purification."
"914","Imam Shaabi, may God have mercy on him, said: When a woman neglects to perform her period and menstruates, she will perform Qadha (of this prayer)."
"915","Saeed bin Jubayr, may God have mercy on him, said: If a woman menstruates during prayer, there is no qada on her. Imam al-Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: Yaqub: Ibn al-Qaqa'a is a male judge and Abu Yusuf: Shaykh Makki."
"916","Ata, may God have mercy on him, said: When a woman becomes pure before Maghrib, she will pray Zuhr and Asr, and if she is pure before Fajr, she will pray Maghrib Isha."
"917","The above-mentioned hadith is also narrated from Saeed Ibn Al-Musayyib, may God have mercy on him."
"918","It is also narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"919","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Hasan (may Allah be pleased with him) that a woman who is purified during prayer will pray."
"920","Ata, Taus and Mujahid, may God have mercy on him, said that when a menstruating woman becomes pure before Fajr, she should pray Maghrib and Isha, and when she becomes pure before sunset, she should pray Zuhr and Asr."
"921","The ruling said about Haeedah that when she sees purity at the end of the day, she should pray Zuhr and Asr, and if she sees purity at the end of the night, she should also pray Maghrib and Isha."
"922","The same has been narrated from Imam Taus (may God have mercy on him)."
"923","It is narrated from Mugheera that Imam Ibrahim Nakhai, may God have mercy on him, used to say: At the time of Asr, if a woman is pure, then she should recite Zuhr and Asr."
"924","Shu'ba said: I asked Hamad (bin Abi Sulaiman): When a woman is pure during prayer? He said: Pray."
"925","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: When a woman is pure at the time of a prayer, she should pray, and she will not pray another prayer."
"926","Imam Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: I read this statement from Imam Malik, may God have mercy on him, in the presence of Zayd bin Yahya: If a woman becomes pure after Asr? He said: Zuhr and Asr (both) will be recited. Imam al-Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: If the time of tahr is a little before sunset, then only Asr will be recited, not Zuhr, and if it is pure after sunset, then there is no wajib on it. Said: No."
"927","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that a woman wrote to him that I have been suffering from Istihaza for so many days and I have heard that Sayyidna Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said that such a woman will take bath during every prayer. Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: We do not find any leave for you except the saying of Ali."
"928","Yahya bin Abi Kathir said: Abu Salama or Ikrimah narrated to me that Umm al-Mo'minin Sayyidah Zainab (RA) used to perform I'tikaf with the Messenger of Allah (PBUH), and she used to bleed (Istihazah), and he (PBUH) ordered her to take bath before every prayer."
"929","It was narrated from Yahya bin Abi Kathir that Sayyidna Ali and Sayyidna Ibn Masoud (may Allah be pleased with them) used to say that a musthaza should take a bath during every prayer."
"930","Imam Uza'i, may God have mercy on him, said: I heard from Ata bin Abi Rabah that (the mustahadhah) would perform a ghusl for every two prayers and a separate ghusl for Fajr. Imam Uza'i, may God have mercy on him, said: Zuhri and Makhool, may God have mercy on him, used to say that she would perform ghusl for every prayer."
"931","On the authority of Abu Salamah, Umm Habiba said: Wahib mentioned that Umm Habiba bint Jahsh used to bleed and he asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about it, so he ordered: \Take a bath and pray at the time of every prayer.\"""""
"932","Abu Bashir (Ja'far bin Abi Al-Washiyah) said: I heard Sa'eed bin Jubayr, may God have mercy on him, say: A woman wrote to Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas and Ibn Zubair, may God be pleased with them, that I am mustahadah, not pure, and I am asking you both to remind me of Allah to give me a fatwa. Abu Bashar said: I read this letter and wrote the answer with my own hand that I do not find anything other than the saying of Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) (i.e. what he said is correct). It was said that Kufa is a cold place."
"933","Narrated by Mujahid: Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may God be pleased with him) was asked that his region is a cold region, so he said: (Then) recite Zuhr late and Asr early, and perform ghusl once."
"934","It was narrated from Sayyidah Zainab bint Umm Salama (may Allah be pleased with her) that the daughter of Jahsh was married to Abd al-Rahman bin Awf and she used to bleed, and when she got out of the bath or tub, the blood would come to the surface of the water, then she would pray."
"935","Imam Uza'i, may God have mercy on him, said: I heard from Imam Zuhri and Yahya bin Abi Kathir, may God have mercy on him: They used to say that she (Mustahazah) would perform ghusl separately for each prayer. Imam Uza'i, may God have mercy on him, said: And this tradition has also reached me from Makhool."
"936","Imam Uza'i, may God have mercy on him, said that Ata, may God have mercy on him, informed me that Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him, used to say: There is a ghusl for every two prayers, only the Fajr prayer will be performed with one ghusl."
"937","A woman asked Imam Ibrahim Nakhai, may God have mercy on him, that I continue to bleed. So they said: Sprinkle water, it will stop the blood from you."
"938","It was narrated from Imam Hasan, may God have mercy on him, about a divorced woman whose menstruation could not be detected (i.e. whether it came or stopped), he said: She will wait for a whole year, if menstruation comes, then it is fine, otherwise she will spend three months of Idda after one year, then if her menstruation comes, it is fine, if it does not come, her Idda is complete."
"939","Imam Malik (may Allah have mercy on him) was asked about the divorce of Mustahadhah, so he narrated from Ibn Shihab (Zuhari) on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyib (may Allah have mercy on him) that her Idda is one year. Imam Darmi (may Allah have mercy on him) said: This is the saying of Imam Malik (may Allah have mercy on him)."
"940","Amr bin Dinar said: Jabir bin Zayd was asked about the divorce of such a young girl, Bana Kabir Sunni, whose menstruation has stopped, (what will be her Idda?) So he said: She will spend the same period as her period without menstruation. Imam Taaws (may God have mercy on him) said: I will spend three months of Idda."
"941","On the authority of Muammar, Imam Zahri, may God have mercy on him, said: When a man divorces his wife and stops menstruating once or twice, and this interruption is due to old age, she will complete three months of Idda, and if she is young and is in doubt, she will perform Idda for one year."
"942","Narrated by Qatadah: Ikrima (Mulay Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him) said: A mustahadhah and a woman whose menstruation does not last, sometimes once in a month, sometimes twice, her period will be three months (i.e. the period of divorce)."
"943","It is narrated from Hisham that Hamad said: She will perform the Idda of three Qur'a (i.e. three periods)."
"944","Saeed bin Al-Musayb, may God have mercy on him, said: The period of mustahadhah is one year."
"945","Imam Hasan, may God have mercy on him, said: The mustahadah will perform the Idda according to the period of menstruation, that is, if she is divorced, then there are three Iddas."
"946","Imam al-Zuhri (may Allah have mercy on him) said: Idda will be performed by Iqra (i.e. according to menstruation or purification). Imam al-Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: The people of Hijaz take \Iqra\"" to mean the state of purity"
"947","Imam Hasan (may Allah have mercy on him) said: Mustahadha will perform the Idda according to the Iqra."
"948","It was narrated from Imam Uza'i (may Allah have mercy on him) that I asked (Ibn Shihab) Zuhri (may Allah have mercy on him) about a man who divorced his young wife, she used to menstruate, but at the time of the divorce her menstruation stopped, and she did not see blood, so how long will her period be? He said: Three months."
"949","Imam Uza'i (may Allah have mercy on him) said: And I also asked Imam Zuhri (may Allah have mercy on him) that a man divorced his wife, and if her menstruation stopped twice, then how many days will she spend in ``Idah?'' He said: His Eid will be one year."
"950","He also said: I also asked Imam Zahri, may God have mercy on him: A man divorced his woman who was menstruating, she stopped for three months (i.e. did not menstruate), but once menstruated, then (once) menstruation stopped and she sat for seven or eight months (did not menstruate), then menstruated a second time, the first time came early, the second time menstruated very late, so how will she spend the Eid? He said: If her menses are reversed at the appointed time, then her period will be one year."
"951","Imam Uza'i (may Allah have mercy on him) said: If divorce takes place and menses occur once a year, then how long will it be? He said: If she had menstruation and tahr at the appointed time, then in our opinion, she will spend the period of menstruation."
"952","Narrated by Imam Uza'i, may God have mercy on him: I asked Imam Zuhri, may God have mercy on him: If a man buys a minor slave who cannot conceive, what will be the period of waiting for him? He said: Three months."
"953","Yahya bin Abi Kathir said: There will be a period of forty-five days."
"954","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, used to say about Mustahadhah that she would take bath before every prayer, then pray."
"955","Hammad said: If a musthaza woman does not pray for many months due to ignorance, then she will make up for all those prayers. It was asked: How will she do? He said that if he has the strength, he should perform all the Qaza prayers in one day. It was said to Imam Darmi, may God have mercy on him: You say the same thing? He said: \Yes"
"956","Imam Malik bin Anas (may Allah have mercy on him) said: I asked Imam Zuhri (may Allah have mercy on him) about a pregnant woman who bleeds, and he said: She will give up prayer."
"957","Uthman ibn al-Aswad said: I inquired from Mujahid about my wife who bled, I thought she was pregnant, he said: It is from the tribe of Ghiz al-Arham (Allah knows what a woman holds in her stomach and the swelling of the stomach...) [Al-Ra'd 8/13] \n So what is less becomes more in pregnancy."
"958","Asim al-Ahwal narrated on the authority of Ikrima that the verse (Allah knows best what a woman keeps in her belly, and even the swelling of the belly, everything is with Him by estimation) [Al-Ra'd 8/13] \n Ikramah said: This is the menstruation of pregnancy. If a woman menstruates one day during pregnancy, she adds purity to her pregnancy."
"959","Yahya bin Saeed said: There is no difference for us in one issue. Sayyida Aisha (RA) said: If a pregnant woman bleeds, she will not pray until she is purified (i.e. the bleeding stops)."
"960","Asim (al-Ahul) narrated from Ikramah that \Wama Taghiz al-Raham\"" refers to the menstruation of a pregnant woman"
"961","On the authority of Abu Bashar, Mujahid said about “Wama Taghiz al-Raham”: When a pregnant woman menstruates, it is a defect in the child, and when it exceeds nine months, what was missing is a defect in the child."
"962","Bakr bin Abdullah al-Muzni said: My woman menstruates while she is pregnant."
"963","Abu Muhammad Imam Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: I heard from Sulaiman bin Harb: He used to say that my wife gets her period during pregnancy."
"964","Narrated by Yahya bin Saeed: Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: A pregnant woman should stop praying when she sees blood, it is menstrual blood."
"965","The above-mentioned hadith from Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) through Imam Malik (may Allah have mercy on him)."
"966","On the authority of Layth (bin Abi Salim), Imam Shaabi, may God have mercy on him, said about a pregnant woman who bleeds: If there is fresh blood, she should perform ghusl and pray, and if there is other moisture, she should perform ablution and pray."
"967","Imam Uza'i (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated the same."
"968","Imam Hasan Basri (may Allah have mercy on him) said: If a pregnant woman sees the same blood as she used to during her menstrual period, she will abandon the prayer, and if the same bleeding occurs for a day or two, she will not abandon the prayer."
"969","On the authority of Ata, may God have mercy on him, Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said about a pregnant woman who bleeds: This blood does not prevent prayer (i.e., she should not abandon prayer)."
"970","On the authority of Ata, may God have mercy on him, Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated about a pregnant woman that when she sees blood, she should perform ghusl and pray. Yazid said: No, she will not bathe."
"971","On the authority of Yunus bin Ubayd, Imam Hasan Basri, may God have mercy on him, said about a pregnant woman: Whoever bleeds, she is under the command of Mustahadhah, and she will not abandon prayer."
"972","On the authority of Mughirah (Ibn Muqsim), Imam Ibrahim Nakhai, may God have mercy on him, said about a pregnant woman who bleeds: She should wash off the blood, perform ablution, and pray."
"973","Hajjaj bin Arta'ah narrated on the authority of Ata and Hakam, may God have mercy on him, that he said: When a pregnant woman sees blood, she should perform ablution and pray."
"974","Ata, may God have mercy on him, said about the pregnant woman that whoever sees blood should perform ablution and pray."
"975","Imam Hasan Basri (may Allah have mercy on him) said that he is like Mustahadhah."
"976","Imam Ibrahim Nakhai, may God have mercy on him, said: Menstruation does not occur during pregnancy."
"977","Imam Hasan (may God have mercy on him) said about a pregnant woman who bleeds that she is like a musthaha."
"978","Imam Ibrahim Nakhai (may God have mercy on him) said: When a pregnant woman bleeds, she should not abandon prayer."
"979","On the authority of Hajjaj bin Arta'ah, Ata and Huqam bin Utaiba, may God have mercy on him, said about a pregnant woman and a woman whose period has ended: When these two women see blood, they perform ablution, pray, and do not bathe. (That is, this blood will not count as menstruation, but the order of Mustahadhah will apply to them)."
"980","It is narrated from Ata, may God have mercy on him, that the two women will take bath and pray."
"981","On the authority of Ata bin Abi Rabah, may God have mercy on him, that Sayyida Aisha, may God be pleased with her, said: A pregnant woman does not menstruate, so when she sees blood, she should take a bath and pray."
"982","It is narrated from Imam Haqm bin Utbah, may God have mercy on him, that Imam Ibrahim Nakhai, may God have mercy on him, said about a woman who bleeds during labor: It is menstrual blood, so she will abandon prayer."
"983","Imam Hasan al-Basri (may God have mercy on him) said about a pregnant woman who starts having pain and sees blood on the child: She will not pray. Imam al-Darmi (may Allah have mercy on him) said: Pray until you are pregnant."
"984","Qatadah said about the women who have given birth that their purity is like that of women like them."
"985","It was narrated from Imam Hasan, may God have mercy on him, that women who are pregnant will abstain from prayer for 40 days."
"986","Uthman bin Abi al-Aas used to not go near a woman who was in labor for forty days, (i.e. abstained from sexual intercourse). And Imam Hasan, may God have mercy on him, said: Women who are pregnant are from forty-five to fifty days, after that they will be counted as mustahadhah."
"987","Uthman bin Abi Al-Aas said: The period of Nifas is forty days, if it becomes pure, then it is fine, otherwise, the prayer will be offered, do not exceed it."
"988","Ata, may God have mercy on him, said: If the habit of the soul is known, then it is fine, otherwise it will sit for forty days."
"989","Ata, may God have mercy on him, said: Nifas is menstruation. (That is, its order is the order of menstruation)."
"990","On the authority of Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him: Women in labor will wait for about forty days."
"991","Sayyidah Umm Salama (RA) said that during the time of the Messenger of Allah (PBUH), women in labor used to sit for forty days or forty nights, and some of us used to get inheritance on the freckles of our faces."
"992","It is narrated on the authority of Muawiya bin Qura that the wife of ``Aiz bin Amr narrated that she came after twenty days in the state of nifas and entered her husband's bed. He said: I am your wife, I have become pure, so he struck the wife with a foot and said: Do not deceive me in my religion, even spend forty days. It is in Darqutni and the author that she came to him after taking a bath."
"993","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Women in labor will sit for about forty days."
"994","On the authority of Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him: Women in labor will wait forty days."
"995","Mu'tamar bin Sulaiman narrated from his father that Imam Hasan Basri (may God have mercy on him) said about the souls: If they see blood, wait for forty days, then pray. The narrator said: And Imam Shaabi, may God have mercy on him, said: She will wait for two months, then she will be in the order of Mustahadhah."
"996","Makhool said: A pregnant woman will wait 30 thirty days for the birth of a boy and forty days for a girl. Marwan said: This is also the opinion of Saeed bin Abdul Aziz. Imam Uza'i, may God have mercy on him, said: Both boys and girls are equal (that is, the period of nifas is forty days, during these days the menstruation will be under the control of the woman)."
"997","Imam Hasan (may Allah have mercy on him) said: If you see blood for one or two days during labor, it is the blood of childbirth."
"998","It is narrated from Ata, may God have mercy on him, about a pregnant woman, who bleeds during labor, she (pregnant woman) will do what is recommended."
"999","It was narrated from Imam Ibrahim Nakhai, may God have mercy on him, about a woman who has janabat and then menstruates, he said: She will perform ghusl (janabat)."
"1000","The previous example is also narrated from Imam Hasan (may Allah have mercy on him)."
"1001","Ata, may God have mercy on him, said: Menstruation is a greater thing than Janabat."
"1002","It was narrated from Imam Ibrahim (may God have mercy on him) about a man who has sexual intercourse with his wife, then she menstruates."
"1003","Both Ata and Nakhai, may God have mercy on him, said: Such a woman will perform Ghusl Janabat."
"1004","The same is narrated from Imam Hasan (may Allah have mercy on him) (i.e. it is better to take a bath)."
"1005","Hamad was asked about this and he said: Imam Ibrahim (may Allah have mercy on him) said that she would perform Ghusl Janabat."
"1006","Imam Shaabi, may God have mercy on him, said: That woman will take bath."
"1007","Yahya bin Ayyub stated that I heard Huqam bin Utaiba, may God have mercy on him, say: The Salaf used to prefer a menstruating woman to perform ablution during the prayer, then recite the praises of Allah and praise Allah, that is, recite Subhan Allah, Allahu Akbar, etc."
"1008","It was narrated from Sulaiman al-Taimi that I asked Abu Qalaba: Should a menstruating woman perform ablution and recite dhikr during every prayer? He said: I did not find any reason for it."
"1009","On the authority of Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Amir Jahni, may Allah be pleased with him, he used to order a menstruating woman to perform ablution at the time of prayer and to sit in the place of prayer in the courtyard, so that she would recite dhikr and glorify."
"1010","Ata, may Allah have mercy on him, was asked about a menstruating woman: Can she recite (the Qur'an)? He said: No, she can read half a sentence, but she should perform ablution at the time of every prayer, then sit facing the Qibla and recite Tasbeeh and Takbeer, and pray to Allah Almighty."
"1011","Makhool (Syrian) narrated and said that a menstruating woman should be ordered to perform ablution during the prayer time, then facing the Qibla, she should remember Allah. (i.e. engage in divine remembrance)."
"1012","Imam Ibrahim Nakhai, may God have mercy on him, said: A menstruating woman, a menstruating woman, and a woman with prostration listen to the verse, then the side should perform ghusl and perform prostration (recitation), but the menstruating woman will not do so, because she cannot pray."
"1013","Imam Ibrahim (may Allah have mercy on him) said about a menstruating woman who listens to the verse of prostration, he said: She will not make up for it."
"1014","Imam Ibrahim Nakhai (may Allah have mercy on him) said: Nothing is necessary for such a woman."
"1015","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: We used to menstruate in front of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), but he did not order any of us women to return to prayer."
"1016","It was narrated from Mu'adh (daughter of Abdullah) that a woman asked Sayyida Aisha (may God be pleased with her): Will any of us perform the Qada prayer during her menstrual period? Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: Are you Haruriya? We used to menstruate during the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, and we were not ordered to do Qadha."
"1017","Abu al-Nu'man (Muhammad ibn al-Fazl) said: It is as if Hammad made a difference in Ayyub's hadith and brought this hadith."
"1018","Aamir (Shaabi) said: If a menstruating woman hears the verse of prostration, she should not prostrate."
"1019","Abu Qalaba said: A menstruating woman should not prostrate when she hears the verse Sajdah."
"1020","Imam Ibrahim (may Allah have mercy on him) used to make prostration after listening to the verse of Sajdah of a menstruating woman."
"1021","Abu Ghalib (Ajlan) said: I asked Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him, about a menstruating woman, that she will perform the prayer after ablution? He said: These are the pure wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"1022","Abd al-Rahman bin Qasim narrated from his father that a woman came to Sayyida Ayesha and asked, \After purification"
"1023","Kathir bin Ismail said: I asked Fatimah bint Ali: Do you perform the Qada prayer during the days of menstruation? Answered: No."
"1024","A woman asked Sayyida Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her: Will menstruation make up the prayer? Answered: Are you Haruriya? We, the wives of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were menstruating, did you order them to perform qada? Imam al-Darmi (may Allah have mercy on him) said: This means that pure wives did not perform Qadha."
"1025","Imam Ibrahim (may Allah have mercy on him) said: He will mention Janbi and Hayz Allah and recite Bismillah."
"1026","Sufyan Al-Thawri said: It has reached us from Imam Ibrahim Nakhai and Saeed bin Jubeer, may God have mercy on him, that they both used to say: Junbi and Hayz cannot recite the whole verse, they can recite the letter and the sentence."
"1027","It was narrated from Amir Shaabi, may God have mercy on him, that Junbi and Haydah will not read the Qur'an."
"1028","It was narrated from Imam Ibrahim Nakhai, may God have mercy on him, that Sayyiduna Umar, may God be pleased with him, considered reciting the Qur'an from the side as an abomination or forbade it. Shuba said: I also saw in the book that the same was said about menstruation."
"1029","Imam Ibrahim (may Allah have mercy on him) said: Four (persons) will not read the Qur'an, the one who is in the toilet, and the one who is in the bath, the one who is pregnant and menstruating."
"1030","Imam Ibrahim and Saeed bin Jubeer, may God have mercy on him, said: Menstruating women and men and women with janabat can read the beginning of the verse, but they will not read the whole verse until the end."
"1031","It was narrated from Abul Aaliyah about Haydah that she will not read the Qur'an."
"1032","On the authority of Abdullah Bin Ubaidullah Bin Abi Malikah, Sayyida Aisha used to kiss Sayyida Asmaa while she was menstruating."
"1033","Qatadah, may Allah have mercy on him, stated that Janbi can take the name of Allah Ta'ala."
"1034","Abu Wail (Shaqiq bin Salama) said: It was said that menstruating men cannot read the Qur'an, nor can they recite it in the toilet, and there are two situations in which a man cannot even mention Allah, when performing ablution and during sexual intercourse, yes, when he goes to his wife, he should mention the name of Allah before starting \work\""."""
"1035","It is narrated from Ata, may God have mercy on him, about a menstruating woman: Can she recite the Qur'an? He said: No, only the beginning or the end of the sentence can be read."
"1036","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \Four words are not haram even for menstruating women: \""Glory be to God"
"1037","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) was asked about a menstruating woman who listens to the verse of Sajdah. He said: She will not perform Sajdah because Sajdah is also a prayer."
"1038","Both Imam Ibrahim and Abu Al-Zuha, may God have mercy on him, said that she will not perform Sajdah."
"1039","Both Imam Ibrahim and Saeed bin Jubayr, may God have mercy on him, said: Sajdah is not obligatory on him, the prayer is much greater than that. That is, when he leaves the prayer, the Sajdah is less than that."
"1040","Ata, may God have mercy on him, said: What is better than this is the obligatory prayer that has been prevented, i.e., then prostration."
"1041","Imam Hasan Basri (may Allah have mercy on him) said: She will not prostrate."
"1042","It is narrated from Imam al-Zuhri (may Allah have mercy on him) about a woman who has become pure and listens to the verse of Sajdah, that she will not perform Sajdah until she has taken ghusl."
"1043","On the authority of Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to the women: \Give charity because you will be the most in Hell.\"" A woman who was not well-known asked: Why is this? He said: \""Because you curse a lot"
"1044","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: When a woman is free from menstruation, she should wash the stain on the cloth that was close to her skin, and then she can pray in it."
"1045","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: If one of us had a shirt, she would wear it during the days of her menstruation, and she would have janabat in it."
"1046","Sayyida Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: If one of you gets a blood stain on his clothes, he should mix it with his saliva."
"1047","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: When a woman washes off the blood, even if its effect does not disappear, then she should wipe it with a yellow object or a saffron. That is, rub it so that the color changes."
"1048","A woman asked Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her): If there is blood on the cloth, should I wash it and then cut it if the effect does not go away? He said: Water purifies."
"1049","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) used to say: Abu al-Qasim, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, was in the same cloth with me and I was menstruating. If my blood got on him, he would have washed only that place, not transgressing it, then prayed in it."
"1050","Narrated by Imam Ibrahim Nakhai, may God have mercy on him: If the cloth worn by the menstruating woman gets blood on it, she should wash it. If there is no blood, it is not necessary to wash it."
"1051","Mujahid said: A menstruating woman can pray in the clothes in which she was menstruated, except if there is blood in those clothes, (in such a case) just wash the place of blood."
"1052","Sayyida Asma bint Abi Bakr (RA) said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) about menstrual blood that gets on the clothes, and he (PBUH) said: \Scratch it"
"1053","Imam Ibrahim (may Allah have mercy on him) said: If there is no blood on the cloth of menstruation, there is no need to wash the cloth."
"1054","Sayyida Asma bint Abi Bakr (RA) said: I heard a woman asking the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) about clothes, what should a woman do with these clothes when she is free from menstruation? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \If you see blood on it"
"1055","Sayyida Umm Qays (RA) said: I asked the Prophet (PBUH) about menstrual blood on the cloth, and he (PBUH) said: \Wash it with water and berry leaves and scrape it with wood.\"""""
"1056","Karima said: I asked Sayyida Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her: What should a woman do if her menstrual blood gets on her clothes? Answered: Wash it with water. Said: We wash it but the effect remains. Said: Water cleanses."
"1057","Ata, may God have mercy on him, said: Sayyida Aisha, may God be pleased with her, was of the opinion that a woman should rub it on a stone, rub it with wood, or a horn, and then sprinkle water on it."
"1058","Abdullah bin Uthman bin Khatheem said: I asked Saeed bin Jubayr, may God have mercy on him: If Janbi sweats, he should wipe the sweat with a cloth. He said: There is no harm."
"1059","Abdullah bin Uthman said: Saeed bin Jubayr, may God have mercy on him, did not think there was anything wrong with perspiration in the clothes of Janbi."
"1060","Even Imam Shaabi, may God have mercy on him, did not see any problem in it."
"1061","Imam Hasan (may Allah have mercy on him) said: All the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not have two clothes or a cloak."
"1062","It was narrated from Qasim bin Muhammad that Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) was asked about a man who has sexual intercourse with a woman and then wears a cloth, and he sweats in it, so she did not think there was anything wrong with it."
"1063","Ata, may God have mercy on him, said: There is no harm in praying in the clothes in which a woman or a menstruating woman sweats."
"1064","On the authority of Imam Ibrahim Nakhai, may God have mercy on him, regarding a Janbi who sweats on his clothes, he said: There is no harm, and there is no need to sprinkle water on it."
"1065","Narrated by Imam Ibrahim Nakhai, may God have mercy on him: If a menstrual woman sweats in her clothes, splashing water on her will suffice."
"1066","On the authority of Nafi, may God have mercy on him: Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, used to sweat in his clothes in the state of janabat, and then he would pray in the same clothes."
"1067","On the authority of Ikrima, may God have mercy on him: Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him, did not consider anything wrong with the sweating of the menses and genitals."
"1068","On the authority of Zayd bin Aslam: A man asked the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, what is lawful for me during my wife's period. He said: He should fasten his clothes (Azar), then you can have intercourse upstairs."
"1069","It was narrated on the authority of Nafi, may God have mercy on him, that Abdullah bin Abdullah bin Umar sent a messenger to Sayyida Aisha (may God be pleased with her) to ask her whether a man can have intercourse with his wife while she is menstruating. So they replied: She (the menstruating woman) should suck the azaar well down to the bottom, then the husband should have intercourse with her."
"1070","Imam Ibrahim Nakhai (may God have mercy on him) said: A menstruating woman can have sexual intercourse with her husband between the genital area and the thighs."
"1071","Imam Ibrahim (may Allah have mercy on him) said: Umm Imran knows that I stumble into her genitals while menstruating."
"1072","Malik bin Mughal said: A man asked Ata, may God have mercy on him, about the menstruating woman, and he said that there was nothing wrong with her except for the spot of blood."
"1073","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: When I was menstruating, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would order me, \I should take the azaar\"" and then he would have sexual intercourse with me."""
"1074","Maymoon bin Mehran narrated that Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) was asked: What is permissible for a menstruating man from his wife? Answered: Which is above Azar. That is, only above can enjoy above."
"1075","Masrooq inquired from Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that what is permissible for her husband when a woman is menstruating? Answered: Everything is permissible except sexual intercourse. Asked: And when both are in Ihram, what is forbidden? Answered: Everything is forbidden except speech and conversation."
"1076","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said to a man: Avoid the place of blood."
"1077","Amir Shaabi said: When the dirt stops. Another tradition is that when the blood stops, do whatever you want."
"1078","Mujahid said: There is no harm in playing with the thighs and head of a menstruating woman."
"1079","Mujahid said: Come from anywhere other than the place of Dabar and Hayz."
"1080","Umm al-Mu'minin Sayyidah Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: I was in a quilt with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when I started menstruating. He said: The same thing happened to women. He said: \Allah has decreed this for the daughters of Adam.\"" Umm Salamah said: So I stood up and corrected my position. Then she (Peace be upon her) came back. The Messenger of Allah"
"1081","Sayyida Umm Salamah (RA) said: I was in a cloak with the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) when I started menstruating, I took my clothes and came out secretly. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Has your period come?\"" He said: Yes"
"1082","Umm al-Momineen Sayyidah Maimunah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: The Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) used to have sexual intercourse with any of his wives while menstruating."
"1083","Umm al-Mu'minin Sayyida Aisha (RA) said: When one of us menstruated, the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) would order whom to tie, then he would have intercourse with them."
"1084","On the authority of Abu Misra, Umm al-Mu'minin, may God be pleased with her, said: \I used to wear azaar when I was menstruating"
"1085","Narrated by Yazid bin Abi Ziyad: Ibn Jubayr was asked: When a woman is menstruating, is anything lawful for a man? He said: It is halal above Azar."
"1086","It was narrated from Ubaidah (as-Salmani) about menstruation that even if the bed is one but the quilt should be separate, if there is no quilt then the man should put his quilt on it."
"1087","Shareeh (al-Qazi) said: For a man, it is the part above the surah."
"1088","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to hug me when I was menstruating, touch my head, but there was a cloth between us."
"1089","It was narrated from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, that when a woman was menstruating among the Jews, they would not eat or drink with her, they would throw her out of the room, she could not even stay in the house with people. [2-Al-Baqarah: 222] \They ask you about menstruation"
"1090","Shiba bin Hisham Rasbi said: I asked Salem bin Abdullah about the man who lays down with his wife in a quilt during menstruation. (So they said) We leave women of all ages in the state of menstruation (i.e. we do not pass)."
"1091","Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Umar Radiyallahu Anhuma said: If a woman is not pregnant or menstruating, there is no problem in using her leftover water."
"1092","Hukam bin Utbah, may God have mercy on him, said: In such a case, she will put (the cloth) on her private area."
"1093","Umm al-Momineen, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated from Sayyida Maimunah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to have intercourse with any of his wives in the state of menses over the azar, which was tied up to mid-thigh or knee."
"1094","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: I used to comb the blessed head of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when I was menstruating."
"1095","The above mentioned words are narrated from Sayyida Aisha."
"1096","It was narrated on the authority of Nafi, may God have mercy on him, that Sayyiduna Ibn Umar's maidservants used to wash his feet while menstruating, and they used to hold the musli (place of prayer) for him."
"1097","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: A bowl of water would be brought to me and I would drink water with my face in the state of menses, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would also place the holy incense on the same place and drink water, and a bone with some meat taken out would be brought to me, I would scrape the meat with my teeth, then he (peace be upon him) would also place his blessed incense on the same place and take out the meat, then he would order me, I would not take pain and you would have intercourse with me."
"1098","It was narrated from Imam Ibrahim Nakhai, may God have mercy on him, that it was said that a menstruating woman does not have menstruation in her hands, she can wash her hands and knead the dough, and she can make nabeez."
"1099","It is narrated from Imam Ibrahim, may God have mercy on him: He used to say that there is no menstruation in the hands of the menstruating woman, and he used to say that the menstruating woman is the lover of the living."
"1100","Hammad said: I asked Imam Ibrahim Nakhai (may Allah have mercy on him) about shaking hands with Jews, Christians, Magians and menstruating women, so he did not indicate to perform ablution."
"1101","Abdullah Al-Bahi said: Sayyida Aisha (RA) narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (SAW) was visiting the mosque, and he said to a girl: \Give me a prayer rug.\"" He said: \""The Prophet (SAW) wanted to pray with her lying down"
"1102","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to take out his blessed head from the mosque towards me during I'tikaf and I used to wash it."
"1103","Imam Abraham Nakhai, may God have mercy on him, did not consider any problem in performing ablution on a menstruating woman patient."
"1104","It was narrated from Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that she used to wash the blessed head of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when she was menstruating."
"1105","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: If the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in Itikaaf and I was in the state of menstruation, I would have washed your blessed head."
"1106","Shuba narrated that I heard Mughira saying that the Abu Dhabians sent a messenger to Imam Ibrahim (may God have mercy on him) to inquire about menstruation, that she can perform ablution on a sick person? Ibrahim (may Allah have mercy on him) replied: Yes, he said: Can she support him in prayer? Said: No. Shuba said: I asked Mughirah: Did you hear from Ibrahim, may God have mercy on him? Said: No. Imam al-Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: \Watisandah\"" means that she can support him in prayer? (To which he replied that not in prayer)."""
"1107","It is narrated from Qasim that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Sayyida Ayesha: “Give me a place for prayer.” She said: “I am menstruating.”"
"1108","Imam Hasan (may God have mercy on him) was asked: Can ablution be performed on a menstruating woman who drinks water (and then gives birth)? He laughed and said: Yes."
"1109","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Sa'd (RA) said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) about eating with a menstruating woman, and he (PBUH) said: \Eat with her.\"""""
"1110","It was narrated from Nafi, may God have mercy on him, that Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, would ask his slave girl to pick up the prayer mat from the mosque and give it to her."
"1111","It was narrated from Haram bin Hakim that his uncle (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Sa'd, may God be pleased with him) said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about eating while menstruating, and he, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \One of my wives will be menstruating"
"1112","It is narrated from Qasim that Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) did not think there was any problem in touching the veil during menstruation."
"1113","It was narrated from Mujahid, may God have mercy on him: When a menstruating woman becomes pure (i.e. the bleeding of menstruation stops), her husband should not be near her until she performs ghusl."
"1114","From the second chain of transmission, Mujahid, may God have mercy on him, has said the same."
"1115","Sufyan (may Allah have mercy on him) was asked that if the bleeding of a menstruating woman stops, can the husband have sexual intercourse with her before taking bath? He said: No, it was asked: What if he does not take bath for one or two days? He said: Repentance will be made."
"1116","Mujahid, may God have mercy on him, said about the verse \And do not come near them until they are purified"
"1117","It was narrated by Mujahid, may God have mercy on him, that \until he is purified\"" means when the flow of blood stops"
"1118","Uthman ibn al-Aswad said: I asked Mujahid, may God have mercy on him, about a woman who has menstruated: Is it permissible for her husband to have sexual intercourse with her before performing ghusl? He said: No, unless prayer is permissible (intercourse is also not permissible)."
"1119","It is narrated from Hamad that Imam Ibrahim (may God have mercy on him) said: Do not have sexual intercourse until you have taken ghusl."
"1120","It was narrated from Imam Hasan, may God have mercy on him, about a man who performs ablution on his wife before taking a bath after she has been purified, he said: Until she performs a bath, she is in the order of menstruation, and there is an expiation on her, so he should ask about the bath."
"1121","Narrated by Imam Hassan, may God have mercy on him: Her husband will not have intercourse with such a woman."
"1122","Abu al-Khair Murshid al-Alizni said: I heard Sayyidna Uqbah bin Amir Jahni, may God be pleased with him, say: By Allah, I do not have sexual intercourse with my wife on the day she is pure, even if another day passes."
"1123","It is narrated from Ata, may God have mercy on him, that when a woman sees purity, can her husband have sexual intercourse with her or not? He said: Cohabitation is not permissible until he has taken ghusl."
"1124","On the authority of Ata, may God have mercy on him, about such a woman whose bleeding (menstruation) stops, he said: If a man's desire increases, then the woman should wash her private parts, then have sex with her."
"1125","Faruah bin Abi al-Maghra reported, I heard the participant say, a man asked him: If a woman's bleeding stops, can the husband have intercourse with her before performing ghusl? Farwa replied to Abd al-Malik regarding Ata, may God have mercy on him, that he has allowed sexual intercourse before taking a bath during intense sexual desire. Abu Muhammad Imam Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: I am afraid that he has made a mistake, and it was narrated from Laith bin Abi Salim instead of Ata, may God have mercy on him, because I do not know anything like that from Abdul Malik. Abu Muhammad, may God have mercy on him, said: \Al-Shabiq\"" is a man who is very lustful."""
"1126","Imam Hasan Basri (may Allah have mercy on him) said: I have seen the women of Madinah praying with khazab on."
"1127","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) was asked about a woman who rubs her dyed hand, she said: I would rather have my hands cut off with knives."
"1128","It was narrated from Abu Sa'eed (Kathir bin Ubaid) that a woman asked Sayyida Aisha (may God be pleased with her): Can a woman pray after applying khazab? He said: Scratch the yarn and throw it away. Imam al-Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: Abu Saeed is the son of Abul Anbas, and the name of Abul Anbas is Saeed bin Kathir bin Ubaid."
"1129","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may God be pleased with him) said: Our women used to apply henna at night, and when the morning came, they would open it, perform ablution and pray. And after the prayer, she would put on the khazab again, and if it was time for zuhr, then she would open it, perform ablution and pray, in this way the color would be very good, and this thing would not prevent the prayer."
"1130","It was narrated from Nafi, may God have mercy on him, that the women of Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them, used to apply henna (henna) when they were menstruating."
"1131","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Our women used to wear khazaab after Isha and when morning came, they would open it, perform ablution and pray, and when they recited zuhr, they would tie it again and when they had to pray asr, they would untie it."
"1132","Ismail bin Abi Khalid and Amir Shaabi, may God have mercy on him, both said about this person: Whoever has sexual intercourse with his wife while menstruating, he said: He has committed a sin, he should seek forgiveness from Allah, repent, and not do it again."
"1133","The above saying is narrated from Ata, may God have mercy on him."
"1134","Saeed bin Jubayr, may God have mercy on him, said: He committed a sin, but there is no expiation for him."
"1135","Narrated by Abd al-Rahman bin Qasim, his father Qasim was asked about a person who has intercourse with his wife while she is menstruating. He said: He will apologize to Allah Almighty and repent."
"1136","It is narrated from Ata, may God have mercy on him: He should seek forgiveness from Allah and there is no expiation for him. That is, when he has intercourse with his wife while she is menstruating."
"1137","On the authority of Malik bin Al-Khattab on the authority of Al-Anbri: I was listening to Ibn Abi Malikah, who was asked if a man should have sexual intercourse with his wife while she is menstruating. He said: He should seek forgiveness from Allah."
"1138","On the authority of Abu Qalaba, may God have mercy on him: A man came to Sayyiduna Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, and said: I have seen in a dream that I am urinating bloody. He said: Yes, it is so. He said: Fear Allah and do not do this in the future."
"1139","It was narrated from Imam Muhammad bin Sireen, may God have mercy on him, about a man who has sexual intercourse with his wife while she is menstruating, he said: He should seek forgiveness from Allah."
"1140","Yazid bin Ibrahim narrated that I heard Imam Hasan Basri, may God have mercy on him, say about a person who does not fast during the days of Ramadan, he said: On him is the expiation of freeing a slave or slaughtering a camel, or twenty Sa'a (about 45 kilos) of grain is obligatory for forty poor people. And a similar expiation is obligatory on the person who has sexual intercourse with his wife during menstruation."
"1141","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said: \He should give half a dinar in charity.\"""""
"1142","On the authority of Muqsim, Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him, said: A man who sleeps with his wife while she is menstruating should give one dinar or half a dinar in charity."
"1143","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: A man who sleeps with his wife while she is menstruating should give one dinar or half a dinar in charity. Shu'ba said: This ruling is fixed in my memorization, and so-and-so has mentioned the saying of Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him. Someone said: Narrate it to us from your memory and leave so-and-so's words aside. He said: By Allah, even if I meet Umar Nuh (peace be upon him), I do not like to narrate it or remain silent. Abu Muhammad Darami, may God have mercy on him, said: Abdul Hameed: Ibn Zayd bin Abdul Rahman bin Zayd bin Al-Khattab was the governor of Kufa on behalf of Umar bin Abdul Aziz, may God have mercy on him."
"1144","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: If you have sexual intercourse while the blood is flowing, then it is one dinar, and if you have sexual intercourse after the bleeding has stopped, then it is half a dinar."
"1145","On the authority of Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \A man who has intercourse with a menstruating woman should give half a dinar in charity.\"""""
"1146","Abdul Hameed bin Zayd bin Al-Khattab said: Sayyidna Umar bin Al-Khattab (RA) had a wife who disliked sexual intercourse. When he wanted her, she used to pretend she was menstruating (once). He had intercourse with her, but when he saw her, she was telling the truth. So Sayyidna Umar (RA) came to the Messenger of Allah (SAW) and he (SAW) ordered her to give two khums dinars in charity."
"1147","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) was asked: What if a man has sexual intercourse with his wife while she is menstruating? He said: One dinar or half a dinar should be given in charity. Imam Ibrahim Nakhai, may God have mercy on him, said: And ask for forgiveness."
"1148","On the authority of Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When a man has sexual intercourse with his wife while she is menstruating"
"1149","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him, said: When a man has sexual intercourse with his wife in such a state that she is menstruating, one dinar must be given in charity. Imam Ibrahim (may Allah have mercy on him) said: And Istighfar must also be sought."
"1150","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, about a man who has sexual intercourse with his wife while she is menstruating."
"1151","It is narrated from Muqsim that Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Such a person will give one dinar or half a dinar in charity."
"1152","Imam Uza'i (may Allah have mercy on him) also narrated about a man who has intercourse with his wife during menstruation or after she has been purified before taking a bath."
"1153","Ata, may Allah have mercy on him, said: When a man has intercourse with his wife during menstruation, he should give half a dinar in charity. Someone from the audience asked that Hasan (May Allah have mercy on him) says that a slave should be freed? He said: I do not prevent you from this, get as close to Allah as possible. That is, it is better to give charity as much as possible with repentance and forgiveness."
"1154","It is narrated from Ata, may God have mercy on him, that Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him, said: A man who has intercourse with his wife during menstruation will give one dinar in charity."
"1155","Ibn Sabat said: I asked Hafsa bint Abd al-Rahman, Abd al-Rahman who was the son of Abu Bakr. I asked Hafsa: I want to ask you about one thing, but I feel shy. He said: (Son) Nephew, ask what do you want to ask? He said: I want to ask about sexual intercourse with women. He replied that Sayyidah Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated to me, saying that the Ansar did not have sexual intercourse with the wife lying on her face or stomach (i.e. lying on her stomach), and the emigrants used to do so. He refused, and the woman came to Sayyida Umm Salama (RA) and narrated the incident, so when the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) came, the woman went out because of shame. \﴿"""
"1156","Mujahid, may Allah have mercy on him, said: I recited the Qur'an three times to Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, in such a way that he would stop at each verse and ask about what that verse was revealed about, and what was its meaning. I asked Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him, that what is your opinion about \When you are purified"
"1157","It was narrated by Mujahid, may God have mercy on him: «﴿Fatuhuhun from the place of the commandment of Allah﴾» [Baqarah: 222/2] means that they have been ordered to fulfill their need in the place from which they were prevented after purification. (That is, you can have sexual intercourse and avoid sexual intercourse)."
"1158","Abu-Razin explained the meaning of the holy verse «﴿فَأْتوهُنَّ مْهْهْهُ أَمَرَكُمُ اللہُُ﴾” to have sexual intercourse from the place of purity, that is, not in Dabar, but in Qib (Furj)."
"1159","It was narrated from Mujahid, may God have mercy on him: «﴿ And you leave what Allah created for you in the form of your wives. Mujahid, may Allah have mercy on him, said: By Allah, this means the private part of a woman."
"1160","Narrated by Ikramah, may God have mercy on him: The honorable verse: “Your women are your fields, come from wherever you like.” He said: This refers to the Sharam Gah Faraj (i.e. have sexual intercourse before, not during Dabar)."
"1161","Ali Bin Ali Rifa'i narrated that I heard Hasan, may God have mercy on him, he used to say: The Jews did not leave any stone unturned to persecute the Muslims, he used to say: O Companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace! By Allah, the only thing that is lawful for you is that you have intercourse with your wives from one side. He said: On this, Allah Almighty revealed this verse: \Your wives are your fields"
"1162","On the authority of Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, it was narrated that the verse: “Fattuwa Harthaqum annay shaytum” means that you come from anywhere, before and after, while intercourse is only in a certain place."
"1163","Ikramah, may God have mercy on him, said: The people of Jahiliyyah used to treat menstruating women like magicians, so when the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, was mentioned about it, this noble verse was revealed: [Al-Baqarah: 222/2] And it became more severe about menstruating women."
"1164","It was narrated from Mujahid, may God have mercy on him, that it is blood. (That is, menstrual blood is dirt.) And Qatadah, may God have mercy on him, said: It is dirt."
"1165","On the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayb, may God have mercy on him, regarding the matter of “(Nisa’u’ukum) harth for you, so it is your harth-kum, and it is not for you.” [Al-Baqarah: 223/2], he said: If you want, you can divorce or if you want, don’t divorce."
"1166","Hasan al-Basri (May Allah have mercy on him) narrated: Do whatever you want, as long as intercourse is in a designated place."
"1167","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah Ansari (RA) that the Jews said to the Muslims that whoever has sexual intercourse with his wife from behind, her child will be born a virgin, so Allah revealed this honorable verse: [Baqarah: 223/2] \Women are your crops"
"1168","It was narrated from Ikramah, may God have mercy on him, that he should have sexual intercourse with his wife whether he is sitting in front of him or behind him."
"1169","Imam Ibrahim Nakhai, may God have mercy on him, said: «﴿Fatuhuhun from where Allah commands you...﴾» [Baqarah: 222/2] means that (intercourse) should be in the refrigerator."
"1170","Mujahid, may God have mercy on him, said: A man who has sexual intercourse with his wife is equivalent to having sexual intercourse with a man (i.e. Aghlam). In Istishahhad, the verse was recited: “And they ask you about menstruation, say that it is impurity. has given you permission to have intercourse.” [Al-Baqarah 222/2] It is explained that stay away from menstruating women, i.e. the fridge, then he recited this verse of Surah Baqarah: \Your women are your fields and come to your fields from wherever you want\"" meaning that you should have sexual intercourse from standing to sitting or lying on your stomach"
"1171","On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Hurairah, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Whoever associates with a menstruating woman"
"1172","Abul-Qaqa' (Abdullah bin Khalid) al-Jarimi said: A man came to Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with him, and said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman! Can I visit my wife from wherever I want? He said: Yes, he said: From which side do I want to come? He said: Yes, he then asked: Can I have sexual intercourse in any way I want? He said: Yes, another person said: Sir! Its purpose (there is something else, i.e. its purpose is to have sexual intercourse in Dabar) is bad. Imam al-Darmi (may God have mercy on him) was asked: Is this your opinion? He said: Yes."
"1173","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, called sexual intercourse with a woman very abominable and regarded it as a serious defect."
"1174","On the authority of Amr bin Dinar, the verse: (Lot (peace be upon him) said to his people) \Indeed"
"1175","On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Hurairah, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \The man who has intercourse with his wife"
"1176","On the authority of Sayyiduna Ali bin Mutlaq, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \If one of you breaks his ablution during prayer"
"1177","Abu al-Habaab Saeed bin Yasar said: I asked Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him: What is your opinion if I perform Thamida with female slaves? Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (RA) said: What is this Tahmid? I said: Dabar, so he said: Can any of the Muslims do such a (dirty thing)?"
"1178","Harami bin Abdullah said: In a meeting of Bani Waqif, we were discussing women and what is enjoyed by them, then Sayyidna Khuzimah bin Thabit (RA) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: \People! Allah is not ashamed of the truth. Do not have sexual intercourse with women.\"""""
"1179","Mujahid, may Allah have mercy on him, said: People used to avoid menstruating women, but they used to come near them (i.e. have sexual intercourse). They asked the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, about this. Then Allah revealed this order: \People ask you about menstruation"
"1180","It is narrated about Taaws, Saeed, Mujahid, Ata, may Allah have mercy on him, that they strongly refused women to have sexual intercourse in the Siren (place of excrement), and said that it is disbelief."
"1181","Both Ata may Allah have mercy on him and Zuhri may Allah have mercy on him said: Janabat and menstruation have the same bath."
"1182","Sayyiduna Huzaifah (may Allah be pleased with him) said to his wife: Put water in your hair before the fire enters it. (Al-Baqiyyah and Al-Baqayya Min al-Baqiyyah)"
"1183","Jami bin Umayr, a member of Bani Taymullah bin Thaalba, said: I went with my mother and aunt to Sayyida Aisha, one of them asked her: How do you perform ghusl? He replied: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to perform the ablution of prayer at the time of Ghusl, then he would pour water on his head three times, and we pour water on our head five times because of dandruff."
"1184","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyidna Abu Huraira (RA) that he asked Sayyida A'isha (RA): A woman who takes a bath should she untie her hair? Answered: «Bakh» (Hit Teri) Will she spend an Oqiya? It is enough for him to pour water on his head three times."
"1185","Sayyidna Abdullah Ibn Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu said: She will comb her hair with her fingers."
"1186","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) about the (bathing) of a menstruating woman and a female woman, that she will pour water on both of her heads, and will not open her hair."
"1187","Ata, may God have mercy on him, also died in the same way."
"1188","On the authority of Mansoor, Imam Ibrahim Nakhai, may God have mercy on him, said: When the edges and roots of the roots are wet, they will not open them."
"1189","It has been narrated from Nafi (Moolay Ibn Umar) that the wives and maidservants of Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them, did not untie their braids when they performed Ghusl for menstruation and Janabat."
"1190","Sayyidah Umm Salama (may Allah be pleased with her) said: Women should not open their braids during menstruation or Janabat (ghusl)."
"1191","Sayyida Umm Salma (RA) the wife of the Prophet (PBUH) said that a woman came to the Prophet (PBUH) and asked, \How do I tie a braid on my head?\"" He said: \""Put three cups of water on your head"
"1192","Sayyidna Huzaifah (RA) said to his wife: Water the hair up to the roots, do not put fire in it. Mansoor said: Sayyiduna Hudhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him) meant Janabat (i.e. wash your hair thoroughly during Ghusl Janabat)."
"1193","The above-mentioned hadith has been narrated from Sayyiduna Hudhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him) in another chain of transmission (the above has been translated, it is added that if the water does not reach even a small place, he will be punished)."
"1194","Sayyiduna Jabir (RA) said: When a woman performs Ghusl Janabat, she will not untie her hair, but she will wash it by pouring water on the roots of her hair."
"1195","It is narrated from Ata, may God have mercy on him, that if a woman is on her side and her hair is knotted, will she untie it? He said: No, but pour water well on your head so that even the roots get watered."
"1196","Umrah bint Hayyan Sahmiyyah said: Umm al-Mu'minin Sayyidah Aisha (RA) said to me: Is there anyone among you who cannot afford to take the smoke of Qast after she is free from menstruation? If he can't afford it, \Aas\"""
"1197","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: When a woman takes a ghusl, she should put tayyab in place of the blood. (That is, put something fragrant there)."
"1198","Nafi narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Ibn Umar that his wives and maidservants did not open their hair when they were performing the ghusl of menstruation and janabat, but they used to exaggerate in shedding water. (so that the roots are well irrigated and water reaches them)."
"1199","It was narrated from Imam Ibrahim Nakhai, may God have mercy on him, that there is no problem in menstruating women taking something from the mosque."
"1200","Imam Ibrahim (may Allah have mercy on him) said: A menstruating woman can take anything from the mosque, but she will not enter."
"1201","Qatadah, may God have mercy on him, said: A Janbi can take (anything) from the mosque, but he cannot keep it."
"1202","On the authority of Ata, may God have mercy on him, about taking something from the mosque during menstruation, he said: She can take anything except the Mushaf."
"1203","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, said, \There is no journey to the south except for a traveler who is traveling.\"""""
"1204","Sayyiduna Anas Radiyallahu Anhu said: The above mentioned verse means that one should pass through the mosque in the state of Janabat, not sitting."
"1205","Abu Ubaidah said: A Junbi can pass through the mosque, but he will not sit in it. He read this verse in Istishahad:"
"1206","Salim and Saeed, may God have mercy on him, both said: He may pass, but he will not sit."
"1207","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) that we used to walk in the mosque in a state of janabat and did not see anything wrong with it."
"1208","On the authority of Ata, may God have mercy on her, regarding a menstruating woman hanging an amulet or a Qur'an (verse) around her neck, he said: If it is written on leather, the woman should remove it, and if it is in a silver shell, there is no problem. Imam Darmi (may Allah have mercy on him) was asked: Do you also say the same? He said: Yes."
"1209","Al-Mutar (Al-Waraq) narrated that I asked Hasan and Ata, may God have mercy on him, about a man who is accompanied by his wife on a journey and menstruates, then becomes pure, but does not get water. Both of them said: She will do tayammum and pray. Matar said: Can her husband make wati with her in this condition? He said: Prayer is greater than that. That is, when she can pray, she can also meet her husband."
"1210","It is narrated from Ata, may God have mercy on him, that a woman who is purified from menstruation and does not get water, said: When she performs tayammum, she can find a husband. Imam Darmi (may Allah have mercy on him) was asked: Do you have the same opinion? He said: O Allah."
"1211","It is narrated from Taaws, may God have mercy on him, that if a slave girl does not menstruate, her waiting period is forty-five (45) days."
"1212","Abu Qalaba, may God have mercy on him, said: Three months is its duration."
"1213","It was narrated from Imam Uza'i (may Allah have mercy on him) that I asked Imam Zahri (may Allah have mercy on him) that if a man buys a minor slave girl who has not menstruated and cannot get pregnant like her, how long will her waiting period be? He said: Three months."
"1214","Yahya bin Abi Kathir has stated that the period of Istbara Rahm of a slave girl is 45 days."
"1215","On the authority of Yahya bin Bishr, Ikramah, may God have mercy on him, said: (Its duration is) one month. Imam Darmi (may Allah have mercy on him) was asked: What is your opinion? He said: Three months is a strong preventive period and one month is sufficient."
"1216","On the authority of Sayyiduna Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said: \The example of the obligatory prayers is like a sweet river flowing at your door"
"1217","On the authority of Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, he heard the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: \If there is a canal at the door of a man in which he bathes five times a day"
"1218","Muhammad bin Hasan bin Ali said: We asked Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) during the time of the pilgrims who used to pray late. Sayyidna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray the Zuhr prayer when the sun was setting, and the Asr prayer when the sun was clear, and he prayed the Maghrib prayer when the sun set, and he prayed the Isha prayer sometimes early and sometimes late. If you did, you would pray late, and all of them (or he said) or the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray in the dark."
"1219","It was narrated from Ibn Shihab that Umar ibn Abdul Aziz, may God have mercy on him, was late in the (Asr) prayer one day, so Urwah ibn Zubair came to him and said: (Similarly) Mughirah ibn Shuba delayed his prayer one day. Don't you know that Gabriel (A.S.) came to the Messenger of Allah (S.A.W) and he prayed and the Messenger (S.A.W) also prayed. Then Gabriel (A.S.) prayed and he also prayed. Then Jibreel (peace be upon him) said that I have been given a similar order. Umar bin Abdul Aziz (may Allah have mercy on him) said: Urwa, you know what you are saying. Did Jibreel (peace be upon him) tell the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) the times of prayer? Arwa said: Bashir bin Abi Masoud used to say the same thing in the manner of his father. Urwa said: Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) used to offer the Asr prayer while the sun was still in his room, even before he climbed the wall."
"1220","Muhammad bin Ishaq said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came here (Imam Dari, may Allah have mercy on him) came to Madinah, at the time of prayer (people) used to gather without calling the Adhan, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intended to make a bugle (narsinga) of the Jews with which they (Jews) would call the people to prayer, but then he (peace be upon him) disapproved of it, then he ordered a bell to be carved so that it would be used by the Muslims. be played for the prayers, while Abdullah bin Zayd bin Abd Rabbah (who was the brother of Harith bin Lakhzraj) had a dream, so he came to the service of the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of Allah! Tonight while I was sleeping, a man passed by me wearing two green clothes and carrying a bell in his hand. I said: O servant of Allah, will you sell this bell? He said: What will you do to him? I said, I will call you for prayer through him, so he said, \Shall I tell you something good from him?\"" I said: What is that? He said: You say so. \""Allah Akbar"
"1221","Muhammad bin Abd Rabbah narrated from his father in the same way (the above hadith)."
"1222","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Zayd bin Abd Rabbah said: My father Abdullah bin Zayd said: When the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered the bell. And then narrated the aforementioned hadith."
"1223","Salim narrated on the authority of his father (Abdullah bin Umar) that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, \Bilaal gives the call to prayer at night"
"1224","It was narrated from Sayyida Aisha (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) had two muezzins, the sons of Bilal and Umm Maktoum, so the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \Bilal gives the call to prayer during the night"
"1225","It was narrated from Hafs bin Umar bin Sa'd Mu'zin that Sa'd used to give the call to prayer in the Prophet's Mosque. Hafs said: My family narrated to me that Bilal came to call the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, for the Fajr prayer. The people said: He, may God bless him and grant him peace, is sleeping. Bilal said loudly: \Al-Salaat Khair min al-Nawm\"" \""Prayer is better than sleep\"""
"1226","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said that during the time of the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him), the words of the call to prayer were said twice and the words of Iqamah (the words of Iqamah) were said once."
"1227","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Anas that Bilal was ordered to say the words of Adhan twice and once in Iqamah."
"1228","Sayyiduna Anas (RA) said: Bilal was ordered to say the words of Adhan twice and the words of Iqamah once."
"1229","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated it in the same way."
"1230","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Mahzourah that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, asked about twenty men to call for the Adhan, so they gave the Adhan, but he liked the voice of Abu Mahzourah, and he taught them the Adhan. \Allah is great"
"1231","Abu Mahzoora narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught him 19 words of Adhan and 17 words of Iqamah."
"1232","It is narrated from Abu Juhaifa that he saw Sayyiduna Bilal giving the call to prayer and said: I also turned my face to and fro in the call to prayer with his face."
"1233","It was narrated from Abu Juhaifa that Bilal carried his stick, then gave the call to prayer, and put his fingers in both his ears. Imam Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: (The above) hadith of Sufyan Thauri is more correct."
"1234","Sayyidna Sahl bin Sa'd (RA) reported that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \Two (times) of supplication are not rejected or less rejected. One is the supplication at the time of the call to prayer"
"1235","It was narrated from Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \When you hear the voice of the muezzin"
"1236","Isa bin Talha said: We came to the service of Sayyiduna Mu'awiyah, and the muezzin gave the call to prayer and said: \Allah Akbar"
"1237","Muhammad bin Amr from his father, he narrated from his grandfather that Sayyiduna Muawiyah (RA) heard the muezzin saying: “Allah is great, Allah is great.” So he said: “Allah is great, Allah is great.” Messenger of God, I testify that Muhammad is the Messenger of God, so he also said in response: \I testify that Muhammad is the Messenger of God"
"1238","On the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When the call to prayer is given, Satan farts and runs away so that he cannot hear the call to prayer. She did not come. Imam al-Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: In this hadith, the word \reward\"" means: \""Aqeem\"""
"1239","Sayyidina Abu Huraira (RA) saw a man leaving the mosque after the Adhan and said: He has disobeyed Abu Qasim (PBUH)."
"1240","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (RA) reported that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) used to come outside and lead them in the Zuhr prayer when the sun had set."
"1241","On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When the heat becomes intense"
"1242","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Anas that after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had offered the Asr prayer, the traveler would go to the upper part of Madinah, and even after reaching there, the sun would still be high."
"1243","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Salama bin Akwa, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray Maghrib at sunset, when the upper edge of the sun had set."
"1244","On the authority of Sayyiduna Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \My Ummah will remain in good health until it waits for the stars to become thick in the west.\"""""
"1245","It was narrated from Sayyidna Nu'man bin Basheer (may Allah be pleased with him) that I am more knowledgeable about the time of this prayer than anyone else. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray (Isha) when the moon sets on the third night. Yahya said: Imam Darmi, may God have mercy on him, dictated this tradition from his book in the manner of Bashir bin Thabit."
"1246","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that one night the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, delayed the Isha prayer so much that almost a third of the night had passed, then he came while the worshipers were sitting in groups and circles dozing off. going, I made up my mind to ask a person to lead the prayer, then I would go to the houses of those who stayed behind from the prayer (congregation), and set fire to their houses.\""
1247"""
"1247","(Marfu' Hadith) Nasr ibn 'Ali informed us, 'Abd al-A'la narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from 'Urwah, from 'A'ishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) delayed the 'Isha' prayer until 'Umar ibn al-Khattab called out to him: ""The women and children have slept."" So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came out and said: ""There is no one on the face of the earth praying this prayer except you."" And no one prayed that day except the people of Medina."
"1248","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delayed one night (the Isha prayer) until a large part of the night had passed, and those who were in the mosque were asleep, then he came out and said: \If he had not thought of putting hardship on his Ummah"
"1249","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, delayed the Isha prayer one night. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, the women and children have slept, so he came outside and water was dripping from his side."
"1250","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: The wives of the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) used to offer the Fajr prayer with the Prophet (may peace be upon him), then return wrapped in their cloaks before they were recognized."
"1251","Sayyidna Rafi' bin Khadij (RA) narrated that the Prophet (PBUH) said: \Pray the Fajr prayer in the morning"
"1252","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Rafi bin Khadij, may Allah be pleased with him, that perform the Fajr prayer in the light, this is the reason for the great reward."
"1253","It is narrated in the same way by Ibn Ajlan. Also it has a marvi with «asfarwa»."
"1254","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \Whoever completes one rak'ah of a prayer has completed the prayer (Ba Jama'at).\"""""
"1255","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated the same thing in another way."
"1256","On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Whoever prays one rak'ah of Fajr before sunrise"
"1257","Sayyidina Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \When you see a man who is in the habit of coming and going to the mosque"
"1258","Sayyiduna Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Whoever prays the Isha prayer in congregation will have the reward of staying half the night"
"1259","Abu Bakr Shaibani says: The owner of this house narrated the hadith to me. And he pointed to the house of Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) that he (sayyedna Ibn Masoud may Allah be pleased with him) inquired from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, what is the best or most beloved deed in the sight of Allah? He said: To perform the prayer at its (first) time."
"1260","Sayyiduna Ka'b bin Ajra (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) came to us in the mosque. We were seven people, three Arabs and four Mawwalis (slaves), or four Arabs and three Mawwalis. The Prophet (PBUH) came from the room and sat with us. The narrator said: He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bowed his head to the ground for a while, then raised his blessed head and said: \Do you know what your Lord says?\"" We said: Only Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: \""Allah Almighty says: Whoever prays the prayer at its (first) time and performs its conditions and parts correctly"
"1261","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Dharr that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: \What will you do when you are left among people who pray late?\"" He said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: \""Perform the prayer at its time and (if necessary) leave the mosque"
"1262","Sayyiduna Abu Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \O Abu Dharr! What will you do when there will be leaders above you who will offer the prayer at the last time?\"" Asked: What do you command me? He said: \""You should perform the prayer at its (first) time"
"1263","On the authority of Sayyiduna Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \If a person forgets a prayer or falls asleep"
"1264","Salim narrated on the authority of his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him) that: Whoever misses the Asr prayer, it is as if his family and property have all been lost."
"1265","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: Whoever misses the Asr prayer, it is as if his family and children have been killed (or robbed). Imam al-Darmi, may Allah have mercy on him, said: \O malah\"" means \""wealth\"" instead of children."""
"1266","On the authority of Sayyiduna Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said on the Day of the Trench: \May Allah fill the graves of these polytheists and their houses with fire"
"1267","Sayyiduna Jabir Radiyallahu Anhu said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \There is nothing between a servant and shirk or disbelief except leaving the prayer.\"" Imam al-Darmi"
"1268","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar that the people were performing the Fajr prayer in the Kaaba when a companion came to them and said that the Qur'an was revealed to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he was ordered to turn his face towards the Kaaba."
"1269","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) said: It was asked: O Messenger of Allah, what is your opinion about those people who died while praying towards Bayt al-Maqdis? So Allah Ta'ala revealed this honorable verse: \Allah Ta'ala will not lose your faith.\"" [Baqarah: 143/2]"""
"1270","Sayyida Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to start the prayer with Takbeer, and he used to start with the recitation of Al-Hamdu Lillah Rabbi al-Alameen, and he used to end the prayer with taslim."
"1271","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to perform the Rifi'idin whenever he stood up for prayer."
"1272","Sayyiduna Ali bin Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, said that when the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say Takbeer and then recite this supplication: \Inni wajahtu... wa atubu ilaik\"" i.e. I turned my face towards the one who created the earth and the sky"
"1273","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, that when the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, would stand up at night, he would recite \Subhaanka Allahhum ........... Nafsha Wa Nafha\"" after Takbeer"
"1274","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH), Abu Bakr, Umar and Uthman (RA) used to start their prayers with the recitation of \Alhamdulillah"
"1275","Sayyiduna Wail bin Hajar (RA) said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) placing his right hand over his left hand on the joint (the joint of the wrist)."
"1276","It was narrated from Sayyidna Ubada bin Samit (RA) that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \He who does not recite Umm Al-Qur'an (Fatiha) has no prayer at all.\"""""
"1277","Sayyidna Samra bin Jundab (RA) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) used to remain silent (in prayer) in two places: when he entered the prayer (i.e. at the time of the opening prayer), and the second Sukta when he was free from recitation (i.e. before bowing). has said correctly. Imam al-Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: Qatadah, may God have mercy on him, used to say the Sukta three times (i.e., after the Takbeer Tahrimah, then after the Fatiha, then before bowing at the end of the Qur'at). (It is also the same in Safar al-Saadat, so that after Surah Fatiha, Muqtadi should recite Surah Fatiha during the cant)."
"1278","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) used to be silent for a while between Takbeer (Tahreema) and recitation. Abu Zariyah said: I understand that Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) said \Haniyah\"" along with \""Iskatah\"". I (Sayyidna Abu Hurairah"
"1279","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When the reciter says"
"1280","On the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Huraira, may God bless him and grant him peace, the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When the Imam recites \""Ghair-e-al-Maghzoob-Alihim-Wala-Dha-Daliin\"" then say Amen"
"1281","Sayyiduna Wail bin Hajar, may God be pleased with him, said: When the Messenger of God, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, recited \Walaa Al-Dhaaleen\"""
"1282","It was narrated from Abu Bakr bin Abdul Rahman and Abu Salama that they prayed behind Sayyiduna Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with them, and when they bowed, they said, “Allah Akbar.” When they raised their heads from bowing, they said, “Same Allah, Praise be to God.” Then they said, “Rabbi, praise be to you.” By the One in Whose possession is my soul, I am the most like you in prayer to the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace. His prayer was like that until he left this world."
"1283","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) saying \Allah Akbar\"" every time he stood up"
"1284","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that when the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, would say “Allah Akbar” and raise both his hands up to his shoulders (i.e. make the prostration), and when he bowed, he would say Takbeer and make the bow, and when he raised his head from the bow, he would make the same way, and he would not make the bow in between prostrations or prostrations."
"1285","Malik bin Al-Hawairth narrated that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said Takbeer Tahrehimah, he would raise his hands up to his ears, and similarly, while going into Ruku, and when he raised his head from Ruku, he would perform Rif Yadeen."
"1286","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Wail Hazrami (RA) that he prayed with the Messenger of Allah (PBUH), when he bowed down and when he stood up, he would say Takbeer, and he would raise both his hands during Takbeer, and turn the salutation to the right and left. Said: Yes."
"1287","It was narrated from Sayyidna Malik bin Huwayrth, may Allah be pleased with him, that I attended the service of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, along with some people from my people (Bani Layth). We were all young and we stayed with him for twenty days. Recite as you have seen me praying. When the time for prayer comes, let one of you give the Adhan for you, then the eldest among you should lead you.\""
1288"""
"1288","(Marfu' Hadith) 'Affan informed us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""When three gather, let one of them lead them, and the most worthy of them to lead is the one who recites (Qur'an) the most."""
"1289","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) said: I was with my aunt (Sahiba) Sayyida Maimunah (RA) when the Prophet (PBUH) came after Isha and he prayed four rak'ahs, then he stood up and said: Did Batwa fall asleep? or said a similar word, then stood up and began to pray, so I went and joined him on his left side."
"1290","It was narrated from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, was riding a horse, and he fell from it, and his right side was injured. When he prays, you also pray standing, when he bows, you also bow, and when he says, \Same Allah"
"1291","Abdullah bin Abdullah (bin Utbah) said: I attended the service of Sayyida Aisha (RA) and asked her: Will you not tell me about the condition of the Messenger of Allah (PBUH)'s illness? He said: Of course, (listen) the illness of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) increased, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) inquired: \Have the people prayed?\"" We said: No"
"1292","Sayyidna Sahl bin Sa'd (RA) said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) sitting on the pulpit, then he said Takbeer-e-Tahreema, and the people also said Takbeer, then he bowed on the pulpit, then he raised his head from bowing, then in the same position he moved back with his feet upside down and prostrated under the pulpit, then climbed up and completed the prayer in the same way. Imam Abu Muhammad Darami, may God have mercy on him, said: In this regard, the Imam is allowed to lead the prayer by standing higher than the worshipers and he can perform this much in the prayer."
"1293","Sayyidna Abu Mas'ud Ansari (RA) said: A man came to the Prophet (PBUH) and said: O Messenger of Allah! By Allah, I lie down in the Fajr prayer because of the long prayer of such and such a person. The narrator said: I have never seen the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in such intense anger and rage in preaching and exhortation than that day. There will be a weak and needy person."
"1294","Sayyidna Qatadah (RA) said: I heard Sayyidna Anas (RA) saying: The Prophet (PBUH) used to lead a very light, light and perfect prayer."
"1295","Abdullah bin Abi Qatadah narrated from his father that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When Iqamah is called for prayer"
"1296","Sayyiduna Abu Qatada (RA) narrated that the Prophet (PBUH) said: \When Iqamah is said"
"1297","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Keep your ranks equal"
"1298","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyidina Bara bin Azib that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Keep your ranks equal so that there is no difference in your hearts.\"""""
"1299","It was narrated from Sayyidna Arbaad bin Saariyyah that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray for forgiveness three times for those in the first row and once for those in the second row."
"1300","Sayyidna Arbaad bin Sariyyah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the same way (from another chain of transmission)."
"1301","Sayyidna Abu Mas'ud Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) would put his hands on our shoulders and say: Do not stand back and forth lest your hearts become divided (i.e., there will be a split in your hearts). Next to me stand the wise and prudent among you, then those who are close to them, then those who are close to them."
"1302","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: \Let wise and understanding people stand near me"
"1303","On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \The best row among the rows of men is the first row"
"1304","Sayyiduna Abi bin Ka'b, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, offered the Fajr prayer, then he turned towards us and said: \Is such and such a person present?\"" The Companions said: No"
"1305","Sayyidna Abi bin Ka'b (RA) narrated a similar narration from the Prophet (PBUH)."
"1306","Sayyidna Abi bin Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated a similar narration from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) (in another way)."
"1307","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (SAW) said: \No prayer is heavier on the hypocrites than Isha and Fajr"
"1308","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “I had decided to order my men to collect firewood, then to order a man to lead the prayer, then I would go to those who were lagging behind (not attending) this prayer and burn them along with their houses. If they know the reward and virtue of these prayers, they will walk (on their knees)."
"1309","It was narrated from Nafi, may God have mercy on him, that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, encamped at the place of \Zajnan\"" on a cold night"
"1310","Dawood bin Abi Hind said: I asked Saeed bin Al-Musayb, may God have mercy on him, that a man prayed in his house, then found the Imam praying, so should he pray with that Imam? Saeed bin Al-Museeb, may God have mercy on him, said: Yes, pray. I said: Then which of these two prayers will be considered (obligatory)? Ibn Al-Musayyib, may God have mercy on him, said: The one who prayed with the Imam, Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (RA) narrated to us that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \A man's prayer with a congregation is more than twenty times better than his prayer alone.\"""""
"1311","On the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \A man's prayer in congregation is twenty-seven times greater than praying alone.\"""""
"1312","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \When the wife of one of you asks for permission to go to the mosque"
"1313","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) said: \Do not prevent the handmaids of Allah from the mosques"
"1314","Saeed bin Aamir said: «Al-Tafalah» (means) something that has a fragrance."
"1315","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \If the evening meal is placed in front of you and it is (also) time for prayer"
"1316","On the authority of Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When the evening meal is in front of you and Iqamah is called"
"1317","On the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When you come for prayer"
"1318","Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \When you come for prayer"
"1319","Sayyiduna Abi bin Ka'b, may Allah be pleased with him, said: In my knowledge, among the people of Madinah, none of the people who prayed had their house so far from the Masjid (of the Prophet), (in spite of this) he used to attend all the prayers with the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace (i.e., no prayer was interrupted by the congregation). I absolutely do not like that my house is attached to the Masjid (of the Prophet), when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was informed about this, he asked this person about it, and he said: O Messenger of Allah (I said this because) so that in my book of deeds my footsteps and my return to my family and my comings and goings will be written (and I will be rewarded for it), or saying similar words, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Accordingly, He granted you all this. (or said a similar phrase)."
"1320","Hilal bin Yasaf said: Ziyad bin Abi al-Jaad took me by the hand and made me stand next to a sheikh of Banu Asad who was called Wabsa bin Mabad, then he said that he narrated the hadith from me and that shakh (Wabsa) was listening that the Messenger of God saw a man who prayed behind him (alone) and did not join the row, the Messenger of God ordered him to return the prayer. Imam al-Darmi (may Allah have mercy on him) said: Imam Ahmad bin Hanbal (may Allah have mercy on him) called the hadith of Amr bin Marra more authentic, and according to me, the hadith of Yazid bin Ziyad bin Abi al-Jaad is more authentic (the meaning of both hadiths is the same)."
"1321","It was narrated on the authority of Wabsa bin Mabad that a man prayed alone behind the rows, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to return (i.e. pray again), Imam Abu Muhammad, may God have mercy on him, said: This is what I say."
"1322","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrated that his grandmother Malikah prepared food and invited the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) to eat. He (PBUH) ate the food and then said: \Let me teach you the prayer.\"" Sayyidna Anas (RA) said: I picked up a sack of mine which had become black from frequent use. (Zamir ) formed a row behind him"
"1323","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Saeed al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to stand for thirty verses in the first two rak'ats of Zuhr, and half of that in the last two rak'ats, and in the first two rak'ats of Asr, he used to stand equal to the last rak'ats of Zuhr and half of that in the last two rak'ats of Asr."
"1324","In this way, it is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Saeed al-Khudri (may God be pleased with him) that he (peace and blessings of God be upon him) used to recite after Surah Al-Sajda."
"1325","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir bin Samrah (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) used to recite \Wal-Samaa-Wal-Tareq\"" and \""Wal-Samaa-Zat-Al-Brooj\"" in the Zuhr and Asr prayers."""
"1326","It was narrated from Sayyidina Abu Qatadah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite Surah Fatiha and two surahs in the first two rakats of Zuhr and Asr prayers (i.e. Surah Fatiha and one Surah Kuma in al-Bukhari in each rakat) and sometimes he used to recite the verse to us and recited the long recitation in the first rakat."
"1327","Abu Asim (Dahhak bin Makhalid) reported, from Uza'i, he narrated the same from Yahya on his authority."
"1328","Abdullah bin Abu Qatada narrated that his father (Sayyidna Abu Qatada, may God be pleased with him) narrated to him that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite Surah Fatiha and two surahs in the first two rakats of Dhuhr, and in the last two rakats he would recite only Surat Fatiha, and sometimes he would recite the verse to us, and he would make the first rakat long, and not make the second rakat so long, similarly in the Asr prayer and in the same way in the Fajr prayer."
"1329","Sayyida Umm al-Fazl (RA) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) reciting Surah Mursalat in Maghrib prayer."
"1330","Hamad bin Jubayr bin Mut'am narrated from his father that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reciting Surah Wal-Toor in Maghrib prayer."
"1331","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) that Sayyidna Muadh (may Allah be pleased with him) used to pray with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he would return and lead his people (tribes) in prayer. One night he came and recited Surah Al-Baqarah in the Isha prayer. So he complained to the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Mu'adh: \You are the cause of fitnah"
"1332","Ziyad bin Al-Ulaqa said: I heard from my uncle, he used to say that I prayed Fajr with the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he recited “﴿Wal-Nakhl-Basiqat﴾” [Q:10] in one rakat."
"1333","Sayyiduna Qutb bin Malik (RA) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) reciting \Wal-Nakhl-Basiqat-La-Ha-Tal-A-Nazid\"" in the first rak'ah of the Fajr prayer [Q: 10/50]."""
"1334","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Amr bin Harith (may God be pleased with him) that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reciting “Idha al-Shams Qur’at” in the Fajr prayer. What is the meaning of ``as''? (When the night falls)."
"1335","Abu Na'im reported that Mas'ar narrated a hadith from us on the authority of Waleed and he narrated the same on the authority of Sayyiduna Amr bin Harith (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"1336","Siyar bin Salama said: I came with my father to the service of Sayyidna Abu Barza Aslami, who was in a bamboo hut. My father asked him about the prayer times of the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace. Sayyidna Abu Barza, may God bless him and grant him peace, said that he, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray the ``hajir'', which you call Zuhr, at the time of sunset, and when he had finished the Asr prayer, one of us would return to his home on the far side of Madinah. When he went, the sun was still strong. Siyar said: I do not remember what he said about Maghrib, and he liked to delay the Isha prayer, which you call ``Utma'', and he used to finish the morning prayer when a man could recognize the person sitting near him, and you used to recite sixty to a hundred verses in that (morning prayer)."
"1337","Sayyidna Jabir bin Samrah (RA) said: The Prophet (PBUH) entered the mosque, saw the people raising their eyes to the sky in prayer, and said: \Avoid it"
"1338","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \What is wrong with those who raise their eyes to the sky in prayer?\"" He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stopped them very sternly until the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: \""You must desist from this action"
"1339","Mus'ab bin Sa'd narrated that Banu Abdullah bin Mas'ud used to place his hands between his thighs when he bowed, so I prayed next to Sa'd (bin Abi Waqqas), so I did the same, but he hit my hand. When he finished the prayer, he said: We used to place our hands in the same way (joined between the thighs), we were ordered to place our palms on our knees."
"1340","Muhammad bin Yusuf reported that Israel narrated from Abu Ishaq, he narrated from Musab in the same way."
"1341","Sayyiduna Abu Mas'ud Ansari (RA) said: Shall I lead you in prayer like the Messenger of Allah (PBUH)? (Salam al-Barad) said: So they said the Takbeer, bowed and placed their two hands (palms) on their two knees, and kept their fingers open until each joint became straight."
"1342","Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Aamir, may God be pleased with him, says that when this verse \Glory be to the name of your Lord the Most High\"" was revealed"
"1343","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Huzaifah that he prayed one night with the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He used to say \Sajjan Rabi al-Azeem\"" in bowing and \""Subhaan Rabi al-Ali\"" in prostration."""
"1344","It was narrated from Abbas bin Sahl that Muhammad bin Muslimah, Abu Asid, Abu Hameed and Sahl bin Saad were together and the prayer of the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, was mentioned. He used to place his palms on both knees, as if the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was holding them, and kept his elbows apart from his sides, and (in bowing) he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would neither bow down nor raise his head."
"1345","Salim, narrating from his father (Sayyidna Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him), said that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) started the prayer, he would raise his hands to his shoulders, then when he bowed, he would raise his hands in the same way, then when he raised his head from bowing, he would raise his hands in the same way and say: They used to say \Wallak Al-Hamdu\"""
"1346","Al-Zuhri narrated a similar hadith from Salem on the authority of Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may God be pleased with him) and only said “Rabbi walik al-Hamdu” (i.e. did not say “Allahum Rabbna”)."
"1347","On the authority of Sayyiduna Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When the Imam says"
"1348","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: “Indeed, the Imam is so that you follow his example, when he says “Allah Akbar” then you say “Allah Akbar” after him, when he goes into Ruku, you also bow, and when he goes into Sajdah, you also prostrate, and when he (Imam) says “Sami’ Allah limn Hamidahu”. If he says, then you should say: \Allah"
"1349","Sayyidina Abu Musa al-Ash'ari (RA) said that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) gave a sermon and taught us our prayer and taught us our Sunnah. (The narrator) said: I think that he (PBUH) said: \When Iqamah is said for prayer"
"1350","Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, said: When the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, would raise his head from bowing, he used to say: “Rabbanna lak al-hamdu ...... mink al-jad” meaning: “O our Lord, all praises belong to You throughout the heavens and the earth, and after that, as much praise as You want, You are worthy of praise and praise, better is what the servant said and we all belong to You.” Servants, O Allah, there is no one withholding what You give, and no one gives to what You do not give, and before You, the wealth (or position) will not benefit the possessor (saheb mansab)."
"1351","Sayyiduna Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would raise his head from bowing, he would say: \Hear Allah's praise"
"1352","On the authority of Sayyiduna Muawiya, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \My body has become heavy"
"1353","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Does anyone among you who raises his head (in ruku' or prostration) before the Imam"
"1354","It was narrated from Anas bin Malik (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) encouraged the people to pray, and forbade them to compete when they bow and prostrate before him, and forbade them to greet him before him, and he said: \I see you from all sides behind me and in front of me.\"""""
"1355","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Your Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) was ordered to prostrate on seven limbs, and not to wrap his hair or clothes. Shu'ba said: And once Amr bin Dinar narrated this hadith to me like this: The Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \I have been ordered to prostrate on seven limbs and that (in prostration) I should neither wrap my hair nor my clothes.\"""""
"1356","On the authority of Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \I have been ordered to prostrate on seven limbs"
"1357","Sayyiduna Wail bin Hajar (RA) said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (PBUH), when he went into Sajdah, he would place his knees before his hands (on the ground) and when he stood up (for the second Rak'at), he would raise his hands before his knees."
"1358","On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said: \When one of you prays"
"1359","Qatadah, may God have mercy on him, said: I heard Sayyidna Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, saying that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Keep moderation in prostration and do not spread your hands like a dog.\"""""
"1360","Sayyiduna Abd al-Rahman bin Shibul Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade spreading the arms (in prostration) like beasts, and hooting like a crow (i.e. prostrating hastily), and setting a place in the mosque as a camel sets (its place)."
"1361","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Hudhayfah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say “Rabbi Aghafirli” between the two prostrations. Imam Darmi (may Allah have mercy on him) was asked: Do you also say the same? Said: Sometimes I say it, sometimes I keep silent."
"1362","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, said: (In his illness) the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, raised the veil, and the people were lined up behind Sayyidna Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: \People! There is nothing left of the good news of prophethood except a good and good dream that a Muslim sees"
"1363","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \I have been forbidden to recite Qur'aat while bowing and prostrating"
"1364","Sayyidina Abu Mas'ud Radiyallahu Anhu said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \A man's prayer is not correct unless he keeps his back straight in Ruku' and Sajjud.\"""""
"1365","Sayyidina Abu Qatadah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \The worst of people in terms of theft is the person who steals during his prayer.\"" It was said: O Messenger of Allah! How can one steal prayer? He said: \""Do not perform Ruku' and Sajdah fully (correctly).\"""""
"1366","On the authority of Sayyidna Rafa’ah and Malik, who were both sons of Rafa’ and from the people of Badr, they said: “We were sitting next to the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, or he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sitting and we were around him.” The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) responded to him and said: \Go pray again"
"1367","Umm al-Mu'minin Sayyidah Maimunah bint Harith (may Allah be pleased with her) said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated, he would keep his hands apart from his sides until the person behind him could see the whiteness of his armpits."
"1368","Sayyida Maimunah (may Allah be pleased with her) said that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would prostrate, he would keep his arms away from his side, so far that a kid could pass under (the baths). (That is, the baths should be kept so spacious that a baby goat can come out from under them)."
"1369","Sayyida Maimunah, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: When the Messenger of God, peace and blessings of God be upon him, would prostrate, he would keep both hands open (separated from the sides) so that the whiteness of his hair would show from behind, and when he sat down, he would rest them on his left thigh."
"1370","Bara bin Azib (may Allah be pleased with him) stated that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bowed, the interval between his bowing and his raising his head from bowing, and the interval between his prostration and the two prostrations were almost equal."
"1371","Sayyiduna Bara bin Azib (RA) said: I considered the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (PBUH), and I found his standing up from bowing, then standing straight from bowing, then his prostration, and sitting between the two prostrations, then his prostration, and the assembly between salam and insaraf were almost equally excellent. Abu Muhammad (Imam al-Darmi), may God have mercy on him, said: Bilal bin Hameed, in my opinion, is Abu Hameed al-Wazan."
"1372","Sayyidna Mughira bin Shuba (may God be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of God (may God bless him and grant him peace) came and Sayyidna Mughira (may God be pleased with him) was also with him. He saw that the people had started the Fajr prayer, and had put Sayyidna Abdur Rahman bin Awf (radiy-Allahu anhu) forward to lead the prayer. It was done, when Sayyiduna Abd al-Rahman (RA) greeted the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) when he stood up and finished the prayer, the people were frightened, Subhan Allah Subhan Allah."
"1373","Sayyiduna Al-Mughira (RA) said: When we reached the people, they had already finished the prayer, and Sayyidna Abd al-Rahman bin Awf (RA) was leading them in the Fajr prayer and had gone into ruku, and when they felt the arrival of the Prophet (PBUH), they started to move back. The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) gestured with his blessed hand. (The first) Rak'at was missed, so we recited it. Abu Muhammad Imam Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: According to the fatwa, I am convinced of the opinion of the people of Kufa that the missed rak'ah should be made up, that is, the qadha will be accepted, and the next rak'ah of the imam will be the second one."
"1374","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: We used to pray with the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) in intense heat, and when one of us could not keep his forehead on the ground, he would spread his cloth and pray on it."
"1375","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying (at the time of tashahhud) in this way (pointing), Ibn Ayaina pointed with his finger and Abu Waleed (reported) pointed with his index finger."
"1376","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to sit down at the end of the prayer (for tashahhud), placing his left hand on his left knee and his right hand on his right knee and pointing his finger."
"1377","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) said: When we used to pray behind the Messenger of Allah (Peace be upon him), he would say: Peace be upon Allah before His servants, Peace be upon Gabriel and Michael, Peace be upon Israfel, Peace be upon so-and-so, Sayyiduna Ibn Masoud (RA) said: Then the Messenger of Allah (Peace be upon him) turned to us and said: “Peace be upon Allah Himself (what do you greet upon Him) when you are sitting in prayer (for witnessing)? Go and say: \Al Tahiyat llah ..........."""
"1378","Qasim bin Mukhaimarah narrated that Alqamah held my hand and narrated to me the hadith that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) held his hand and said that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) held Abdullah’s hand and taught him to recite tashahhud in prayer and “(Al-Tahiyyat-ul-Lillah-Wal-Salawat-Wal-Tayyibaat............. Al-Saalihiin)\ Zuhair said: I think he remembered until \""I testify that there is no god but Allah and I testify that Muhammad is his servant and messenger\"". Then he said: When you have done or said this"
"1379","Ibn Abi Laila says: I met Sayyidna Ka'b bin Ajra, may Allah be pleased with him, and he said: Shall I not give you a gift? When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us, we said: We have learned the way to greet you, how should we greet you? He said: Say: \O Allah! Have mercy on Muhammad and the family of Muhammad in the same way that You had mercy on Abraham. Indeed"
"1380","Naeem Mujmar narrated from the freed slave of Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, that Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Zayd Ansari, who had a dream of giving the call to prayer during the time of the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, (the dream was seen by his father Abdullah, who died as a Muslim). Ibn Sa'd asked him, who is Abu Numan bin Bashir: O Messenger of Allah! Allah Ta'ala has ordered us to pray, how should we pray for you? He said: \Say like this: \""O Allah"
"1381","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) says: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \When one of you finishes martyrdom"
"1382","The same is true of Uzai."
"1383","Sayyidna Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas, may Allah be pleased with him, said: When the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, would greet him to his right, the whiteness of his face would be visible."
"1384","Abu Mu'mar said: I prayed behind a man in Makkah and he greeted both sides. And the ruling said: The Holy Prophet (PBUH) used to do the same."
"1385","Sayyida Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, said: The Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to sit as long as he said: \O Allah"
"1386","Sayyiduna Thawban, may Allah be pleased with him, said: When the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, would finish the prayer, he would say \Astagfir-Allah\"" three times"
"1387","Warid, the scribe of Sayyidna Mughira bin Shuba, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Sayyidna Mughira bin Shuba, may Allah be pleased with him, wrote a letter to me for Sayyidna Muawiya, may God bless him and grant him peace, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited this dua after every obligatory prayer. \There is none worthy of worship except Allah"
"1388","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) said that no one should make any part of Satan in his prayer in such a way that he considers it necessary for him to turn from the right side."
"1389","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turning from his right side."
"1390","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) walked on his right side after the prayer."
"1391","On the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA): Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (RA) said: O Messenger of Allah! The rich people have taken away all the rewards and rewards, they pray as we pray, and they fast as we fast, they give charity with their remaining wealth and we have nothing to give charity to. The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Shall I not tell you such a deed that if you follow it"
"1392","Sayyiduna Zayd bin Thabit, may God be pleased with him, said: We were ordered to say \Subhaan Allah\"" 33 times"
"1393","Sayyiduna Tamim Dari, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \(On the Day of Resurrection) the first thing that will be taken into account from a servant is his prayer"
"1394","Sayyidna Abu Hameed Sa'idi (RA) said that those who were with ten companions of the Messenger of Allah (PBUH), among them was Sayyidna Abu Qatadah (RA). Sayyiduna Abu Hameed (may Allah be pleased with him) said: You are the most knowledgeable about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him). He said: Why so? Aren't you a follower of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) more than us and one who lives with him more than us? He said: Yes, it is so. He said: Then present it? Sayyidina Abu Hameed (may Allah be pleased with him) said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood for prayer, he would raise his hands to his shoulders, then say Allahu Akbar until all the joints were straight, then he would recite, then say Allahu Akbar and raise both hands to his shoulders, then he would bow down and place his two palms on both of his knees until each bone returned to its original position, and (in bowing) he would neither raise his head nor bend his back (equal to the back). ), then raising his head (from bowing) he would say \Sami'Allah Liman Hamda\"" and raise his hands up to his shoulders. Abu Asim says: I think that even at that time he said: (Standing up from bowing) until every bone (joint) was in its place (original position)"
"1395","Sayyiduna Wail bin Hajar (RA) said: I decided in my heart that I will definitely see the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) and see how he prays. So I saw you: standing, saying Allahu Akbar, and raising both your hands up to your ears (i.e. doing rifa yadin), and placing your right hand on top of your left paw. Place the left foot (step) and place your left hand on the left thigh and left knee and place the right elbow on the right thigh, then bend the two fingers (i.e. thumb and middle finger) to form a circle and keep the index finger upright. I saw you moving it as if praying with gestures. Sayyiduna Wail (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Then I came after a long time in the winter and saw people (dressed) in cloaks and moving their hands inside the cloaks (for making ablution)."
"1396","Hattan bin Abdullah al-Raqashi said: Sayyidna Abu Musa al-Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him) led us one of the two Isha prayers (i.e. Maghrib or Isha), then a man from the congregation said: The prayer is obligatory along with good deeds and zakat. All the people remained silent, then Sayyidna Abu Musa said: O Hattan! Perhaps you have said this? I said: No, I did not say this (prayer is obligatory with good deeds), and how should I say it. I was afraid that you (will reprimand me) would be angry with me. A man said: I said this word and my intention was good. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave a sermon and taught us the prayer and explained his Sunnah. The narrator said: I think he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “When the prayer is established, one of you should lead the imam, then when the imam says “Allah Akbar” you should also say “Allah Akbar”, and when he says “Ghir Al-Mughdub Alaihi wa Al-Dhaalin” then say Amen, Allah will accept it. He will go into Ruku and you will go into Ruku after following the Imam and raise your head from Ruku, Imam will raise his head before you. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Your doing this is in accordance with the imam's bowing"
"1397","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to come out for prayer and carry Imama bint Zainab (his granddaughter) on his neck or shoulder."
"1398","Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah Ansari (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) carried Imama bint Zainab in prayer."
"1399","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated on the authority of Sayyidna Suhayb (may Allah be pleased with him) that he (Sahayb) passed by the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) and greeted him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying."
"1400","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to the mosque of Bani Awf bin Amr (which is in the Quba), he (may God bless him and grant him peace) began to pray, and people also filled the mosque. He said with hand gestures: He used to answer like this."
"1401","On the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \For men there is glorification and for women there is praise.\"""""
"1402","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyidna Sahl bin Saad that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When something happens to you in prayer (you forget it)"
"1403","From this chain of transmission, Sayyiduna Sahl bin Saad (RA) has narrated a similar hadith from the Prophet (PBUH)."
"1404","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyidna Zaid bin Thabit (RA) that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \Make it obligatory to pray in your homes because the best prayer for a person is to pray in the house in congregation.\"""""
"1405","Jabir bin Yazid bin Aswad narrates from his father (Sayyidna Yazid, may Allah be pleased with him) that he prayed Fajr with the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Sayyidina Yazid (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (SAW) called them, and they were brought while they were trembling. He (SAW) said: \What prevented you from praying?\"" Both of them said: We had prayed at our places. He said: \""Do not sit like that in the future. When you pray at home"
"1406","It was narrated from Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) saw a man praying alone and said: \Is there no man who can give charity to him and pray with him?\"""""
"1407","On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, a man entered the mosque and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, had already gathered. Imam al-Darmi (may Allah have mercy on him) said: He can offer the Asr prayer, but if he offers the Maghrib prayer again, he should offer four rak'ats."
"1408","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyidina Abu Huraira that a man said: O Messenger of Allah! Can a man pray in a cloth? He said: \Does each of you get two clothes or each of you has two clothes.\"""""
"1409","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \No one should pray in a single garment without any of it on his shoulders.\"""""
"1410","It was narrated from Sayyidina Abu Huraira that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade two types of clothing: One is that a person sits with his knees wrapped in a cloth in such a way that there is no veil between his private parts and the sky, and the other is the Ishtamal Sama, which is worn by the Jews."
"1411","It was narrated from Umm al-Momineen, Sayyidah Maimunah, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray on the Khumra."
"1412","It was narrated from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace be upon him) prayed on a mat."
"1413","It is narrated on the authority of Sayyidna Mu'awiya bin Abi Sufyan (RA) that he asked Sayyida Umm Habiba (RA) who was his real sister: Did the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) pray in the clothes that he used to have intercourse with, she said: Yes, when there was no impurity in those clothes."
"1414","Sayyidna Mu'awiya bin Sufyan (RA) narrated from his sister, Sayyida Umm Habiba (RA), the wife of the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him), that he asked Sayyida Umm Habiba (RA): Did the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) pray in the clothes in which he used to associate with her? He said: Yes (he used to read) when he did not see impurity in this cloth."
"1415","Saeed bin Yazid Azdi said: I asked Sayyidna Anas bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him: Did the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, pray with his shoes on? Said: Yes (used to read)."
"1416","Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) said that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) was once praying with his Companions when he suddenly took off his shoes and placed them on his left side. When the Companions saw this, they also took off their shoes. When the Prophet (peace be upon him) finished the prayer, he said: \What compelled you to take off your shoes?\"" He said: We saw you take off your shoe"
"1417","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira disliked Sadal and attributed the dislike to the Messenger of Allah."
"1418","Abu Rafi' (the teacher of the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace) said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw me prostrating with a pair of shoes on, so he, may God bless him and grant him peace, untied them."
"1419","The freed slave of Kareeb Ibn Abbas said that Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) saw Abdullah Ibn Harith praying with his hair tied back, so Sayyidna Ibn Abbas (RA) stood behind him and started to untie the hair, another person also supported him. Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: \The example of a person who prays with his hands tied behind his back is like that of someone who prays with his hands tied behind his back.\"""""
"1420","Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Saeed narrated from his father that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Whenever one of you yawns"
"1421","It was narrated from Sayyida Aisha that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When one of you feels drowsy while praying"
"1422","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas (RA) said: I was informed that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said that the prayer of a person who prays while sitting is half the prayer. I have received news that you said: The prayer of a person who prays sitting is half a prayer, and you yourself are praying sitting? He (peace be upon him) said: \Yes (I have said so)"
"1423","Umm al-Momineen Sayyida Hafsa bint Umar, the blessed wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I never saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, perform Nafil prayer while sitting. Only a year or two before the death of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sitting and praying, in which he (peace be upon him) would recite the Surah with a trident and it would become longer and longer."
"1424","This hadith was also narrated by Sayyida Hafsa (may God be pleased with her) on the authority of Uthman bin Umar."
"1425","Sayyidna Mu'iqib Ibn Abi Talha (RA) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) was asked about removing pebbles in the mosque, and he (PBUH) said: \If it is very necessary"
"1426","Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may God be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of God (peace and blessings of God be upon him) said: \When one of you stands up for prayer"
"1427","Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) says that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \I have been given five things which were not given to any Prophet before me. The Prophet was sent to his own nation and I have been sent as a Prophet to all mankind in general. The booty has been made lawful for me"
"1428","Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \The whole earth is a place of prostration (mosque) except for graves and baths.\"" (It is not permissible to pray in tombs and baths). Imam Darmi (may Allah have mercy on him) was asked: If someone prays in a tomb"
"1429","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may God be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: When it is time for prayer and you do not find any place other than goats' and camels' (places for them to sit), pray in goats' pens and do not pray in camels' pens."
"1430","It is narrated on the authority of Mahmud bin Labaid that when Sayyiduna Uthman (RA) planned to build a mosque, the people disliked it. Sayyiduna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: \Whoever builds a mosque for Allah"
"1431","On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Qatadah Al-Salami, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said: \When any of you comes to the mosque"
"1432","Abu Hameed and Abu Aseed Ansari, may Allah be pleased with them, say that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When a person among you enters the mosque"
"1433","Shuba said: I asked Qatadah: Did you hear Sayyiduna Anas narrating from the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, that spitting in the mosque is a sin? Qatadah said: Yes, and (also heard that) his expiation is to bury him."
"1434","On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When a servant prays standing"
"1435","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was giving a sermon, and while he was giving a sermon, he saw phlegm (on the wall) towards the Qiblah of the mosque. Do not put""
1436"""
"1436","A marfu' hadith: Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Sa'd, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, that Abu Sa'id and Abu Hurayra informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) saw some sputum on the wall of the mosque, so he took a pebble and scraped it off, then said: ""When one of you expels phlegm, let him not expel it in front of him or to his right, but let him spit to his left or under his foot."
"1437","Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I was sleeping in the Masjid (of the Prophet) when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me and warned me with his blessed feet and said: Do I not see you sleeping here? I said: O Prophet of Allah! I was blinded."
"1438","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (RA) said: I used to sleep in the Prophet's Mosque because there were no wives or children. I dreamed that I was taken to a well, in which men were hanging. It was said: Take them to the right side (i.e. to the people of Paradise). I narrated this dream to (my sister) Sayyida Hafsa (may God be pleased with her) and requested her to relate it to the Messenger of God (may God bless him and grant him peace), so she narrated it to him (may God bless him and grant him peace), and he (may God bless him and grant him peace) said: \Who has seen this dream?\"" He said: (My brother) Ibn Umar"
"1439","On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When you see someone buying and selling in the mosque"
"1440","Sufyan bin Uyaina said to Amr bin Dinar: Did you hear from Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) that a man came to the Prophet's Mosque carrying an arrow, and the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said to him: \Stop their tips?\"" Said: Yes."""
"1441","It is narrated on the authority of Sayyida Aisha and Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, both of whom said: When the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, fell ill (i.e., dying), he used to put a sheet over his blessed face, and when he began to suffocate, he would open his mouth and say: \May Allah curse the Jews and the Christians"
"1442","Abu Thamama Hanat said: Sayyiduna Ka'b bin Ajrah (RA) found me on the floor (on my way to the mosque) and I was intertwining my fingers, so he said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \When one of you goes out to the mosque with the intention of performing ablution"
"1443","Sayyiduna Ka'b bin Ajrah (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \When you intend to go to the mosque after performing ablution"
"1444","Sayyidina Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If a person performs ablution (at home) and then goes out for prayer, he remains in prayer until he returns to his house."
"1445","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \The angels continue to pray for the servant as long as he is sitting in the place where he prayed"
"1446","On the authority of Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \The Hour will not be established until people take pride in the mosques.\"""""
"1447","Sayyiduna Abu Juhaifa (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Bataha (valley) in the afternoon and prayed two rak'ahs of Zuhr and Asr (i.e. with congregational offerings), and in front of him was a spearhead, and women's rides were passing in front of him."
"1448","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) that a javelin (stick) would be made for the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) and he would turn towards it and pray (i.e. in the air he would pray with the javelin or stick turned into seventeen)."
"1449","On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said: \When one of you is praying"
"1450","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform the Salat while riding a camel."
"1451","Sayyidna Urwa bin Zubair (RA) narrated that Sayyida Aisha (RA) informed him that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) used to pray and she used to lie on the bed of the house between him and the Qiblah like a funeral."
"1452","Sayyidina Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \When something in front of a man is not equal to the back wood of a crib"
"1453","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I and Fazl (his brother) came sitting on a donkey and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was leading the prayer in Mina or Arafat. (Narrated by al-Bukhari: No one challenged me on this)."
"1454","Basr bin Saeed said: Abu Jahim Ansari sent me to ask Sayyidna Zayd bin Khalid Jahni, may Allah be pleased with him, what he had heard from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about the man who passed in front of the prayer. He said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \If one of you stands for forty days"
"1455","Basr bin Saeed reported that Zayd bin Khalid Jahni sent him to the service of Sayyidna Abu Jahim (Abdullah) Ansari to ask him what he had heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say about the one who passes in front of the person praying. Sayyiduna Abu Jahim, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \If the person who passes in front of a person who is praying knows how much of a sin he is committing"
"1456","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) said: \A prayer in this mosque of mine is a thousand degrees better than all other mosques except Masjid Haram.\"""""
"1457","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) said: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \One prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers in other mosques"
"1458","On the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Huraira, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \One prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers in all other mosques"
"1459","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \One should not travel to any mosque except for three mosques"
"1460","Sayyiduna Abu Dardah (RA) said: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Whoever goes out to pray in the darkness of the night"
"1461","Sayyiduna Abu Dharr Ghafari (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \Allah"
"1462","It was narrated from Abdullah Bin Habshi that the Prophet was asked which action is best. He said: \There is no doubt that believing in Allah Ta'ala is the best deed"
"1463","Sayyiduna Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \Whoever prays the two cold prayers (Fajr and Asr) on time"
"1464","On the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \The person who prays Fajr is in the covenant of Allah"
"1465","Abdullah bin Arqam narrated that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When it is time for prayer and a person needs the toilet"
"1466","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (SAW) forbade praying with hands on the waist."
"1467","Sayyiduna Abu Burza Aslami (RA) said: The Prophet (SAW) used to dislike sleeping before the Isha prayer and talking after the prayer."
"1468","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: When the Messenger of Allah (SAW) sent Sayyiduna Ali bin Abi Talib (RA) to Makkah, I was with him. He announced four things until his voice was full: Listen, only the soul of faith will enter Paradise. The period is four months, after this period Allah and His Messenger are absolved from polytheism."
"1469","On the authority of Sabrah (bin Mabad Jahni) that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Teach a seven-year-old child to pray"
"1470","Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Aamir (RA) said that there were three hours (times) in which the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) used to prevent us from praying and burying the dead at these times: at sunrise until the sun rises to a certain height, at sunset until the sun tilts towards the west, at sunset until the sun sets completely."
"1471","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated that some of his favorite people narrated the hadith to me, including Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, and Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, is the most favorite to me. The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \There is no prayer after the Fajr prayer until the sun rises"
"1472","Abu Ishaq said: I heard from Aswad bin Yazid and Masrooq, they testified that Sayyida Aisha testified that whenever the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, visited her house, he used to pray these two rak'ahs. Imam al-Darmi (may Allah have mercy on him) said: He meant the two rak'ahs after Asr prayer."
"1473","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) says that the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) never missed two rak'ahs after Asr."
"1474","It was narrated on the authority of Kareeb (a freed slave of Ibn Abbas) that Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, Sayyidna Abd al-Rahman bin Al-Azhar, and Sayyidna Saud bin Mukharama (RA) sent them to Sayyida Aisha (RA) and asked her to say the salam of all of us and to ask her about the two rak'ats after the Asr prayer and to say that we have been informed that you also perform this rak'at although we have hadith from the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) that you The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade praying after Asr prayer. Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, said: And after Asr prayer, I killed people with Sayyiduna Umar, may Allah be pleased with them. Kareeb said: I came to the service of Sayyida Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, and conveyed to her the message of those people, so she said: Go and ask Sayyida Umm Salama, may God be pleased with her. He sent to Anha with the same message that he had sent to Sayyida Aisha. Sayyidah Umm Salama (RA) said: I heard from the Messenger of Allah (PBUH), he used to forbid it, but one day I saw him praying two rak'ahs after Asr. After reading these two rak'ats, I said to the slave girl: Go stand by you and say: Umm Salma says: O Messenger of Allah! I have heard you forbidding them, so what do I see that you are studying yourself? If the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) signaled with his hand, he should stop for a while, so the slave girl did the same and he signaled with his hand, so she stood back from him. When he (peace be upon him) had finished, he said: \O daughter of Abu Umayyah! You asked me about praying two rak'ahs after Asr prayer? The thing is that some people of Abdul Qais came to me to convert to Islam"
"1475","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray two rak'ahs before the Zuhr prayer, two rak'ahs after it, two rak'ahs after the Maghrib prayer, two rak'ahs after the Isha prayer, and two rak'ahs after the Jumu'ah prayer."
"1476","Sayyida Umm Habiba, the wife of the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, narrated that she heard the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: \Whoever prays 12 rak'ahs of the Sunnah in addition to the obligatory prayer"
"1477","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: The Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) never missed four rak'ahs before the Zuhr prayer and two rak'ahs (Sunnah) before the Fajr prayer."
"1478","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mughfil (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \There is a prayer between every two calls (Azan and Iqamah)"
"1479","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: During the blessed era of the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him), the muezzin would give the Maghrib call to prayer, and the chosen companions of the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) would cling to the pillars. He said: And you, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, would hardly have waited."
"1480","Sayyida Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to hide what he recited in those two rak'ahs (i.e., he did not recite aloud) and mentioned that he used to recite \Qul ya ayyah al-kafiroon\"" and \""Qul hu Allah is One\"". Saeed bin Aamir said: That is"
"1481","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (RA) said: Sayyida Hafsa (RA) narrated that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray two light rak'ahs after dawn, and this was an hour in which I was not present at the service of the Prophet (peace be upon him)."
"1482","Umm al-Mu'minin, Sayyida Hafsa, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: When the muezzin was silent from the Fajr call, and the morning dawned, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would recite two light rak'ahs before the congregation stood up."
"1483","Salim narrated from his father Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) used to pray two rak'ahs of the Sunnah after the Friday prayer, and Sayyida Hafsa (RA) informed him that when the morning dawned, he (PBUH) used to pray two rak'ahs of the Sunnah."
"1484","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed two rak'ahs before Fajr, if any need arose, he would have spoken to me, otherwise he would have gone to pray without saying a word."
"1485","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray eleven rak'ahs between the Isha and Fajr prayers, saying salam on every two rak'ahs and praying one rak'ah of witr, then when the muezzin was silent after giving the Fajr call to prayer, he would recite two light rak'ahs (sunnah), then lie down on his side until the muezzin was present for the service and you would accompany him."
"1486","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \When the Iqamah of the prayer is said"
"1487","From this chain of transmission, Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrated the same from the Prophet (PBUH)."
"1488","Sayyiduna Ibn Bahina, may Allah be pleased with him, said: When the prayer was finished, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw a person who was praying two rak'ahs of the Sunnah. When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, finished the prayer, people surrounded him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Do you pray the four rak'ahs of Fajr?\"""""
"1489","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Huraira that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When the Iqamah of the prayer is said (i.e. Takbeer)"
"1490","It was narrated from Naeem bin Hamar Ghatfani that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Allah Almighty says: O son of Adam! Pray four rak'ats for me at the beginning of the day"
"1491","Ibn Abi Laili says: No one has informed us except Sayyida Umm Hani (RA) that the Prophet (SAW) prayed Chasht, so she (Sayyida Umm Hani (RA) mentioned that on the day of the conquest of Makkah, the Messenger of Allah (SAW) took bath in her house, then prayed eight rak'ahs and said, \I have never seen you (SAWS) perform such a light prayer"
"1492","Sayyidah Umm Hani bint Abi Talib (RA) narrates that she went to the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) on the day of the conquest of Makkah and found him taking a ghusl and Sayyida Fatimah (RA) was covering him. The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Who is this?\"" I said: I am Umm Hani. He said: Then when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished his bath"
"1493","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: My dear friend (Muhammad (PBUH)) has bequeathed me three things which I cannot leave before death. Reciting Witr before going to sleep, fasting for three days in every month, and praying two rakats of Chasht."
"1494","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never offered Chasht prayer while traveling or visiting."
"1495","It was narrated from Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Bakra that his father (Abu Bakra) saw some people praying Chasht and said: These people pray such a prayer that neither the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, nor his common companions did."
"1496","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyidna Zaid bin Arqam that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out after sunrise and saw people praying, so he said: \The time for the Salat al-Awabeen is when the feet of the camels start burning.\"""""
"1497","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \The day and night prayers are two rak'ahs each.\"" Some narrators said Rakatin Rakatin."""
"1498","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: A person asked the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, about the night prayer (Tahjud), and he, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \(It is) two rak'ahs. When one of you is afraid of dawn"
"1499","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Salam, may Allah be pleased with him, said: When the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to Madinah, people were waiting for him. After hearing this, I also came out with other people and now I saw the blessed face of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Will enter.\""
1500"""
"1500","(Marfu' Hadith) Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Harun ibn Riyab, from al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, who said: I entered the Mosque of Damascus, and there was a man excessively bowing and prostrating. I said: ""I will not leave until I see if he knows whether he finished on an even (shaf') or odd (witr) number."" When he finished, I said: ""O servant of Allah, do you know if you finished on an even or odd number?"" He said: ""If I do not know, then Allah knows."" Then he said: ""I heard my beloved Abu al-Qasim (ﷺ) say: 'No servant prostrates a prostration to Allah except that Allah raises him by it a degree and removes from him by it a sin.'"" I said: ""Who are you, may Allah have mercy on you?"" He said: ""I am Abu Dharr."" He said: ""My soul fell short (in humility) before me."""
"1501","Sha'a'a narrated that I saw Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abi Ufa, may Allah be pleased with him, he prayed two rak'ahs and said that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) received the good news of the conquest of Makkah or the beheading of Abu Jahl, he (peace be upon him) prayed two rak'ahs at the time of Chasht."
"1502","Sayyidna Qays bin Sa'd (may God be pleased with him) said: I went to Hira (a city of Kufa) and saw that the people there were prostrating to their leader. Shall we not bow down to you? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \If I were to order someone to prostrate"
"1503","Narrated Abu Burida, his father said: An Arab came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah! Allow me to bow to you? The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \If I had ordered a person to prostrate to anyone"
"1504","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas’ud (RA) that when the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) recited Surah Najm, he prostrated therein (on the verse Sajdah), and all the people present there prostrated except for one sheikh (old man) who took a handful of sand and pebbles and placed them on his forehead and said: This is enough for me (instead of prostrating). Died in state)."
"1505","Sayyidina Abu Saeed al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, said: One day, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited Surah S, and when he reached the verse of Sajdah, he came down from the pulpit, and after prostrating, we also prostrated with him, and then he recited Surah S for the second time (Friday Sermon), and we got ready for prostration. (i.e. Sajdah is not necessary) but I have seen you preparing for Sajdah. So he came down and he prostrated, so we also prostrated with him."
"1506","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said about the prostration of Surah S: This prostration is not one of the obligatory recitations, and I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrating upon it."
"1507","Sayyiduna Abu Salama (RA) said: I asked Sayyidna Abu Huraira (RA): Prostrate in “Izza al-Samaa Anshaqat” [Sura Al-Anshaqaq]."
"1508","Sayyiduna Abu Salama (RA) said: I saw Sayyidna Abu Huraira (RA) prostrating in the verse of “Izza al-Samaa Anshaqat” [Surah Al-Anshaqaq 1/84], so I said: O Abu Hurairah! Is this what I see you prostrating in the sky? He replied that if I had not seen the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrating in it, I would never have prostrated."
"1509","On the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prostrated in \Izza al-Sama' anshaqat\""."""
"1510","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: We prostrated with the Prophet (PBUH) in “Izza al-Sama’a Anshakat” and “Iqra Bismi Rabbik” (Surah Al-Alaq)."
"1511","Sayyidna Zaid bin Thabit (RA) said: I recited Surah Al-Najm with the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) and he did not prostrate in it."
"1512","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray eleven rak'ahs between Isha and Fajr, saying salam on every two rak'ahs and praying one rak'ah of witr, and before raising his head in this Tahajjud prayer, he (may God bless him and grant him peace) used to prostrate so (long) that one of you recites fifty verses, then when the muezzin finished the Fajr call, he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would recite two light rak'ahs and (right) crouch. But you would lie down until the muezzin came to you and you would take him out."
"1513","Abu Salama bin Abdur Rahman said: I asked Sayyida Aisha about the night prayer of the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray thirteen rakats (prayer at night)."
"1514","(Marfu' Hadith) Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from Sa'd ibn Hisham, that he divorced his wife and came to Medina to sell his property to put it into weapons and mounts. He met a group of the Ansar who said: ""Six of us intended that during the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), but he forbade them and said: 'Do you not have an example in me?'"" Then he came to Basrah, and he narrated to us that he met 'Abdullah ibn 'Abbas and asked him about the Witr. He said: ""Shall I not inform you of the most knowledgeable person regarding the Witr of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)?"" I said: ""Yes."" He said: ""The Mother of the Believers, 'A'ishah. Go to her and ask her, then return to me and inform me of what she tells you."" I went to Hakim ibn Aflah and said: ""Come with me to the Mother of the Believers, 'A'ishah."" He said: ""I will not go to her; I was forbidden from these two factions (parties), but she refused except to go ahead."" I said: ""I adjure you by Allah to go."" So we went, greeted her, and she recognized Hakim's voice. She said: ""Who is this?"" I said: ""Sa'd ibn Hisham."" She said: ""Who is Hisham?"" I said: ""Hisham ibn 'Amir."" She said: ""What an excellent man; he was killed on the day of Uhud."" I said: ""Inform us of the character of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)."" She said: ""Do you not recite the Qur'an?"" I said: ""Yes."" She said: ""Then his character was the Qur'an."" I wanted to stand and not ask anyone about anything until I meet Allah, but the matter of standing (Qiyam al-Layl) presented itself to me. I said: ""Inform us of the standing of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)."" She said: ""Do you not recite: 'O you wrapped in garments (Al-Muzzammil)'?"" I said: ""Yes."" She said: ""That was the standing of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). The beginning of the Surah was revealed, so the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and his Companions stood until their feet swelled, and its end was withheld in the heaven for sixteen months, then it was revealed, so the standing of the night became voluntary after it had been obligatory."" I wanted to stand and not ask anyone about anything until I meet Allah, but the matter of Witr presented itself to me. I said: ""Inform us of the Witr of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)."" She said: ""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), when he slept, placed his siwak with me. Then Allah would awaken him whenever He willed. He would pray nine rak'ahs, not sitting except in the eighth, where he would praise Allah and supplicate his Lord, then stand without giving salam. Then he would sit in the ninth, praise Allah, supplicate his Lord, and give a salam we could hear. Then he would pray two rak'ahs sitting. That is eleven rak'ahs, O my son. When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) grew old and gained weight, he prayed seven rak'ahs, not sitting except in the sixth... (similar description) ... That is nine, O my son. And the Prophet (ﷺ), if sleep or illness overcame him, would pray twelve rak'ahs during the day. And the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), when he adopted a practice, loved to persist in it. And the Prophet of Allah (ﷺ) never stood a whole night until morning, nor recited the entire Qur'an in a single night, nor fasted a complete month other than Ramadan."" I went to Ibn 'Abbas and informed him. He said: ""She spoke the truth to you. Would that I had entered upon her to hear it directly from her."" I said: ""Would that I had known you would not enter upon her, I would not have informed you."""
"1515","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Huraira that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \After the obligatory prayer"
"1516","Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab (RA) said that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \If a person neglects his duty or any of it and falls asleep and recites it between Fajr and Zuhr"
"1517","Sayyidina Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \Allah descends on the sky every night when the last half of the night remains"
"1518","Sayyidina Abu Huraira (RA) reported that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: “Our Lord, whose name is blessed, descends on the world every night at the time when the last third of the night is left, He says: Whoever prays to Me, I will accept his prayer, whoever asks Me for forgiveness, I will forgive him, and whoever asks Me, I will fill his cradle, (Fajr). It continues to be preached till then.”"
"1519","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyidna Jubayr bin Mut'am, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Allah"
"1520","Sayyidna Rafa'ah bin Araba Jahni (RA) said: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \When half or two-thirds of the night has passed"
"1521","Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya, from Hilal ibn Abi Maymunah, from 'Ata' ibn Yasar, that Rifa'ah informed him, from the Prophet, peace be upon him, something similar."
"1522","Sayyiduna Ali, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When the night is a third or a half.\"" And narrated the above-mentioned hadith of descent."""
"1523","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) saying: “If I did not feel hardship on my ummah, I would order them to rub their teeth during every prayer and delay the Isha prayer for a third of the night, because when the first third of the night has passed, Allah, the Exalted, comes to the sky and stays there until dawn, and the angel proclaims: Is there no one who asks for something to be given, is there no one who prays that he prays? Be accepted, is there not a sick person to be healed, is there not a sinner who seeks forgiveness and is forgiven?”"
"1524","From this chain of command, the above-mentioned hadith is narrated like the narration of Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"1525","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may God be pleased with him, said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would get up for Tahajjud at night, he would recite this dua: “Allahum lak al-hamdu ........ wala hawla wala quwa illa bik” until, “O my Allah! All praise is due to You, You are the light of the heavens and the earth and all the universe that dwells in them.” Yes, you are the one who controls the heavens and the earth and all the creatures that live in them, all the praises are beautiful to you and you are the king of all the heavens and the earth and all the creatures in them, you are true, your command is true, your promise is true, your meeting is true, heaven is true, hell is true, rising after death is true, all the prophets are true and Muhammad, peace be upon him, is true, O Allah! I have believed, and I trust in You, and I have turned to You, and I argue with Your arguments, and I have commanded You, so forgive all the mistakes that happened before me and those that will happen after, whether they are visible or hidden, You are the One who leads forward and holds back, there is no god but You, and power and strength are from You alone."
"1526","It was narrated from Sayyidna Abu Mas'ud (RA) that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \Whoever recites the last two verses of Surah Baqarah in a night"
"1527","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \Allah has not permitted anything as much as He permitted His Prophet to recite the Holy Qur'an loudly and with good melody.\"""""
"1528","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard Sayyidna Abu Musa al-Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him) reciting, and said: \He has been given a voice from the voices of the House of Dawud.\"""""
"1529","On the authority of Saad bin Abi Waqqas, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \He who does not recite the Qur'an with pleasure is not one of us.\"""""
"1530","On the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Allah does not listen to anything with such love (and attention) as He listens to a Prophet reciting the Qur'an with melodious melodiousness.\"" Imam al-Darmi"
"1531","Sayyiduna Abu Saeed bin Mu'ali (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) passed by me and said: \Have you not read the commandment of Allah: \""O you who believe"
"1532","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \He who recites the Holy Qur'an in less than three days has not understood anything.\"""""
"1533","On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When the call to prayer is given, Satan turns his back and runs away, emitting wind so that he cannot hear the call to prayer. Do it, it reminds him of things that were not in the mind of the person praying, in this way a person does not even remember how many prayers he has prayed, so when one of you cannot remember how many rak'ahs he has prayed three or four, then he should perform two Sajdah while sitting (i.e. perform Sajdah)."
"1534","Sayyidina Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When one of you does not know whether he has prayed three rak'ahs or four rak'ahs"
"1535","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) offered one of the two afternoon prayers and prayed two rak'ahs before salutations. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood near a piece of wood placed in the mosque and supported it with his hand. Yazid bin Haroon said: Ibn Aun told us to place the hands in this way, placing one hand on the back of the other and joining the fingers of the upper hand to the fingers of the lower hand. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood up, it was evident that he was angry. Those who were going to leave quickly left and said, \The prayer has been shortened"
"1536","Sayyidina Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) prayed the Zuhr or Asr prayers and in one of them he offered the salam over two rak'ahs, then Dhul-Shamalin bin Abd bin Amr bin Nazlat al-Khuza'i, who was an ally of Banuzahra, said: O Messenger of Allah! The prayer is reduced or you have forgotten? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Neither have I forgotten"
"1537","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, offered five rak'ahs of the Zuhr prayer."
"1538","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Malik Ibn Bahina (may God be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of God (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) offered us two rak'ahs of prayer and he stood and did not sit down (i.e. he did not perform tashahhud) and the Muqtadi also stood with him (peace be upon him)."
"1539","On the authority of Sayyiduna Malik Ibn Bahina, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood for two rak'ahs in the Zuhr or Asr prayer, and then did not return for tashahhud, until he had finished his prayer, then performed two prostrations, and then greeted him."
"1540","Ziyad bin Al-Aqalah said: When Sayyidna Mughira bin Shuba (RA) led us in prayer, they did not stand up after two rak'ahs. The worshipers said Subhan Allah, but he indicated that they should also stand up."
"1541","Sayyiduna Muawiyah bin Hukm Salmi (RA) said: I was praying with the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) when a person sneezed, so I said, \May God have mercy on you.\"" Now people started staring at me. Then he said"
"1542","This chain of transmission is similar to the above-mentioned hadith."
"1543","On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered two black things to be killed in prayer."
"1544","Ya'li bin Umayyah said: I told Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, that Allah, the Exalted, said: \Do not shorten the prayer if you are afraid...\"" [Nisaa: 101/4] That is"
"1545","Salim narrated from his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar) that I prayed two rakats of Qasr with the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, Abu Bakr and Umar (by shortening Zuhr Asr) in Mina."
"1546","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) said: We prayed four rak'ahs of the Zuhr prayer with the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) in Madinah, and he prayed two rak'ahs (Qasr) in the afternoon in Dhul-Hulaifah."
"1547","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) says: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed four rak'ats of Zuhr prayer in Madinah and two rak'ats of Asr prayer in Dhul-Hulaifah."
"1548","Sayyida Ayesha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: When the prayer was first made obligatory, it was only two rak'ahs, which were kept during the journey and extended during Hadar (i.e. during Iqamah). He said: He also had the same opinion as the opinion of Sayyiduna Uthan."
"1549","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) said: When we set out with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intending to go to Makkah (for the farewell Hajj), he (may God bless him and grant him peace) continued to make Qasr until we reached Makkah and he stayed there for ten days and kept making Qasr until he returned."
"1550","Sayyiduna Ala bin Hazrami (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \A Muhajir can stay in Makkah for three days after performing Hajj.\"""""
"1551","Sayyiduna Alaa bin Hadrami (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (SAW) allowed the emigrants to stay in Makkah for three days before returning after Hajj. Abu Muhammad Imam Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: I also say the same."
"1552","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir (RA) that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) used to pray (Nafili) on his camel facing the east, and when he recited the fard, he would dismount and then pray facing the Qiblah."
"1553","Sayyidna Amir bin Rabi'ah (RA) said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) performing the nafl prayer on a camel."
"1554","Sayyiduna Mu'adh bin Jabal (RA) said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) in the year of the Tabuk campaign, and he (PBUH) used to pray together, in such a way that he prayed Zuhr and Asr together, then he went inside, and when he came out, he prayed Maghrib and Isha together."
"1555","It was narrated from Sayyidina Abu Ayyub Ansari that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited Maghrib and Isha in Muzdalifah and combined them (i.e. read them one after the other)."
"1556","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, had to travel quickly, so he used to recite Maghrib and Isha at the same time."
"1557","Both Al-Haqam and Salama bin Kaheel (may God have mercy on him) said: Sayyiduna Saeed bin Jubayr (may Allah be pleased with him) prayed for us three rakats of Maghrib after Iqamah in Muzdalifah, then he stood up after salutations, then he prayed two rakats of Isha, then he narrated the hadith that Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) prayed in the same way at that place, and Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) also did the same at that place."
"1558","The above-mentioned hadith is also narrated from this chain of transmission."
"1559","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Ka'b bin Malik (RA) that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) would return from his journey in the morning, then go to the mosque, pray two rak'ahs, and then talk to the people."
"1560","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) in the expedition to Najd (Zat al-Raqqa), so when we faced the enemy, we formed ranks and the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) led us in the prayer (of fear). Then these people returned and came to the place of the group that had not prayed yet. Now this group came and bowed and made two prostrations with him, then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of God be upon him, returned the salutation and each person from this group stood up and performed one bow and two prostrations individually."
"1561","Sahl bin Abi Hatmah said about Salat al-Khuf: The imam prays with one group and one group stands firm against the enemy, then the imam leads one rakat with the group that is with him, then this group moves to the place of the group that is facing the enemy, and he comes and prays one rakat with the imam, then each group completes one rakat by itself."
"1562","From another chain of transmission, Sahl bin Abi Hasthama has narrated the same example from the Holy Prophet (peace be upon him)."
"1563","Sayyiduna Abu Saeed al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, said: We were prevented (from prayer) on the Day of the Trench until a part of the night had passed, then the fighting stopped, as Allah the Exalted said: 25/33] So the Holy Prophet called Sayyiduna Bilal (RA) and ordered him to Iqamah (Takbeer) and he prayed Zuhr in a very good manner, as he (PBUH) used to pray in his time. He commanded ``Anhu, he said Iqamah and he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) offered the ``Isha'' prayer, and this was until the verse of ``Salat al-Khuf'', ``Fin Khiftum Farijalah aw Rukbaan...'' [Baqarah: 239/2] was revealed."
"1564","On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with him: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Verily"
"1565","On the authority of Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed eight bows and four prostrations in Al-Kusuf prayer."
"1566","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyida Aisha that a Jewish woman came to her and said, May Allah protect you from the punishment of the grave. Then when the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came, I said: Will the people be punished in their graves? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sought refuge in Allah. Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: One day the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting on a horse and the sun was eclipsed. which was a little shorter than the first standing, then bowed and bowed longer, but it was shorter than the first bow, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed two prostrations, then stood up and recited the second rak'ah in the same way. I seek Your refuge, O Allah! I seek Your refuge from the punishment of Hell."
"1567","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, said: When the sun was eclipsed, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, offered two rak'at prayers. Now if you see such an (eclipse), immediately go to prayer."
"1568","Imam Malik, may God have mercy on him, narrated in the same way from Hisham bin Urwa on the authority of Abiyya on the authority of Sayyida Aisha, may God be pleased with her."
"1569","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: When the sun was eclipsed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed."
"1570","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyida Asma bint Abi Bakr, that when the sun was eclipsed, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered charity."
"1571","From the second chain of transmission, Sayyida Asmaa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated the same narration from the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him)."
"1572","Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Zayd Radiyallahu Anhu narrates that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out to the Eidgah with the people to pray for rain, so he wept towards the Qibla and turned his cloak upside down."
"1573","Ibad bin Tamim reported that his uncle informed him that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took him to the place of Eidgah to pray for rain for the people, stood and prayed to Allah, then turned towards the Qiblah and threw up his cloak (the prayer of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was accepted) and it rained."
"1574","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not raise his hands in any prayer except praying for rain."
"1575","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (RA) said that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \When any of you wants to come for the Friday prayer"
"1576","Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \Ghusl is obligatory for every adult on Friday.\"""""
"1577","A similar hadith is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him."
"1578","Sayyidna Abu Hurairah (RA) narrated that Sayyidna Umar bin Al-Khattab (RA) was giving a sermon, and in the meantime, a person entered. After hearing the call to prayer, I only performed ablution. Sayyiduna Umar said: Only ablution? Have you not heard that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When any of you wants to come (for prayer) on Friday"
"1579","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyidna Samurah that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \He who performs ablution for Friday has done good"
"1580","Sayyiduna Salman Farsi, a companion of the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, narrated that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever takes a bath on Friday and performs a thorough purification, then applies oil and emits whatever fragrance is available in the house, then goes out (for Friday) and does not come between two people, and prays as much as he can, then remains silent when the Imam comes (for the sermon), then all his sins will be forgiven from that Friday to the next Friday.” are done.”"
"1581","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Prophet (PBUH) used to recite Surah Al-Sajda and Surah Al-Insan in the Fajr prayer on Fridays."
"1582","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \The example of the one who rushes to the Friday prayer is like the one who sacrifices a camel"
"1583","On the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When it is Friday"
"1584","Sayyiduna Zubayr bin Al-Awam (RA) said: We used to pray the Friday prayer with the Prophet (PBUH), then when we returned, we would hasten to go under the shade of the fort of Banugnam, which was equal to our feet."
"1585","Sayyiduna Salama bin Akwa (may Allah be pleased with him) said: When we returned with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after offering the Friday prayer, the shade of the walls was not enough for us to stay in it."
"1586","On the authority of Aus (bin Aus Thaqafi, may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Whoever takes a bath on Friday"
"1587","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \When the imam is giving the Friday sermon and you tell the person sitting next to you to shut up"
"1588","On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \If you say to the person sitting next to you"
"1589","Sayyidna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated the same as before in this chain of transmission."
"1590","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \When a person among you comes (to the mosque) and the Imam is giving a sermon or has left for the sermon"
"1591","Ayyad bin Abdullah said: Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) came and Marwan was delivering the sermon. Sayyidna Abu Saeed (RA) stood up and started to pray. Marwan's soldiers came and stopped him from praying. Sayyidna Abu Saeed (RA) said: \I will not abandon these two rak'ahs because I saw the Messenger of Allah (SAW) ordering it.\"""""
"1592","Rabi bin Sabih Basri said: I saw Imam Hasan Basri, may God have mercy on him, recite two rak'ahs during the sermon, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, said: \When the Imam is giving the khutbah and one of you enters the mosque"
"1593","Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) said: One day the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) gave us a sermon and recited Surah S. Then when he passed the verse of prostration, he got down and prostrated."
"1594","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) says: A person came to the mosque on Friday and the Prophet (PBUH) was giving a sermon. Answered: No, he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Get up and recite two rak'ahs.\"" Imam Darmi (may Allah have mercy on him) said: I also say the same."""
"1595","Abu Wail said: Sayyidna Ammar bin Yasir (RA) gave us a very short and very eloquent sermon, so we said: O Abu Yaqzan! Would it have been better if the sermon was longer? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, he used to say: \A man's lengthening his prayer and shortening his sermon is a sign of his understanding"
"1596","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Samurah (RA) said: I prayed with the Holy Prophet (PBUH) and his prayer (PBUH) was also in the middle and his sermon was also in the middle (i.e. neither too long nor too short)."
"1597","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to give two sermons while standing and sit between the two sermons."
"1598","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Samrah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to deliver two sermons and sit between them and recite the Qur'an during the sermon and admonish the people."
"1599","Hussain (bin Abd al-Rahman) said: Amara bin Ruwaibah saw Marwan's son Bishr raising his hands on the pulpit, so he said: May Allah curse those two hands."
"1600","Hussain bin Abdur Rahman said: Amara bin Ruwaibah saw Bishr bin Marwan raising his hands for supplication on the pulpit on Friday, so he scolded him and said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the pulpit and he (did not do so) only pointed with his finger, and he pointed from the side with his index finger."
"1601","Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) said: Before the pulpit was built, the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) used to deliver sermons while standing next to a palm tree. Then when the pulpit was set up (and you began to go towards it), that trunk wept with a soft voice until we heard its voice, so the Messenger of Allah, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, placed his hand on it, and its voice ceased."
"1602","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated that the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to deliver sermons by clinging to a palm trunk before the pulpit was built."
"1603","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated a similar narration from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1604","Sayyiduna Sahl bin Sa'd Radiyallahu Anhu said: When there were many people in Madinah, people would come and not be able to listen to the sermon of the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, and would return like that. The people have grown up, the visitor comes and cannot hear your words, he said: Then whatever you want, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called the son of an Ansari woman who was a carpenter (carpenter) and asked him to build a pulpit out of forest bark. He went to her and placed his blessed hand on her, and she became silent."
"1605","Dahhak bin Qays inquired from Sayyidna Numan bin Basheer, which Surah did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, recite after Surah Jumu'ah on Friday? Answered that: \He used to read Hadith al-Ghashiya\""."""
"1606","Dahhak bin Qais Fahri said: We asked Sayyiduna Nu'man bin Bashir Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him: Which surah did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite on Fridays, apart from the Surah in which Friday is mentioned? He replied: You used to read with him \Hal"""
"1607","Sayyiduna Nu'man bin Basheer (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) used to recite \Sabhi Asma Rabbik Al-A'ala\"" and \""Hal Attak Hadith Al-Ghashiyya\"" in the Eid and Friday prayers"
"1608","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: I met Ka'b Al-Ahbar, may God have mercy on him, and I started narrating the hadiths of the Messenger of Allah (PBUH), and he began to tell me about the Torah, until when Friday was mentioned, I said that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \There comes a time in which a Muslim asks for a favor from Allah"
"1609","Sayyidna Ibn Umar and Sayyidna Abu Huraira (RA) narrated that they heard the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) saying on the wood of his pulpit that people should refrain from skipping Friday, otherwise Allah will seal their hearts, then they will be among the heedless."
"1610","Sayyidna Abu Jaad Zamri (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \Whoever skips Jumu'ah out of laziness"
"1611","Sayyidna Aus bin Aus, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \The best day of your days is Friday"
"1612","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray two rak'ahs (Sunnah) in his house after Friday."
"1613","Salim narrated from his father, Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray two rak'ahs after Friday."
"1614","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyidina Abu Huraira that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Whoever among you wishes to pray after Friday"
"1615","Sayyidna Al-Khajrah ibn Hudhafa Adwi (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) came to us and said: \Indeed"
"1616","Ibn Muhairiz Qureshi Jamhi, who lived in the country of Syria, found the time of Sayyiduna Muawiyah (RA). He reported that a man from Binuknana, Makhdji, told him that there was a person in the country of Syria whose surname was Abu Muhammad, who was a Companion, and he said that Witr is obligatory. Makhdji came to Sayyidna Ubada bin Samit, may God be pleased with him, and mentioned this to him. Sayyidna Ubada, may God be pleased with him, said: Abu Muhammad lied. What, the person who brings these prayers in the condition that he has paid their full right, and has not missed any kind of payment, then Allah Almighty has a promise for him that he will enter Paradise, and the person who did not bring these prayers (i.e. abandoned the prayers without considering their importance), then Allah Almighty has no promise, whether He punishes him or admits him to Paradise if He wants."
"1617","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Talha bin Ubaidullah (RA) that a villager came to the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) with disheveled hair and said: O Messenger of Allah! How many prayers has Allah made obligatory on me? He said: \Five prayers and fasting are (also) obligatory.\"" After that"
"1618","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Witr (obligation) is not obligatory like prayer, but it is a Sunnah and do not leave it."
"1619","On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Huraira, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Allah is Witr and He loves Witr.\"""""
"1620","It was narrated from Sayyida Aisha that the night prayer of the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, consisted of thirteen rak'ahs, in which he prayed five rak'ahs of witr and did not sit down, but in the last rak'ah he made tashahhud and returned the salam."
"1621","Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub Ansari said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: \Recite five rak'ahs of witr"
"1622","Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub (RA) narrated the same narration from the Prophet (PBUH) from this chain of transmission."
"1623","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: A person asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the night prayer, and he (peace be upon him) said: \It is two rak'ahs"
"1624","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray eleven rak'ats between Isha and Fajr, and he would offer salam and one rak'at Witr after every two rak'ats."
"1625","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him, said: The Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite \Sabhi Ism Rabbi'k Al-A'ala\"""
"1626","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited Witr in every part of the night, and in the last part of the night, his Witr came close to dawn."
"1627","Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) was asked about Witr, and he (PBUH) said: \Recite Witr before Fajr.\"""""
"1628","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him, said: The Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite Witr three rakats. In the first rakat, he used to recite \Sabhi Asm Rabbik Al-A'ala\"" in the second rakat"
"1629","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite Witr on a camel. Imam Darmi (may Allah have mercy on him) was asked: Do you also say the same? Said: Yes (i.e. Witr can be recited while riding)."
"1630","Abu Hurairah Saadi said: I asked Sayyiduna Hasan bin Ali (RA): What do you remember from the Messenger of Allah (PBUH)? He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) once made me sit on his shoulder. I took one of the dates from the Sadaqah date and put it in my mouth. Blessings and Exaltations. \O Allah"
"1631","Sayyiduna Hasan bin Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reminded me of some words that I used to say in Qunut. Then he recited the above mentioned supplication, i.e. \Allahum"""
"1632","On the authority of Abu Hurairah Saadi, Sayyiduna Hasan bin Ali, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, reminded me of some words that I recite in Qunut Witr, and up to \Allahummah Ahdini Fiman Hadeet Akhirtak Padhi Tabarakat Wat Ta'alait.\"" Imam al-Darmi Abu Muhammad"
"1633","On the authority of Sayyiduna Thawban, may God bless him and grant him peace, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Surely"
"1634","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah that when the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to make supplications for someone or make supplication for someone, he would recite Qunut after bowing. Save Salma bin Hisham, Ayyash bin Abi Rabiyyah and those who are weak among the Muslims, O Allah tighten your grip on the evil one and make them suffer from a famine like the famine that came in the time of Yusuf (peace be upon him). And by cursing so-and-so, until this noble verse was revealed: \There is nothing for you from the commandment"
"1635","Asim said: I asked Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik about qunut, and he said: It is before bowing. I said: So-and-so thinks that you said that qunut is after bowing. They continued to curse."
"1636","Sayyiduna Bara bin Azib (RA) narrated that the Prophet (PBUH) used to recite Qunut in the Fajr prayer."
"1637","Abu Na'im also narrated a similar narration from Shu'ba."
"1638","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) was asked: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform qunaut in the Fajr prayer? Answered: Yes. Was it inquired or (it was said) I said: Before bowing or after bowing (recited the Qunut)? Said: After bowing for a few days. Imam al-Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: I am a believer and practitioner of this, and in my opinion, this qunut is permissible only in the days of war."
"1639","Abdullah bin Burida narrated from his father that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to go out after eating on the day of Eid al-Fitr, and would not eat anything on Eid al-Adha until he returned and ate from his own sacrifice."
"1640","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) has also narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1641","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I came to pray with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Eid."
"1642","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, says: I testify that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, started the prayer before the sermon on the day of Eid, and then gave the sermon. stay"
"1643","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I was present with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr, Umar and Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) on the day of Eid."
"1644","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, came on the day of Eid al-Fitr and offered a double prayer, and did not offer any prayer before or after it."
"1645","Sayyidna Ammar bin Yasir (RA) said: The Prophet (PBUH) used to say Takbeer seven times in the first Rak'at of Eid and five Takbeer in the second Rak'at, and before the sermon he would start with the prayer."
"1646","Sayyiduna Nu'man bin Basheer (RA) said: The Prophet (PBUH) used to recite \Sabih-e-Ism-Rabbik-Al-Ala\"" and \""Hal-At-Taak Hadith-ul-Ghashiyyah\"" in Eid and Friday prayers"
"1647","Salama bin Nabit narrated that my father or Na'im bin Abi Hind said: I performed Hajj with my father and uncle, and my father said: Look, the one who is giving the sermon on the red camel is the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"1648","Sayyida Umm Atiya, may Allah be pleased with her, said: My father, the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, ordered us to take young virgins and veiled women with us on Eid al-Fitr and Eid al-Adha, and menstruating women (also come to the Eid hall but) stay away from the ranks and do good deeds (i.e. listen to the sermon) and join in the prayers of the Muslims. I said: O Messenger of Allah! What if none of us has a veil? He said: \His sister should cover him with her cloak.\"""""
"1649","Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah (may God be pleased with him) said: I was present with the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) in the Eid prayer. A low-ranking, black-cheeked person stood up and asked: Why is this, O Messenger of Allah? He said: \Because the cow complains"
"1650","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, has also narrated the same meaning from the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace."
"1651","Iyas bin Abi Ramlah said: I was present with Sayyidna Mu'awiya (may Allah be pleased with him) when he asked Sayyidna Zayd bin Arqam (may Allah be pleased with him): Did you observe Eid and Jumu'ah with the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) on the same day? He said: Yes, Sayyiduna Mu'awiyah asked: Then what did you (peace be upon him) do? Zayd said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the Eid prayer, then dismissed him on Friday and said: \Whoever wants to pray"
"1652","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Huraira that when the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, would go out for the Eid prayer, he would return by a different route."
"1653","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that when the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent Sayyiduna Muadh, may Allah be pleased with him, to Yemen, he said: “You are going to a people who are people of the Book. If they accept what you say about this, then tell them that Allah Ta'ala has made it obligatory for them to pay Zakat, which will be taken from their rich and distributed among their poor, then when they accept your word in this too, then avoid taking their good (more refined) wealth and avoid the wailing of the oppressed that there is no barrier between him and Allah Ta'ala.\""
1654"""
"1654","(Marfu' Hadith) Hashim ibn al-Qasim informed us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, who said: I heard Abu Hurayrah narrating from the Prophet (ﷺ) that he said: ""The poor person (miskin) is not the one who is turned away with a morsel or two, a piece or two, a date or two. Rather, the poor person is the one who has no wealth to suffice him, he is too shy to ask people persistently, or he does not ask people persistently."""
"1655","Sayyiduna Jabir, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Anyone who owns camels"
"1656","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) say: “The owner of a camel who does not pay his dues will come on the Day of Resurrection in many numbers and their owner will be made to sit on the ground and they will trample him with their feet and hooves. The cows will hit him with their horns and trample him under foot, and the goat owner who does not pay his due will also come many on the Day of Resurrection and their owner will be made to sit on the ground and those goats will hit him with their horns and crush him with their hooves, and on that day none of them will be hornless or broken horn, and the owner of the treasure who does not pay the due of this treasure will be the treasure on the Day of Resurrection. A bald dragon will follow (his worldly owner) with his mouth open, and when he comes to (the owner) in the form of a dragon, he will run away, then he will call, \Take your treasure that you have hidden"
"1657","Sayyiduna Abu Dharr also narrated part of the previous hadith from the Messenger of Allah."
"1658","On the authority of Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, wrote about Zakat, which was about goats, that there is one goat for every forty goats up to one hundred and twenty goats, then if there are more than that, two hundred goats are two goats, then from two hundred to three hundred there are three goats. And an old, blind or defective goat will not be accepted in Zakat."
"1659","Abu Bakr bin Muhammad bin Amr bin Hazm narrated to his father from his grandfather (Sayyidna Amr bin Hazm, may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, wrote to Sayyidna Amr bin Hazm, may Allah be pleased with him, for the people of Yemen: There is a goat (Zakat), so when one is more than one hundred and twenty, there are two goats up to two hundred, then if one goat is above two hundred, then there are three goats in them up to three hundred."
"1660","Abdullah bin Abi Bakr bin Muhammad bin Amr bin Hazm narrated from his father, he narrated from his grandfather that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote a letter to him ......... and narrated the hadith as mentioned above."
"1661","Sayyiduna Mu'adh (RA) said: When the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) sent me to Yemen, he ordered me to take a two-year-old heifer or bull for zakat from every forty cows (bulls) and a one-year-old male or female for every thirty cows."
"1662","Sayyiduna Mu'adh said, \The Messenger of Allah"
"1663","Ahmad bin Yunus has narrated the same from Abu Bakr bin Ayyash."
"1664","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) wrote the Sadaqah (statement of Zakat) which had not yet reached the recipients of Zakat, that the Prophet (PBUH) died. After his death it was enforced and implemented by Sayyiduna Abu Bakr. After Sayyiduna Abu Bakr, Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) followed it, and when Sayyiduna Omar (may Allah be pleased with him) was martyred, the statement of zakat was attached to his sword or will, and the zakat of camels was such that for every five camels up to twenty-five camels there was one goat, for twenty-five camels up to thirty-five one-year-old camels, and if not, two-year-old camels, more than thirty-five up to forty-five. One Bint Lubun (two-year-old camels) and forty-six to sixty one Haqqa (three-year-old camels) If more than sixty, then up to seventy-five Jizaa (four-year-old camels), if more than seventy-five, then two Bint Lubuns (two two-year-old camels), from ninety-one to one hundred twenty Two Haqqas (three three-year-old camels), if more than that, one Haqqa (three-year-old camels) for every fifty and every forty I am a Bint Lubun (two-year-old camel)."
"1665","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, has also narrated this tradition in the same way."
"1666","Abu Bakr bin Muhammad bin Amr bin Hazm narrated from his father, who narrated from his grandfather that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, wrote to Amr bin Hazm, may God bless him and grant him peace, for Shahrabeel bin Abd Kalal, Harith bin Abd Kalal and Naeem bin Abd Kalal, that five ounces of silver has five dirhams as zakat, and if there is more silver than that, one dirham should be increased for every forty dirhams, and less than five ounces, there is no zakat."
"1667","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that \I forgave the zakat of horses and slaves"
"1668","Sayyidna Suwayd bin Ghafla (RA) said: When a person who received Zakat from the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) came to us, I held his hand and read his law, in which it was written that miscellaneous property should not be collected, nor should collected property be separated for fear of Zakat."
"1669","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated that when the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent Sayyiduna Mu'adh, may Allah be pleased with him, to Yemen, he said: \Avoid taking their fine wealth (in zakat).\"""""
"1670","On the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \There is no zakat on a Muslim for his horse and slave.\"""""
"1671","On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Zakah is not obligatory on less than five Wasq (grains)"
"1672","Sayyidina Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \There is no zakat on less than five wasaqs of grains and dates"
"1673","Abu Bakr bin Muhammad bin Amr bin Hazm narrated from his father, who narrated from his grandfather that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, wrote to Sayyiduna Amr bin Hazm, may God bless him and grant him peace, for Sharhbeel bin Abd Kalal, Harith bin Abd Kalal, and Naeem bin Abd Kalal, saying, “Five dirhams are obligatory for zakat on five ounces of silver. There is no zakat on less than an awqiyyah.”"
"1674","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) that Sayyidna Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about paying Zakat before the time, so he (may Allah bless him and grant him peace) allowed him to do so. Imam Abu Muhammad Darami (may Allah have mercy on him) said: I am convinced of this and there is no problem in paying Zakat before the time when Zakat becomes obligatory."
"1675","Sayyida Fatimah bint Qays (RA) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) saying: \Surely there is some right in your property besides Zakat.\"""""
"1676","Sayyidna Maan bin Yazid (RA) narrated that I and my father and grandfather pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (PBUH), he (PBUH) engaged me and it was he (PBUH) who performed my marriage. That is, my father Yazid took out some dinars with the intention of charity and my father kept them with a man in the mosque. You got the reward of the intention and the meaning that you took is now yours."
"1677","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \It is not permissible for a rich man to take charity"
"1678","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \He who begs while he is rich will come on the Day of Judgment with scars on his face.\"" It was asked: What is the limit of wealth? He said: \""Fifty dirhams or its equivalent in gold.\"""""
"1679","From this second chain of transmission, Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) narrated the same narration from the Prophet (PBUH)."
"1680","Sayyidna Abu Huraira (RA) said that Sayyidna Hasan bin Ali (RA) picked one of the dates from the zakat and put it in his mouth, then the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \Take it out. Don't you know that we do not eat charity?\"""""
"1681","Sayyidna Abu Laila Bilal Ansari (RA) said: I was with the Holy Prophet (SAW) and Sayyidna Hasan bin Ali (RA) was with him."
"1682","Sayyiduna Mu'awiyah (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \Do not cling to me and ask. By Allah"
"1683","Sayyiduna Thawban (RA) narrated from a freed slave of the Messenger of Allah (SAW) that the Messenger of Allah (SAW) said: \Whoever asks for something from someone despite his wealth"
"1684","Sayyidina Abu Saeed al-Khudri (may God be pleased with him) narrated that some people of the Ansar asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he gave it to them. It is (i.e. there is no need to ask) and the one who is careless (of the question), then Allah makes him needy (rich), and the one who exerts patience, then Allah gives him patience and independence."
"1685","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) said: I heard Sayyidna 'Umar (RA), he used to say: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) used to give me wealth. I used to say: Give it to the one who needs it more than me. He (PBUH) used to say: \Take whatever Allah bestows on you from this wealth without greed and desire and do not set your heart after what you do not get.\"""""
"1686","This is also the narration from Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) in this second chain of transmission."
"1687","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, from this chain of transmission."
"1688","Sayyiduna Hakeem bin Hizam (RA) said: I asked the Prophet (PBUH) for something, and he granted it. I asked again, and he granted it again. If he greedily takes this wealth, there will be no blessing in his wealth, his example is like a person who eats but does not fill his stomach."
"1689","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) saying: \The best charity (charity) is that which a person is rich after giving it"
"1690","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (RA) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) saying: \The upper hand is better than the lower hand\"""
"1691","Sayyiduna Hakeem bin Hizam (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \The best charity is that which is given while you are wealthy"
"1692","Sayyidah Zaynab, the wife of Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud, may Allah be pleased with her, said that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \O community of women! Give charity"
"1693","Sayyiduna Anas (RA) said: Sayyidna Abu Talha (RA) was the richest among the Ansar of Madinah in terms of property and gardens, and the most beloved of his gardens was the garden of Birha, which was in front of the Prophet’s Mosque, and the Prophet (PBUH) used to visit it and drink its sweet water. Sayyidna Anas (RA) said: Al-Bir"
"1694","Sayyiduna Imran bin Hussain (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) certainly ordered us to give charity in every sermon he gave us, and forbade us to do misalah. (Messula means cutting off the ears, nose, etc. of a dead man)."
"1695","On the authority of Sayyidna Udi bin Hatim Tai, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, said: \Avoid the fire even if it is by giving a piece of date. If you cannot do that"
"1696","Sayyidna Abul Baba Ansari (RA) reported that when the Messenger of Allah (SAW) agreed with me, I said: O Messenger of Allah! My repentance is to leave my tribal residence and settle with you and give up my wealth and give it as charity for Allah and the Messenger. The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \A third of it is sufficient for you.\"""""
"1697","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: We were sitting with the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) when a man brought gold equal to an egg which he had found in a raid. And Ahmad (bin Khalid) said that it was obtained from a gold mine and this is correct. This person said: O Messenger of Allah! Take it, it is a charity from me and by Allah I have no wealth other than this. Upon hearing this, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned away from him. Then the man came from the left of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said this. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \One of you comes with all his wealth and he has nothing but this wealth"
"1698","Aslam said: I heard from Sayyiduna Umar, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered us to give charity. By chance, I had a lot of wealth at that time. I said in my heart: Today, if I succeed, I will defeat Sayyiduna Abu Bakr, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: I have left this much. Then Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (RA) also brought everything he had with him. He (PBUH) said: \O Abu Bakr"
"1699","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) said that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) made the zakat (Sadaqa al-Fitr) of Ramadan one Saa of dates or one Saa of barley obligatory on every Muslim, free, slave, male or female. Imam al-Darmi (may God have mercy on him) was asked: Do you also say the same, that is, you believe in one Sa'a? He said: Imam Malik, may God have mercy on him, also believed in the same."
"1700","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered us to give one saa of dates or one saa of barley as Sadaqah al-Fitr from every small, large, free and slave."
"1701","Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) said: When the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) was with us, we used to take out a Saa of grain or a Saa of dates or a Saa of barley or a Saa of cheese or a Saa of raisins from every small and large slave, and it continued like this until after Hajj or Umrah, Sayyidna Muawiya (RA) came to us in Madinah and said: I think two of this Syriac wheat. Mad is equal to one saa of dates, so people took this thing (i.e. half a saa of fitrah for wheat), Sayyiduna Abu Saeed al-Khudri said: But I take out as much fitra as I used to take out (in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him) (i.e. a whole saa), Imam Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: In my opinion, one saa of fitra should be taken out of any of the aforementioned species."
"1702","Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) said: We used to take out one saa of grain or one saa of dates or one saa of barley or one saa of raisins or one saa of cheese in Ramadan."
"1703","Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) said: We used to give Sadaqah al-Fitr during the time of the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) and then mentioned the above."
"1704","Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Aamir (RA) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) saying: \Sahib Maks will not enter Jannah.\"" Imam al-Darmi (may Allah have mercy on him) said: Sahib Maks means one who collects tithes."""
"1705","Sayyiduna Mu'adh (RA) said: When the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) sent me to Yemen, he ordered me to collect the usher (tenth) of the fruits (of zakat) that grow from the soil, and to take zakat of the twentieth part of what is watered by camels."
"1706","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \There is no recompense for the wound inflicted by an animal"
"1707","Sayyidna Abu Hameed Ansari Sa'idi (RA) reported that the Messenger of Allah (SAW) entrusted a man with the responsibility of collecting Zakat. What it is is for you, and it is offered for me. The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Do you sit in the house of your father and mother and see whether you are given gifts or not?\"" Then in the evening"
"1708","Sayyiduna Jarir, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When a person receiving Zakat comes to you"
"1709","Sayyiduna Jarir (may Allah be pleased with him) also narrated from this chain of narrators according to the previous hadith."
"1710","Sayyida Hawa, may Allah be pleased with her, said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \O Muslim women! Let none of you despise giving anything to his neighbor"
"1711","Sayyiduna Sakhr bin Ailat (RA) said: I arrested the maternal grandmother of Mughira bin Shuba (RA) and took her to the service of the Messenger of Allah (PBUH). The Prophet (SAW) asked about it, then said: \O Sakhr! When a people becomes Muslim"
"1712","Also from this chain of narrators, the hadith of Sayyiduna Sakhr, may God be pleased with him, is narrated, which is longer than the above-mentioned hadith of Abu Naeem."
"1713","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \Whoever gives charity from his lawful earnings"
"1714","On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \No wealth is diminished by giving charity"
"1715","Bahz bin Hakim narrates from his grandfather, his father, that he heard the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: \For every forty camels that graze in the forest"
"1716","Sayyidna Qubaysa bin Muhariq Hilali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I became a guarantor of a qarna, so I came to the service of the Messenger of Allah (sallallahu alaihi wasallam) and he said: \Qubaysa! Wait"
"1717","On the authority of Sayyiduna Hakeem bin Hizam, may Allah be pleased with him, a person asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, which charity is best. He said: \The charity that has been given to a relative who has hatred and enmity.\"""""
"1718","Sayyiduna Salman bin Amir Al-Zabee (RA) mentioned that the Prophet (PBUH) said: \Giving charity to the poor is charity"
"1719","Sayyiduna Salman bin Aamir Razbi, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Giving charity to the poor is charity, and giving charity to a relative is two things: charity and salah (mercy)."
"1720","Salah bin Zafar said: We were with Sayyidna Ammar bin Yasir, may Allah be pleased with him, and he brought a roasted goat and said, \Eat.\"""""
"1721","Sumak bin Harb said: I woke up on a day that it became difficult for me (to know) whether it was Sha'ban or the day of Ramadan, so I fasted and I came to Ikramah, I saw that they were eating bread and vegetables. He did not say, \Insha'Allah"
"1722","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, while mentioning fasting, said: \Do not start your fast until you see the moon"
"1723","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) said: Or he said: Abu al-Qasim (may Allah bless him and grant him peace) said: \Fast when you see the moon"
"1724","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, was surprised at such a person who fasted Ramadan before (seeing the moon), and he used to say that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \You fast when you see the moon"
"1725","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: When the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw the moon on the first night, he would say: \Allah Akbar Allahum Ahilahu Alayna\""."""
"1726","Sayyiduna Talha, may Allah be pleased with him, said that when the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw the moon on the first night, he would say: \O Allah"
"1727","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \Do not fast one or two days before Ramadan"
"1728","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with him, said that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \The month is (sometimes) twenty-nine days"
"1729","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The people saw the moon (but did not show it), I asked the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, that I had seen the moon, so he, may God bless him and grant him peace, fasted and ordered the people to fast."
"1730","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) said: An Arab came to the Holy Prophet (PBUH) and said: I have seen the moon. He (PBUH) said: \Do you bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah?\"" He said: Yes"
"1731","Sayyiduna Bara bin Azib (RA) said: In the beginning of Islam, when the Companions of the Prophet (PBUH) were fasting and it was time to break the fast, if a fasting person went to sleep before breaking the fast, he could not eat that night or the next day until evening. Then it happened that Sayyiduna Qays bin Sarmah Ansari was fasting, when it was time to break the fast, he came to his wife and said: Do you have anything to eat? He said: At that time there is nothing, but I will go and get it from somewhere. Qais had worked all day, so he caught his eye. When his wife came back, he saw him sleeping, so he said: Alas, you were deprived. When the afternoon came, Qais fainted. Al-Raffath to women...» [Baqarah: 187/2] That is, it has been made lawful for you to have intercourse with your wives during the nights of Ramadan. The Companions of the Prophet (may Allah be pleased with them) were very happy and ate and drank until the white streak (of the morning) appeared to them with a black streak."
"1732","Sayyiduna Adi bin Hatim Radiyallahu Anhu said: When this verse: \Eat and drink until it becomes clear to you the white line from the black line at dawn\"" [Baqarah: 187/2] was revealed"
"1733","Sayyidna Zaid bin Thabit (RA) said: We ate Suhoor with the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then he stood up for prayer. Said that the distance was equal to reading fifty verses."
"1734","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Do Suhoor because there is a blessing in Suhoor.\"""""
"1735","The slave of Abu Qais Amr bin Al-Aas said: Sayyidna Amr bin Al-Aas used to order us to keep food so that we would have suhoor but did not eat much. We said: You order us to keep food but do not eat much. Sayyiduna Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) replied that I do not order to keep food because I have a great appetite for food, but I have heard from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he says: \The difference between our fasting and that of the People of the Book is this suhoor food\"" (that is why I eat a little)."""
"1736","On the authority of Umm al-Mominin Sayyida Hafsa, may Allah be pleased with her, the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said: \Whoever does not intend to fast before Fajr"
"1737","Sayyiduna Sahl bin Sa'd (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \People will be in good health as long as they continue to break the fast.\"""""
"1738","Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \When the night comes from this side (i.e. the east) and the day goes this way (i.e. the west)"
"1739","It was narrated from Sayyidna Salman bin Aamir (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) said: \When one of you breaks his fast"
"1740","On the authority of Sayyidna Zaid bin Khalid Jahni, the Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, said: \Whoever breaks the fast for a fasting person"
"1741","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \You people beware of wasal.\"" The people said: \""You do wasal?\"" He said: \""I am not like you. My Lord feeds and drinks me at night.\"""""
"1742","Sayyiduna Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Do not break the fast.\"" It was asked: Do you do that? He said: \""I am not like any of you"
"1743","On the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, he heard the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: \Do not fast continuously without breaking the fast and Suhoor; yes"
"1744","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (SAW) forbade Wasal Soom (fasting for several consecutive days without breaking Iftar and Suhoor). Do you disconnect? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \I am not like you. My Lord feeds me at night.\"" Even then"
"1745","Umm al-Mominin narrated on the authority of Sayyida Aisha (RA) that Sayyidna Hamza bin Amr Aslami (RA) said to the Messenger of Allah (PBUH): O Messenger of Allah! I intend to travel, what do you order me? He said: \Fast if you want and don't if you want.\"""""
"1746","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, said: When the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, left (Madinah) in the year Mecca was conquered, he fasted (on the journey) and all the people also fasted, and when he reached the Kadid place, he, may God bless him and grant him peace, broke the fast and all the people also broke the fast."
"1747","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) mentioned that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey (conquest) when he saw a crowd and saw that people were shadowing a person. He (peace be upon him) inquired: \What is the matter?\"" It was said: There is a person who is fasting. The Prophet"
"1748","On the authority of Sayyiduna Ka'b bin Asim al-Ash'ari, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Fasting while traveling is not good.\"""""
"1749","Sayyiduna Ka'b bin Asim Ash'ari (RA) narrated from the Prophet (PBUH) that fasting while traveling is not good."
"1750","Sayyidina Abu Umayyah, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I came to the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, from a journey. When I intended to return, he, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \O Abu Umayyah! Stop for lunch.\"" I said: O Prophet of Allah! I am fasting"
"1751","Ubaid bin Jubayr said: When Sayyidna Abu Basra Ghafari (RA) left Fustat (a city) in Ramadan, I rode with him in a boat. Sayyiduna Abu Basra (RA) said: Do you hate the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah (PBUH)?"
"1752","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \Whoever does not fast one day of Ramadan due to illness or excuse"
"1753","On the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Whoever skips the fast of one day of Ramadan without an excuse that Allah has permitted (travel and illness)"
"1754","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: A person came to the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) and said: I am destroyed and ruined. He (PBUH) said: \What destroyed you?\"" He said: I had intercourse with my wife in the month of Ramadan. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Free a slave.” He said: “I do not have the strength.” He said: “Then fast for two consecutive months.” Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: Suddenly a large bag containing dates was brought to the Messenger of Allah (PBUH). He (PBUH) inquired"
"1755","From this chain of narration, Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (R.A.) narrated that a man broke his fast in Ramadan."
"1756","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) says that a man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that I have been burnt (in the fire of Hell). So he told the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he had had intercourse with his wife in Ramadan. Then a bag was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) which was called ``Azq (or vessels) and there were dates in it. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: \Where is the burning one?\"" When the man stood up"
"1757","Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrated that the Prophet (PBUH) said to a woman: \Do not fast without the permission of your husband.\"""""
"1758","On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Huraira, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \A woman should not fast in the presence of her husband without his permission for even one day of postnatal fasting except Ramadan.\"""""
"1759","On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \If her husband is present"
"1760","It was narrated from Sayyida Aisha that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to kiss while fasting. Urwa said: But this kiss (while fasting) is not a good thing."
"1761","It was narrated from Sayyida Aisha that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss her while he was fasting."
"1762","Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab (RA) said: I came to Sarwar and received a kiss while fasting, then I attended the service of the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) and said: \Today I committed a great crime. I was fasting and received a kiss?\"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""What do you think if you wash yourself with water while fasting?\"" I said: There is no harm in it. He said: \""Then why is there any harm in it?\"""""
"1763","Umm al-Momineen Sayyida Umm Salama and Umm al-Momineen Sayya Ayesha (RA) reported that the Prophet (PBUH) used to wake up in the morning even when he was in Janabat due to sexual intercourse, but still he (PBUH) used to fast."
"1764","On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Whoever forgets to eat and drink while fasting"
"1765","Sayyidina Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \When one of you forgets to eat or drink while fasting"
"1766","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyidna Abu Dardaa that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, vomited on purpose and then broke his fast. Madan said: I met Sayyidna Thawban, may Allah be pleased with him, in the mosque of Damascus."
"1767","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \When a fasting person vomits spontaneously"
"1768","Sayyiduna Shaddad bin Aws (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I used to go with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the 18th of Ramadan, and he saw a man who was wearing heels."
"1769","Sayyiduna Thawban, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated a hadith that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, was traveling towards Baqi', when he saw a man who was giving back, so he said: \The fast of the one who is giving back and the one who is giving is broken.\"" Imam al-Darmi"
"1770","Sayyiduna Abu Ubaidah bin Jarrah (RA) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) saying: \Fasting is a shield until it is torn.\"" Imam al-Darmi"
"1771","Abd al-Rahman bin Nu'man Abu Nu'man Ansari narrated that my father narrated from my grandfather that my grandfather was brought to the Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, and the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, placed his hand on his head and said: \If you are fasting"
"1772","Sayyiduna Salama bin Akua, may Allah be pleased with him, said: When this verse, \Even those who have the strength to fast should give a ransom for the food of a poor person\"""
"1773","It was narrated from Sayyidah Umm Hani bint Abi Talib (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) came to her while she was fasting. A vessel of water was brought to the Prophet (PBUH) from which he drank water. If it was for Qada of the fast, then fast on the second day, and if it was a post-natal fast, then if you want, then make Qada if your heart does not want to, then do not do Qada."
"1774","Sayyida Umm Hani (RA) said: On the day of the conquest of Makkah, Sayyida Fatima (RA) came and sat on the left side of the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him), and Sayyida Umm Hani (RA) was on the right side. I was fasting and now I broke the fast? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Was the judgment fast?\"" He said: No"
"1775","Sayyidina Abu Huraira (RA) said that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \When a person is called for food and he is fasting"
"1776","It was narrated from Sayyidah Umm Amara bint Ka'b that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to him and he served him food."
"1777","Sayyida Umm Salama (RA) said: I did not see the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) fasting for the entire month except Sha'ban. He used to combine the fasts of Sha'ban with Ramadan so that two full months of continuous fasting would occur."
"1778","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \When half of Sha'ban has passed"
"1779","From this chain of narrators, Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated the same as the above-mentioned hadith."
"1780","On the authority of Imran bin Hussain, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said to a person: \Did you fast at the end of this month?\"" He said: No. He said: \""When you have fasted Ramadan"
"1781","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him, said: Except for Ramadan, the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, never fasted for a whole month, and when he fasted, he would continue to fast until the narrator would say, By Allah! You will not break the fast, and when you break the (post-mortem) fast, the narrator will say, By Allah, you will not fast anymore."
"1782","Mutraf bin Abdullah bin Al-Shakhair narrated from his father (Sayyidna Abdullah) that a person was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, that he was always fasting."
"1783","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) says: My best friend (Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace) has bequeathed to me three things that I can never give up, the first is to recite Witr and go to bed, the second is to fast for three days in every month, and the third is to never miss two rak'ahs of Chasht prayer."
"1784","The above mentioned hadith is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA)."
"1785","Mu'awiya bin Qura narrated from his father (Sayyidna Qura) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \The fasting days of Baid is equivalent to fasting the whole year despite breaking the fast.\"" (as Sheikh Ahmed Al-Saati said in Al-Fath Al-Arbani 157/9)."""
"1786","Muhammad bin Ubad bin Ja'far said: I asked Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA): Did the Prophet (PBUH) forbid fasting on Fridays? Said: Yes, by the Lord of this Kaaba."
"1787","Abdullah bin Basr narrated from his sister, whose name was Sama, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Do not fast on Saturday except for the obligatory fast"
"1788","The slave of Sayyiduna Usama bin Zayd (RA) narrated that he used to travel with Sayyidna Usama (RA) to Wadi al-Qura where he had cattle (camels etc.), so he used to fast on Mondays and Thursdays on the way. Sayyiduna Osama (may Allah be pleased with him) replied: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to fast on Mondays and Thursdays and used to say: \People's deeds are presented on Mondays and Thursdays.\"""""
"1789","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Huraira that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to fast on Mondays and Thursdays. (ie on Monday and Thursday)."
"1790","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the most beloved of all fasts to Allah is the fast of David, peace be upon him, he used to fast one day and break his fast one day, and the most beloved to Allah is the prayer of David (peace be upon him) among the (night) prayers. Imam al-Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: This last sentence is incorrect, the correct one is that he used to sleep at midnight, pray for a third of the night, and recite the tasbih for a third of the night."
"1791","On the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \It is not permissible to fast for two days"
"1792","On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Ayyub Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Whoever fasts Ramadan and then fasts six days of Shawwal"
"1793","On the authority of Sayyiduna Thawban, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \(The fasts of one year were completed in this way) that the fasts of one month became ten months"
"1794","Nu'man bin Sa'd said: A man came to Sayyiduna Ali (RA) and asked him in which month he should fast after the month of Ramadan. Sayyidna Ali (RA) said: No one has asked me about this since I heard it from the Messenger of Allah (PBUH). So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to observe the fast of Muharram, and said: \On this day"
"1795","On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \The best fasts after Ramadan are the fasts of the month you call Muharram.\"""""
"1796","The above mentioned hadith is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA)."
"1797","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, said that when the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to Medina, he saw the Jews fasting on Ashura."
"1798","It was narrated from Sayyida Aisha that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to fast on Ashura and ordered us to fast."
"1799","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Salama bin Akwa, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent a person from the tribe of Islam on the day of Ashura with the message that it is the day of Ashura, and whoever has eaten or drunk should complete the rest of the day, and whoever has not eaten or drunk should fast on that day."
"1800","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \This is the day of Ashura"
"1801","Umm al-Momineen Sayyida Aisha (RA) said: In the days of Jahiliyyah, Quraysh used to fast on the day of Ashura, then when the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) came to Madinah, he (PBUH) fasted and ordered to fast until the fasting of Ramadan became obligatory, and he abandoned Ashura."
"1802","Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Aamir (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \The Day of Arafah and the Days of Al-Tashreeq are the Eid days of our people of Islam"
"1803","Ibn Abi Najih narrated from his father that he said: Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (RA) was asked about fasting on the Day of Arafah, and he said: I performed Hajj with the Prophet (SAW) and he did not fast on the day of Arafah. I performed Hajj with Sayyiduna Uthan, may Allah be pleased with him, and he did not fast on that day, and I do not fast on that day, nor do I order or forbid fasting."
"1804","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Bishr bin Suhaim (RA) that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) ordered him or a person to announce on the days of Tashreeq that \only a believer will enter Paradise"
"1805","It was narrated from Abu Marah, a freed slave of Aqeel, that he and Abdullah bin Amr, his father, came to the service of Sayyidna Amr bin Al-Aas (RA) on the first or second day after Eid al-Adha (on the eleventh or twelfth of Dhu al-Hijjah), and Sayyidna Amr Bin Al-Aas (RA) prepared food for them both. Abdullah said: I am fasting. Sayyidna Amr (RA) said: Break the fast because the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) ordered us to fast on those days. ordered to break the fast and forbade fasting, so Abdullah bin Amr broke the fast and ate, I also ate with him."
"1806","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) that a woman took the vow of Hajj but she passed away, so her brother came to the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) and asked him about it. He said: Yes, he said: \Pay the debt of Allah Almighty"
"1807","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \The smell of the mouth of a fasting person is better in the sight of Allah than the smell of musk. There are two times of happiness for a fasting person"
"1808","Sayyidina Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \Allah Almighty says: The reward for a good deed for the son of Adam is from ten to seven hundred times"
